// smt_encode — THE OBLIGATION WALK (1.5.0; D-218.4, D-218.6, D-218.8): one
// function instance's body, walked in program order over the SAME typed AST
// the emitter lowers, under the SAME generic bindings, producing the
// hypotheses the solver may use and the obligations it must decide. It never
// reads the IR writer -- which is what makes the obligations of the
// `--obligations` run and the `--elide` run identical by construction (P-3).
//
// THE ENCODING IS FAIL-CLOSED OPACITY (P-8). A value the walk can express is
// a term; a value it cannot is an OPAQUE symbol -- declared with its type's
// range axiom and no definition -- and the site's obligation is still recorded
// over it. Every hypothesis asserted here is a fact on every execution that
// reaches the site: a definition is the language's semantics, a range axiom
// is the type's, and the D-210/D-007 traps make the continuing path satisfy
// both. An `unsat` under those hypotheses proves the guard cannot fire on any
// continuing path. What 1.5.0 expresses: plain `intN`/`uintN` and `bool`
// values, literals, `+ - *`, `/ %` (through the truncating definitions --
// P-17), comparisons, `&& || !`, unary minus, the ternary, the widening
// cast, and a binding's definitions in straight-line code. Everything else
// is opaque, and every construct's SUBEXPRESSIONS are still walked, because
// a division inside an argument is a site whatever its parent is.
//
// NAMES ARE SOURCE-DERIVED SSA (P-5): a binding's k-th definition is
// `|name.k|`, an anonymous opaque term `|_.k|`. A branch's assignments are
// visible inside the branch and INVALIDATED after it (a fresh opaque
// version for every name either arm assigned); a loop invalidates the names
// its body assigns before the body is walked and again after it; a `defer`
// body reads every name as opaque (it runs at an exit the straight line does
// not see); and a local or parameter whose ADDRESS is taken anywhere in the
// function is never NAMED at all -- every read of it is a fresh opaque term
// (1.5.2 step 0, DEF-14). 1.5.0 gave such a name a symbol and withheld only
// its DEFINITION, but a stable symbol is itself the fact "every read is the
// same value", and a call handed the address falsifies it: `int32:a = x +
// 1i32; raw bump(@x); 100i32 / (x - a)` kept `|a.1| = |x.1| + 1` across the
// call, z3 proved the divisor -1, and the elided build divided by zero where
// the plain build reached `failsafe`. Contracts as hypotheses are 1.5.3's.
//
// PATH CONDITIONS (1.5.4 step 1; L-1..L-6 in meta/roadmap/1.5/1.5.4.md): a
// branch condition is a fact INSIDE the arm it guards and its negation a fact
// where the arm cannot have been taken -- an `if`'s condition in its then-arm
// and `(not c)` in its else-arm; a `pick` arm's pattern (`(= sel v)`, a
// range) and the negations of the arms before it, its `where` guard once
// inside; after an arm that never falls through (a syntactic terminator:
// `pass`, `fail`, `return`, `exit`, `trap`, `break`, `continue`, `give`, and
// blocks, `if`s and `pick`s made only of those) the OTHER arm's condition
// holds; after a loop nothing `break`s out of, its condition is false; a
// `when`'s `then` block knows the condition held at the first head visit and
// its `end` block that it did not and that the loop changed nothing. Each is
// pushed in the region it is a fact of, so the cone's dominance rule keeps it
// where it belongs.
//
// THE MERGE (1.5.4 step 2; L-7..L-10): a region opened for an ARM carries its
// condition, and leaving it re-pushes every hypothesis recorded directly in
// it into the parent as `(=> c H)` -- a fact of an arm is a fact after the
// arm under the arm's condition (an execution past the arm with `c` true
// fell through the arm's straight line and so passed every site of it; with
// `c` false the implication is vacuous). A loop body's hypotheses are one
// symbolic iteration's and are never re-pushed; a `defer`'s neither. On that
// footing the versions after an `if`, a `when` or a `pick` MERGE: a binding
// the arms left at different versions gets a new one defined `(ite c_1 v_1
// (ite c_2 v_2 ... v_n))` over the arms that fall through, and a havoc only
// where an arm has no condition term or an unnamed version. A pick
// expression's value is the same chain over its arms' `give` terms. `&&`,
// `||` and the ternary are arms too: the right-hand side and the two branches
// are encoded in regions of their own under `a`, `(not a)`, `c`, `(not c)`.
//
// THE COUNTERS (1.5.4 step 3; L-11..L-14): a counted loop's `$` and a range
// `for`'s binding are TERMS. The bounds and the step are captured at entry
// (fresh symbols equal to their terms, as the emitter's slots are -- D-234's
// rule), the direction is `asc = start < limit` as the emitter computes it
// once; the ENTRY row sees the counter at its start; in the body it is a
// fresh symbol inside its range (`start <= $ < limit` ascending, `limit < $
// <= start` descending, and on a numeral step in the right residue class);
// the PRESERVATION and `continue` rows see the incremented counter the head
// will see; after a loop nothing `break`s out of, the invariant holds over
// the EXIT value (past the limit by less than a numeral step; a range's
// binding exactly at its bound). A computed step's positivity is the
// `loop-step` row (S-46), its compare the guard; a literal step is the
// checker's and has neither.
//
// THE CONE (P-4): an obligation's canonical text is the relevance closure of
// its goal over the hypotheses that DOMINATE it -- recorded before it, in a
// branch region on the path from the function's entry to the site. Later
// definitions describe values that exist only if execution passes later
// traps, and a sibling branch's definitions describe values the site's path
// never computes (a then-arm's `x.2 = x.1 + 1`, in range by D-210's trap,
// would otherwise tell an else-arm site that `x.1 < MAX`); using either
// would be unsound. Its SHA-256 over (text, symbol, kind) is the
// obligation's identity (D-218.8).

mod:smt_encode;

use "../../frontend/intern.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/token_kind.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/source_location.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/ast_kind.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/ast.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_expr.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_stmt.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_decl.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/parse_decorate.npk".*;   // limit_target (1.5.2 step 2, D-251)
use "../../frontend/parse_pick.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/types.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/numeric.npk".*;   // tfp_q_decimal: a `tfp` literal's exact Q value (D-195; 1.5.4b step 2)
use "../../frontend/expr_types.npk".*;
use "../../frontend/type_layout.npk".*;   // type_is_list: a `List`'s length is its `count` (1.5.8b step 5)
use "../../frontend/symbols.npk".*;   // a free call's callee, by its symbol (1.5.2 step 3)
use "../../frontend/type_resolve.npk".*;
use "../../../lib/nhash.npk".*;
use "../ir/ir_types.npk".*;
use "../cast_bounds.npk".*;   // D-306's bounds, in the SMT spelling (1.5.8b step 5); len_ceiling_text (D-308 SS7, step 6c)
use "../../frontend/builtins.npk".*;   // builtin_caller_len (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step 6c)
use "./smt_writer.npk".*;
use "./smt_kinds.npk".*;

// --- the state -----------------------------------------------------------------------

// A declared constant.
pub struct:SmtSym = {
    string:text;      // `|x.2|`
    bool:is_bool;     // Bool, else Int
    // AN UNINTERPRETED FUNCTION (1.5.3 step 2, L-3): a `pure never fails`
    // callee's symbol, declared `(declare-fun |f| <sorts> <sort>)` -- its
    // argument sorts as one text, "" for a constant.
    string:sorts;
    // A FLOAT SYMBOL'S SORT (1.5.4b step 3, D-281): `(_ FloatingPoint 8 24)`
    // or `(_ FloatingPoint 11 53)`; "" for an Int or a Bool. No range axiom:
    // a float symbol may be any value of its sort, NaN and the infinities
    // included, and the goal's own conditions say otherwise where they do.
    string:fsort;
};

// One hypothesis: its text and the symbols it mentions (by index into `syms`).
pub struct:SmtHyp = {
    string:text;
    List<int32>:syms;
    int32:region;            // the branch region it was recorded in
};

// One obligation, as the walk records it; `finish` fills the cone and the hash.
pub struct:SmtObl = {
    int32:kind;
    string:goal;             // the property to prove (the file asserts its negation)
    List<int32>:syms;        // the goal's symbols
    int64:hyps;              // hypotheses recorded before it: the cone draws from [0, hyps)
    int32:site;              // the node index that identifies the site (the emitter's key) ...
    int32:space;             // ... in this id space (L-9): SITE_EXPR, SITE_STMT or SITE_DECL
    int32:ordinal;           // the k-th of its kind in this function
    int32:ctx;               // the clause context the site was recorded under (1.5.3 step 2; `LlCtx.cur_ctx`)
    int32:role;              // ROLE_* (1.5.3 step 2, L-13): what the row's retention keeps
    int32:group;             // the rows one guard shares (a loop's three rows, a call's bypass rows)
    int32:traps;             // the traps the group keeps when any of its rows is retained
    int32:defer_stmt;        // DEF-82: the `defer` body this row sits in, or 0
    int32:line;
    int32:col;
    int32:region;            // the branch region of the site
    bool:encoded;            // false: an `unencoded` row (P-12)
    bool:checker;            // THE FRONTEND DECIDED IT (1.5.4 step 4, L-20): no query, verdict `checker`
    bool:derived;            // THE RUNNERS DERIVE IT (D-305 (7), 1.5.8c step 4): a `stack-depth` row -- no query, its verdict read off the group's `terminate` call rows after every file is decided
    string:tier;             // filled by finish (D-281): `int`, `bv`, `fp`; `-` for an unencoded or checker row
    List<int32>:cone_syms;   // filled by finish: symbols in the cone, ascending
    List<int32>:cone_hyps;   // filled by finish: hypotheses in the cone, in order
    string:canon;            // filled by finish: the canonical text
    string:hash;             // filled by finish: sha256 hex of canon + symbol + kind
    bool:discharged;         // set by the elision reader: the manifest says so
};

// A binding in scope: the name, its current symbol (-1: none -- reads of it
// are opaque), and its type.
struct:Bind = {
    int32:name;
    int32:sym;
    int32:type_id;
    int32:rule;      // the `Rules` declaration limiting the name (1.5.2, D-251); 0 for none
    int32:entry;     // the binding's FIRST version (1.5.3 step 2, D-243): what `old(...)` reads
    // A `simd` BINDING'S LANES (D-282, 1.5.4b step 4): one symbol per lane of
    // the element type, a new set at every write -- defined equal to the
    // written value's lanes where those are known -- and a fresh opaque set
    // at every invalidation, restore and merge; empty for any other type.
    List<int32>:lanes;
    // A CONTAINER BINDING'S LENGTH SYMBOL (1.5.8b step 5): `|len.<name>.<k>|`,
    // named lazily at the first read and FRESH after every write or
    // invalidation of the name, so `xs.len` and an element's `bounds` row name
    // one length exactly while the binding is untouched. 0 for none -- an
    // escaped name (DEF-14) and every non-container type keep it 0, and their
    // rows stay `unencoded` rather than resting on a symbol a call could
    // falsify.
    int32:lensym;
};

// A term: encodable or not; when encodable, its text, sort and symbols.
struct:Term = {
    bool:ok;
    bool:is_bool;
    string:text;
    List<int32>:syms;
};

// A FLOAT OPERATION'S DEFINITION (1.5.4b step 3, D-281): every float value
// the walk builds is NAMED -- a fresh symbol of the float sort defined equal
// to the operation -- and recorded here by shape, so the tier-2 translation
// (the Real-interval abstraction) reads a flat list of `sym = op(a, b)`
// rather than parsing nested terms. `op`: `lit` (a = the exact rational of
// the literal's decimal text), `add`/`sub`/`mul`/`div` (a, b symbols),
// `neg`, `sqrt`, `int` (a = an Int term, `to_real` of it), `widen`/`narrow`
// (a = the float symbol crossing widths).
pub struct:FpDef = {
    string:sym;
    string:op;
    string:a;
    string:b;
    int32:ty;
};

// A `simd` EXPRESSION'S LANES (D-282, 1.5.4b step 4): N scalar terms by
// expression index, filled by the walk and read by the consumers below.
pub struct:LaneEntry = { int32:id; List<Term>:lanes; };

pub struct:Encoder = {
    Ast->:ast;
    ExprTypes->:et;
    SymbolTable->:tab;         // a free call's callee is its identifier's symbol (1.5.2 step 3)
    TypeTable->:types;
    InternTable->:interns;
    LlCtx->:ctx;
    TypeResolver->:tr;
    int32:scope;
    string:symbol;             // the function instance's mangled symbol
    List<SmtSym>:syms;
    List<SmtHyp>:hyps;
    List<SmtObl>:obls;
    List<Bind>:binds;
    List<int32>:ver_name;      // per-name version counters
    List<int32>:ver_next;
    List<int32>:escaped;       // names whose address is taken: never defined
    int32:anon;                // anonymous opaque counter
    List<int32>:ordinals;      // per-kind ordinal counters, OK_COUNT + 1 slots
    bool:nonlinear;            // a non-literal `*` or a non-literal divisor appeared
    bool:uses_sdiv;            // a signed division term appeared (the define-funs are needed)
    bool:uses_bv;              // a bit-vector crossing appeared (D-280): the logic is `ALL`
    bool:uses_fp;              // a float term appeared (D-281): the logic is `ALL`
    List<FpDef>:fpdefs;        // the float definitions, in order (tier 2 reads them)
    List<LaneEntry>:lane_tab;  // a `simd` expression's lanes, by expression (D-282)
    List<int32>:region_parent; // branch regions: each one's parent (the root's is -1)
    int32:cur_region;          // the region the walk is in
    // A REGION'S CONDITION AND ITS FIRST HYPOTHESIS (1.5.4 step 2, L-7):
    // `term_none` for a region that is not an arm (a loop body, a `defer`,
    // a pick arm without a pattern term); the hypothesis index the region
    // began at, so leaving it can re-push what it recorded, guarded.
    List<Term>:region_cond;
    List<int64>:region_hyp0;
    // THE LAST `give` WALKED (L-9): a pick expression's arm ends in one, and
    // the arm's value is its term.
    Term:last_give;
    // THE COUNTERS (1.5.4 step 3, L-11): `$` of every enclosing counted
    // loop, innermost last -- the term `$` reads outside a rule -- and, per
    // loop frame, the counter's kind (0 none, 1 a range `for` binding, 2
    // `$`), the binding's name, its step and direction terms, and the index
    // of its `$` entry in `dollars`, so a `continue` can see the incremented
    // counter of the loop it re-enters.
    List<Term>:dollars;
    List<int32>:loop_ckind;
    List<int32>:loop_cname;
    List<Term>:loop_cstep;
    List<Term>:loop_casc;
    List<int64>:loop_cdollar;
    // THE RULE'S SUBJECT (1.5.2 step 3, L-8): the term `$` stands for while a
    // `Rules` body is being instantiated by `enc_rule`; `term_none` outside.
    Term:subject;
    // QUIET (1.5.2 step 3): nonzero while `enc_rule` encodes a rule's clauses,
    // so a guard site INSIDE a clause -- a division -- records no row of the
    // instantiating function's: the guard is the predicate function's own,
    // and the row is recorded there, once (L-1).
    int32:quiet;
    // INSIDE A PROPOSITION (DEF-33, 1.5.4b step 2): a contract clause, an
    // invariant conjunct, a rule's clause, a `prove`. A PROPOSITION HOLDS
    // ONLY WHERE ITS EVALUATION DOES NOT TRAP: every guard inside one -- a
    // shift's amount, a division's divisor, a twisted compare's operands --
    // has its condition conjoined into the proposition's term (`pfacts`,
    // gathered while `in_prop` is set), never pushed as a fact. The row over
    // the proposition then proves the guards pass, so eliding its check
    // removes no live guard, and the proposition as a hypothesis carries
    // them. A guard outside a proposition -- a body site -- pushes its fact
    // after its row, as before.
    int32:in_prop;
    List<Term>:pfacts;
    // THE CONTRACTS' STATE (1.5.3 step 2): `result` while an `ensures` is
    // encoded (`term_none` outside one); `at_entry` while an `old(...)`
    // operand is encoded, so a name reads its entry version; the function's
    // declaration, its impl and its trait (0 outside a method), its success
    // type, and whether it is `failsafe`; the clause context a row is
    // recorded under (0 outside a clause); and the loop stack a `continue`
    // resolves against -- each loop's statement, label and invariant.
    Term:result;
    bool:at_entry;
    int32:fn_decl;
    int32:impl_decl;
    int32:trait_ty;
    int32:ret_type;
    bool:is_failsafe;
    int32:clause_ctx;
    int32:cur_defer;         // DEF-82: the `defer` body being walked, or 0
    List<int32>:loop_sids;
    List<int32>:loop_labels;
    List<int32>:loop_invs;
    // THE MEASURE OF EACH OPEN LOOP (D-304, 1.5.8c step 1): the clause node, the
    // measure's term at the body's start (what a `continue` and the preservation
    // row compare against), and its signedness (the traps a signed one keeps).
    List<int32>:loop_meas;
    List<Term>:loop_mstart;
    List<bool>:loop_msigned;
    // THE FUNCTION'S OWN MEASURE AT ENTRY (D-304 (5), 1.5.8c step 4): the term
    // of its `decreases E` over the parameters' entry versions, `term_none`
    // for a function that states none or whose group has no cycle; every
    // recursive call's row compares the callee's measure over the actuals
    // against it. `in_body` is set while the body is walked: the check the row
    // stands for is emitted in the body alone (a generated predicate has no
    // snapshot), so a recursive call inside a `requires` clause -- walked at
    // the entry -- records no row, as it has no check.
    Term:fn_m0;
    bool:in_body;
    // AN INDEX EXPRESSION'S TERM, BY EXPRESSION (D-286, 1.5.5 step 2): the
    // `disjoint` row compares the index pairs of two paths, and a party's
    // index was encoded when its claim was walked -- earlier, under the
    // versions of that moment, which is exactly what the held address denotes
    // (a version is never reused, so the memo is exact under later writes).
    // Filled by the index arm of `enc_expr` and the assignment target's walk;
    // a walk never encodes an expression twice (its rows would double).
    List<int32>:memo_ids;
    List<Term>:memo_terms;
};

// Branch regions (the dominance rule): a then-arm, an else-arm, a loop body,
// a pick arm, a `when` block and a `defer` body each open a child region of
// the one they sit in; straight-line blocks stay in their region.
func:region_enter = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    drop region_enter_cond(e, raw term_none());
    pass NIL;
};

// AN ARM'S REGION (1.5.4 step 2, L-7): it carries the condition under which
// its facts hold after it, and the hypothesis index it began at.
func:region_enter_cond = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:c) never fails {
    drop list_push(@e.region_parent, e.cur_region);
    drop list_push(@e.region_cond, raw term_copy(c));
    drop list_push(@e.region_hyp0, e.hyps.count);
    e.cur_region = (e.region_parent.count - 1i64) =>! int32;
    pass NIL;
};

// LEAVING AN ARM RE-PUSHES ITS FACTS, GUARDED (L-7): every hypothesis
// recorded DIRECTLY in the region since it began -- a definition, a range
// axiom, a rule, a callee's `ensures`, an inner arm's already-guarded copies
// -- goes into the parent as `(=> c H)`. The arm's own condition is not
// re-pushed (`(=> c c)` says nothing). A region without a condition
// re-pushes nothing: a loop body's facts are one iteration's, a `defer`'s
// run at an exit the straight line does not see.
func:region_leave = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    int32:r = e.cur_region;
    int32:parent = e.region_parent[r => int64];
    if (e.region_cond[r => int64].ok) {
        Term:c = raw term_copy(e.region_cond[r => int64]);
        int64:n0 = e.hyps.count;
        for (int64:h in e.region_hyp0[r => int64]...n0) {
            if (e.hyps[h].region != r) { continue; }
            if (string_equals(e.hyps[h].text, c.text)) { continue; }
            string:gt = raw smt_app2("=>", c.text, e.hyps[h].text);
            List<int32>:gs = raw syms_union(c.syms, e.hyps[h].syms);
            drop hyp_push_in(e, gt, gs, parent);
        }
    }
    e.cur_region = parent;
    pass NIL;
};

// Is region `h` on the path from the root to region `o`?
func:region_dominates = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:h, int32:o) never fails {
    int32:r = o;
    int32:fuel = 4096i32;
    while ((r >= 0i32) && (fuel > 0i32)) decreases fuel {
        if (r == h) { pass true; }
        r = e.region_parent[r => int64];
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
    }
    pass false;
};

pub func:enc_init = Encoder(Ast->:ast, ExprTypes->:et, SymbolTable->:tab, TypeTable->:types,
                            InternTable->:interns, LlCtx->:ctx, TypeResolver->:tr,
                            int32:scope, string:symbol) never fails {
    List<int32>:ords = raw list_init::<int32>(((raw OK_COUNT()) => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...(((raw OK_COUNT()) => int64) + 1i64)) { drop list_push(@ords, 0i32); }
    List<int32>:rp = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
    drop list_push(@rp, 0i32 - 1i32);   // the root region
    List<Term>:rc = raw list_init::<Term>(8i64);
    drop list_push(@rc, raw term_none());
    List<int64>:rh = raw list_init::<int64>(8i64);
    drop list_push(@rh, 0i64);
    pass Encoder{ ast: ast, et: et, tab: tab, types: types, interns: interns, ctx: ctx, tr: tr,
                  scope: scope, symbol: string_concat(symbol, ""),
                  syms: raw list_init::<SmtSym>(32i64),
                  hyps: raw list_init::<SmtHyp>(32i64),
                  obls: raw list_init::<SmtObl>(8i64),
                  binds: raw list_init::<Bind>(16i64),
                  ver_name: raw list_init::<int32>(16i64),
                  ver_next: raw list_init::<int32>(16i64),
                  escaped: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  anon: 0i32, ordinals: move(ords), nonlinear: false, uses_sdiv: false, uses_bv: false, uses_fp: false, fpdefs: raw list_init::<FpDef>(4i64), lane_tab: raw list_init::<LaneEntry>(4i64),
                  region_parent: move(rp), cur_region: 0i32,
                  region_cond: move(rc), region_hyp0: move(rh), last_give: raw term_none(),
                  dollars: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_ckind: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_cname: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_cstep: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_casc: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_cdollar: raw list_init::<int64>(4i64),
                  subject: raw term_none(), quiet: 0i32, in_prop: 0i32,
                  pfacts: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  result: raw term_none(), at_entry: false, fn_decl: 0i32, impl_decl: 0i32,
                  trait_ty: 0i32, ret_type: 0i32, is_failsafe: false, clause_ctx: 0i32, cur_defer: 0i32,
                  loop_sids: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_labels: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_invs: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  fn_m0: raw term_none(), in_body: false,
                  loop_meas: raw list_init::<int32>(4i64),
                  loop_mstart: raw list_init::<Term>(4i64),
                  loop_msigned: raw list_init::<bool>(4i64),
                  memo_ids: raw list_init::<int32>(8i64),
                  memo_terms: raw list_init::<Term>(8i64) };
};

// --- types -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

// An expression's recorded type, under the instance's binding.
func:ty_of = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    pass (raw subst_emitted_param(e.ctx, raw exprtypes_get(e.et, id)));
};

func:is_int = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_INT()));
};

func:is_bool = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_BOOL()));
};

// A WORD (1.5.4b step 1, D-279): an integer, or a flag family (D-230) -- one
// `i32` carrier read as an UNSIGNED 32-bit word, which is what its `|`/`&`
// compute on. Width and signedness through these, never `type_int_bits`
// alone (a flag family's `a` slot is its family index, not a width).
func:is_word = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_INT())) { pass true; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_FLAGS()));
};

func:word_bits = int32(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_FLAGS())) { pass 32i32; }
    pass (raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty));
};

func:word_signed = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_FLAGS())) { pass false; }
    pass (raw type_is_signed(e.types, ty));
};

// A TWISTED KIND (D-278, 1.5.4b step 2): `tbb`, `tfp`, `dim256` (a `tfp256`
// with a unit, D-196) and the ternary family (D-197) -- an Int term in the
// carrier's range with ERR the carrier's most negative value, a VALUE the
// terms carry (D-008). `is_scalar` is what gets a symbol: a word or a
// twisted value, each with its own range axiom.
func:is_twisted = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    int32:k = raw type_kind(e.types, ty);
    if (k == (raw TY_TBB())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_TFP())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_DIM())) { pass true; }
    pass (k == (raw TY_TERN()));
};

func:is_scalar = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (raw is_word(e, ty)) { pass true; }
    pass (raw is_twisted(e, ty));
};

// A FLOAT WITH A TERM (1.5.4b step 3, D-281): `flt32` and `flt64`, the two
// widths that compute -- `flt128` is a storage format (D-143) with no
// arithmetic and no comparison, and gets no term. `is_termed` is everything
// that gets a symbol: a word, a twisted value, a bool, a float.
func:is_float = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) != (raw TY_FLOAT())) { pass false; }
    int32:fb = raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty);
    pass ((fb == 32i32) || (fb == 64i32));
};

func:fp_sort = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (!(raw is_float(e, ty))) { pass ""; }
    if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) == 32i32) { pass "(_ FloatingPoint 8 24)"; }
    pass "(_ FloatingPoint 11 53)";
};

// `eb sb` -- the `to_fp` indices of the width.
func:fp_eb_sb = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) == 32i32) { pass "8 24"; }
    pass "11 53";
};

func:is_termed = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (raw is_scalar(e, ty)) { pass true; }
    if (raw is_bool(e, ty)) { pass true; }
    pass (raw is_float(e, ty));
};

// Does `s` contain `needle`? (The tier of a row is read off its canonical text.)
func:has_sub = bool(string:s, string:needle) never fails {
    if (needle.len == 0i64) { pass true; }
    if (s.len < needle.len) { pass false; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64..(s.len - needle.len)) {
        bool:same = true;
        for (int64:j in 0i64...needle.len) {
            if (s.ptr[i + j] != needle.ptr[j]) { same = false; break; }
        }
        if (same) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// THE SENTINEL AND THE VALID BOUNDS of a twisted type: ERR is the carrier's
// `MIN` (`tbb_min_decimal`'s value, D-008); the valid range is `MIN+1 ..= MAX`
// for `tbb`/`tfp`/`dim256` and the balanced `-B ..= B`, B = (base^digits -
// 1)/2, for the ternary kinds (D-197) -- strictly inside the carrier's, which
// is what leaves the most negative value spare for ERR.
func:tw_min = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    pass (raw smt_int_min(raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)));
};

func:tw_bound = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    pass (raw tern_bound(raw type_tern_base(e.types, ty), raw type_tern_digits(e.types, ty)));
};

func:tw_lo = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_TERN())) { pass (raw smt_int(0i64 - (raw tw_bound(e, ty)))); }
    pass (raw smt_app1("-", raw pow2_minus_one_decimal(((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) => int64) - 1i64)));
};

func:tw_hi = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_TERN())) { pass (raw smt_int(raw tw_bound(e, ty))); }
    pass (raw pow2_minus_one_decimal(((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) => int64) - 1i64));
};

// The range axiom of a twisted symbol: ERR, or a valid value.
func:twisted_axiom = string(Encoder->:e, string:sym, int32:ty) never fails {
    string:valid = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("<=", raw tw_lo(e, ty), sym),
                                raw smt_app2("<=", sym, raw tw_hi(e, ty)));
    pass (raw smt_app2("or", raw smt_app2("=", sym, raw tw_min(e, ty)), valid));
};

// 2^F as a term, F = width/2: a `tfp`'s scale (D-195).
func:tw_pow2f = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    pass (raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) / 2i32) => int64), false));
};

// 2^n as an int64, n < 63 -- by doubling, so no shift amount is computed.
func:pow2_int64 = int64(int32:n) never fails {
    int64:p = 1i64;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) { p = p * 2i64; }
    pass p;
};

// THE CROSSING'S WIDTH (D-280): measured under the profile, the
// Int-to-bit-vector crossing costs 191 rlimit at 32 and 64 bits, 884K at
// 128, 3.6M at 256 and the whole budget at 2048; a general operation wider
// than this stays opaque (safe, unproven), and the Int forms of D-279 cover
// the wide widths' real shapes. Moving it is a measurement, not a decision.
func:BV_CROSS_MAX_BITS = int32() never fails { pass 64i32; };

// --- symbols and hypotheses --------------------------------------------------------------

func:hyp_push = NIL(Encoder->:e, string:text, List<int32>:syms) never fails {
    drop hyp_push_in(e, text, syms, e.cur_region);
    pass NIL;
};

// A GUARD'S CONDITION INSIDE A PROPOSITION (DEF-33): gathered for the
// proposition's own term; `prop_opaque` stands in for a guard the walk has no
// term for, so the proposition is unprovable rather than trap-blind.
func:prop_fact = NIL(Encoder->:e, string:text, List<int32>:syms) never fails {
    List<int32>:copy = raw list_init::<int32>(syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...syms.count) { drop list_push(@copy, syms[i]); }
    drop list_push(@e.pfacts, Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: string_concat(text, ""), syms: move(copy) });
    pass NIL;
};

func:prop_opaque = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    Term:o = raw term_opaque(e, e.types.t_bool);
    if (o.ok) { drop list_push(@e.pfacts, move(o)); }
    pass NIL;
};

// A proposition's encoding: `prop_begin` marks the gathered conditions,
// `prop_end` conjoins those gathered since onto the term and drops them.
func:prop_begin = int64(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    e.in_prop = e.in_prop + 1i32;
    pass e.pfacts.count;
};

func:prop_end = Term(Encoder->:e, int64:mark, Term:c) never fails {
    e.in_prop = e.in_prop - 1i32;
    Term:acc = raw term_copy(c);
    if (acc.ok && acc.is_bool) {
        for (int64:i in mark...e.pfacts.count) {
            acc = raw term_app2("and", e.pfacts[i], acc, true);
        }
    }
    drop list_truncate(@e.pfacts, mark);
    pass acc;
};

// A hypothesis in a NAMED region (1.5.4 step 2): the guarded re-push writes
// into the parent of the region it is leaving.
func:hyp_push_in = NIL(Encoder->:e, string:text, List<int32>:syms, int32:region) never fails {
    List<int32>:copy = raw list_init::<int32>(syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...syms.count) { drop list_push(@copy, syms[i]); }
    SmtHyp:h = SmtHyp{ text: string_concat(text, ""), syms: move(copy), region: region };
    drop list_push(@e.hyps, move(h));
    pass NIL;
};

// Declare a constant; an integer one gets its range axiom as a hypothesis.
func:sym_new = int32(Encoder->:e, string:text, int32:ty) never fails {
    bool:b = raw is_bool(e, ty);
    SmtSym:s = SmtSym{ text: string_concat(text, ""), is_bool: b, sorts: "", fsort: raw fp_sort(e, ty) };
    drop list_push(@e.syms, move(s));
    int32:idx = (e.syms.count - 1i64) =>! int32;
    if (raw is_word(e, ty)) {
        List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one, idx);
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_range_axiom(text, raw word_bits(e, ty),
                                              raw word_signed(e, ty)), one);
    }
    if (raw is_twisted(e, ty)) {
        List<int32>:one2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one2, idx);
        drop hyp_push(e, raw twisted_axiom(e, text, ty), one2);
    }
    pass idx;
};

func:sym_text = string(Encoder->:e, int32:idx) never fails {
    pass (string_concat(e.syms[idx => int64].text, ""));
};

// A declared symbol by its text, or -1.
func:sym_find = int32(Encoder->:e, string:text) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
        if (string_equals(e.syms[i].text, text)) { pass (i =>! int32); }
    }
    pass 0i32 - 1i32;
};

// AN UNINTERPRETED FUNCTION SYMBOL (1.5.3 step 2, L-3): declared once per
// text, with its argument sorts and its result sort; a function symbol rides
// in a term's symbol list like a constant, so the cone closure declares it
// where an application appears.
func:sym_new_fun = int32(Encoder->:e, string:text, string:sorts, bool:ret_bool,
                         string:ret_fsort) never fails {
    int32:have = raw sym_find(e, text);
    if (have >= 0i32) { pass have; }
    SmtSym:s = SmtSym{ text: string_concat(text, ""), is_bool: ret_bool,
                       sorts: string_concat(sorts, ""), fsort: string_concat(ret_fsort, "") };
    drop list_push(@e.syms, move(s));
    pass ((e.syms.count - 1i64) =>! int32);
};

// A fresh anonymous opaque symbol of an int or bool type, as a term.
func:term_opaque = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (!(raw is_termed(e, ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:nm = raw smt_sym("_", e.anon => int64);
    int32:idx = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: raw is_bool(e, ty), text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

func:term_none = Term() never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: false, is_bool: false, text: "", syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64) };
};

// A FRESH SYMBOL WITH NO AXIOM, defined equal to a term (1.5.4b step 2): the
// twisted operations name a raw result before the saturation test reads it
// three times, and the raw result may lie OUTSIDE the type's range -- that
// is what the test decides -- so a typed symbol's axiom would be a false
// hypothesis. Int-sorted; never a Bool.
func:term_name = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:t, string:fsort) never fails {
    if (!(t.ok && (!t.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:nm = raw smt_sym("_", e.anon => int64);
    SmtSym:s = SmtSym{ text: string_concat(nm, ""), is_bool: false, sorts: "", fsort: string_concat(fsort, "") };
    drop list_push(@e.syms, move(s));
    int32:idx = (e.syms.count - 1i64) =>! int32;
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", nm, t.text), raw syms_union(one, t.syms));
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

func:term_lit = Term(string:text, bool:is_bool) never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: is_bool, text: string_concat(text, ""),
               syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64) };
};

func:syms_union = List<int32>(List<int32>:a, List<int32>:b) never fails {
    List<int32>:out = raw list_init::<int32>(a.count + b.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...a.count) { drop list_push(@out, a[i]); }
    for (int64:j in 0i64...b.count) {
        bool:have = false;
        for (int64:k in 0i64...out.count) { if (out[k] == b[j]) { have = true; } }
        if (!have) { drop list_push(@out, b[j]); }
    }
    pass out;
};

func:term_app2 = Term(string:op, Term:a, Term:b, bool:is_bool) never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: is_bool, text: raw smt_app2(op, a.text, b.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, b.syms) };
};

// Is the term a plain numeral (so a product or a division by it is linear)?
func:term_is_numeral = bool(Term:t) never fails {
    if (!t.ok) { pass false; }
    if (t.text.len == 0i64) { pass false; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...t.text.len) {
        uint8:c = t.text.ptr[i];
        if ((c < 48u8) || (c > 57u8)) { pass false; }
    }
    pass true;
};

// --- bindings and versions ---------------------------------------------------------------

func:version_next = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.ver_name.count) {
        if (e.ver_name[i] == name) {
            int32:k = e.ver_next[i];
            e.ver_next[i] = k + 1i32;
            pass (k => int64);
        }
    }
    drop list_push(@e.ver_name, name);
    drop list_push(@e.ver_next, 2i32);
    pass 1i64;
};

func:bind_find = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    int64:i = e.binds.count;
    while (i > 0i64) decreases i {
        i = i - 1i64;
        if (e.binds[i].name == name) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

func:is_escaped = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.escaped.count) { if (e.escaped[i] == name) { pass true; } }
    pass false;
};

// A new version of `name` with type `ty`: defined by `t` when the type is
// int/bool and the term is encodable; opaque (range axiom only) when the
// term is not; symbol-less when the type is neither -- or when the name is
// ADDRESS-TAKEN (DEF-14: an escaped name is never named, so every read of it
// is a fresh opaque term and no fact about it can outlive a call). A
// SUBSTITUTION binding (`enc_under`: a callee's parameter bound to an
// argument term already computed) never consults the escaped set -- the set
// is the CALLER's names, and a callee parameter that happened to share one
// bound unnamed and left its call-site row `open` (DEF-27, 1.5.4 step 0).
func:bind_define = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:ty, Term:t, int32:rule,
                       bool:substitution) never fails {
    int32:sym = 0i32 - 1i32;
    bool:named = raw is_termed(e, ty);   // a flag word (D-279), a twisted value (D-278) and a float (D-281) are named too
    if ((!substitution) && (raw is_escaped(e, name))) { named = false; }
    if (named) {
        string:nm = raw smt_sym(raw intern_get(e.interns, name), raw version_next(e, name));
        sym = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
        bool:define = t.ok;
        if (define) {
            if (t.is_bool != (raw is_bool(e, ty))) { define = false; }
        }
        if (define) {
            List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@one, sym);
            drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", nm, t.text), raw syms_union(one, t.syms));
        }
    }
    List<int32>:lanes = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    if ((raw is_simd(e, ty)) && (substitution || (!(raw is_escaped(e, name))))) { lanes = raw lane_syms_new(e, name, ty); }
    Bind:b = Bind{ name: name, sym: sym, type_id: ty, rule: rule, entry: sym, lanes: move(lanes), lensym: 0i32 - 1i32 };
    drop list_push(@e.binds, move(b));
    pass NIL;
};

// Assignment to an existing binding: a new version in place (same type). An
// escaped name stays unnamed (DEF-14).
func:bind_assign = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, Term:t) never fails {
    int64:i = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (i < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    e.binds[i].lensym = 0i32 - 1i32;   // a write ends the length symbol (1.5.8b step 5)
    int32:ty = e.binds[i].type_id;
    if (!(raw is_termed(e, ty))) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw is_escaped(e, name)) { pass NIL; }
    string:nm = raw smt_sym(raw intern_get(e.interns, name), raw version_next(e, name));
    int32:sym = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
    bool:define = t.ok;
    if (define) { if (t.is_bool != (raw is_bool(e, ty))) { define = false; } }
    if (define) {
        List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one, sym);
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", nm, t.text), raw syms_union(one, t.syms));
    }
    e.binds[i].sym = sym;
    pass NIL;
};

// Every binding named in `names` gets a fresh OPAQUE version (the value after a
// construct the straight line does not see through). An escaped name has no
// version to refresh (DEF-14).
func:invalidate = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:names) never fails {
    for (int64:k in 0i64...names.count) {
        int64:i = raw bind_find(e, names[k]);
        if (i < 0i64) { continue; }
        int32:ty = e.binds[i].type_id;
        // A WRITE OR AN INVALIDATION ENDS THE LENGTH SYMBOL (1.5.8b step 5):
        // the next read of this name's length names a fresh one, because the
        // container it stands for may be another one entirely.
        e.binds[i].lensym = 0i32 - 1i32;
        if (e.binds[i].lanes.count > 0i64) {
            e.binds[i].lanes = raw lane_syms_new(e, names[k], ty);
            continue;
        }
        if (!(raw is_termed(e, ty))) { continue; }
        if (raw is_escaped(e, names[k])) { continue; }
        string:nm = raw smt_sym(raw intern_get(e.interns, names[k]),
                                raw version_next(e, names[k]));
        e.binds[i].sym = raw sym_new(e, nm, ty);
        // A LIMITED NAME KEEPS ITS RULE ACROSS A MERGE (L-7): the fresh
        // version is "the value after the construct", and every write inside
        // was guarded by the rule -- the hypothesis, no obligation.
        drop assert_rule(e, i);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:invalidate_all = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    List<int32>:names = raw list_init::<int32>(e.binds.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds.count) { drop list_push(@names, e.binds[i].name); }
    drop invalidate(e, names);
    pass NIL;
};

// The symbols of every binding, to restore after a branch.
func:snapshot = List<int32>(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    List<int32>:out = raw list_init::<int32>(e.binds.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds.count) { drop list_push(@out, e.binds[i].sym); }
    pass out;
};

func:restore = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:snap) never fails {
    int64:n = snap.count;
    if (e.binds.count < n) { n = e.binds.count; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...n) { e.binds[i].sym = snap[i]; }
    // The lanes of every `simd` binding are fresh past a restore (D-282):
    // the snapshot carries scalar versions only, and opaque is sound.
    drop lanes_refresh_all(e);
    pass NIL;
};

func:scope_mark = int64(Encoder->:e) never fails { pass e.binds.count; };
func:scope_release = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:mark) never fails { drop list_truncate(@e.binds, mark); pass NIL; };

// --- obligations ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

func:record = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, string:goal, List<int32>:syms, int32:space,
                  int32:site, Span:at, bool:encoded) never fails {
    drop record_at(e, kind, goal, syms, space, site, at, encoded, raw ROLE_GUARD(), site, 1i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE FULL ROW (1.5.3 step 2, L-13): its role, the group it shares a guard
// with, and the traps that guard keeps when any row of the group is
// retained -- what the runners' belts read from `rows.txt`.
func:record_at = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, string:goal, List<int32>:syms, int32:space,
                     int32:site, Span:at, bool:encoded, int32:role, int32:group,
                     int32:traps) never fails {
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:ord = e.ordinals[kind => int64] + 1i32;
    e.ordinals[kind => int64] = ord;
    List<int32>:copy = raw list_init::<int32>(syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...syms.count) { drop list_push(@copy, syms[i]); }
    SmtObl:o = SmtObl{ kind: kind, goal: string_concat(goal, ""), syms: move(copy),
                       hyps: e.hyps.count, site: site, space: space, ordinal: ord,
                       ctx: e.clause_ctx, role: role, group: group, traps: traps,
                       defer_stmt: e.cur_defer,
                       line: at.line, col: at.col, region: e.cur_region, encoded: encoded,
                       checker: false, derived: false, tier: "",
                       cone_syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       cone_hyps: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       canon: "", hash: "", discharged: false };
    drop list_push(@e.obls, move(o));
    pass NIL;
};

// A ROW THE FRONTEND DECIDED (1.5.4 step 4, L-19, L-20): an `exhaustive` row
// at a `pick` (the 0.5 analysis refused every uncovered one before the
// backend ran), an `assert-static` row (the fold, TYPE-069). No query, no
// guard, verdict `checker` -- the catalogue's inventory entry.
func:record_checker = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:ord = e.ordinals[kind => int64] + 1i32;
    e.ordinals[kind => int64] = ord;
    SmtObl:o = SmtObl{ kind: kind, goal: "", syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       hyps: e.hyps.count, site: site, space: space, ordinal: ord,
                       ctx: e.clause_ctx, role: raw ROLE_GUARD(), group: site, traps: 0i32,
                       defer_stmt: e.cur_defer,
                       line: at.line, col: at.col, region: e.cur_region, encoded: false,
                       checker: true, derived: false, tier: "",
                       cone_syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       cone_hyps: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       canon: "", hash: "", discharged: false };
    drop list_push(@e.obls, move(o));
    pass NIL;
};

// A ROW THE RUNNERS DERIVE (D-305 (7), 1.5.8c step 4): the `stack-depth` row
// of a recursive group -- no query, no guard; its problem text names the
// group's members and whether every one states a measure, so the row moves
// when the group does, and both runners read its verdict off the group's
// `terminate` call rows once every file is decided (`discharged` when the
// members state measures and every recursive call's row is discharged, `open`
// otherwise). `d` in `rows.txt`.
func:record_derived = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at,
                          string:text) never fails {
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:ord = e.ordinals[kind => int64] + 1i32;
    e.ordinals[kind => int64] = ord;
    SmtObl:o = SmtObl{ kind: kind, goal: string_concat(text, ""), syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       hyps: e.hyps.count, site: site, space: space, ordinal: ord,
                       ctx: e.clause_ctx, role: raw ROLE_GUARD(), group: site, traps: 0i32,
                       defer_stmt: e.cur_defer,
                       line: at.line, col: at.col, region: e.cur_region, encoded: false,
                       checker: false, derived: true, tier: "",
                       cone_syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       cone_hyps: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                       canon: "", hash: "", discharged: false };
    drop list_push(@e.obls, move(o));
    pass NIL;
};

// The D-007 pair at a plain-integer division: `b != 0`, and for a signed
// width `not (a == MIN and b == -1)`. Terms that could not be expressed are
// stood in for by opaque symbols, so the obligation is recorded whatever the
// operands were (P-8, P-12).
func:record_division = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:lt, Term:a, Term:b, int32:site,
                           Span:at) never fails {
    Term:ta = raw term_copy(a);
    Term:tb = raw term_copy(b);
    if (!ta.ok) { ta = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    string:zero = raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, "0"));
    drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_ZERO(), zero, tb.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    // Inside a proposition the pair's conditions are the proposition's (DEF-33).
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, zero, tb.syms); }
    if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, lt)) {
        string:mn = raw smt_int_min(raw type_int_bits(e.types, lt));
        string:both = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("=", ta.text, mn),
                                   raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, "(- 1)"));
        drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_MIN(), raw smt_app1("not", both),
                    raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms), raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, raw smt_app1("not", both), raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms)); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE `overflow` ROW (D-210, D-309; 1.5.8b step 3): at a plain-integer `+ - *`
// or negation the emitter guards -- every one the folder does not write as its
// constant (`fold_node_constant`) -- the goal is the result inside its width,
// the guard's own condition, keyed at the guard's site (K-9). The fact is a
// hypothesis after the site: every continuing path passed the intrinsic's
// overflow bit; inside a proposition it is the proposition's (DEF-33). A result
// the walk could not express leaves the row `unencoded`, and the guard stays.
func:record_overflow = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:t, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if (!(t.ok && (!t.is_bool))) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_OVERFLOW(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    string:goal = raw smt_range_axiom(t.text, raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty),
                                      raw type_is_signed(e.types, ty));
    drop record(e, raw OK_OVERFLOW(), goal, t.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, t.syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, t.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// The any-lane `overflow` row (D-284's guard, D-282's shape): ONE row over
// every result lane's range, the emitter's one trap at the site. A lane the
// walk could not express leaves the row `unencoded`.
func:record_overflow_lanes = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:elem, List<Term>:out, int32:site,
                                 Span:at) never fails {
    string:goal = "";
    List<int32>:gs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    bool:all_ok = (out.count > 0i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...out.count) {
        if (!(out[i].ok && (!out[i].is_bool))) { all_ok = false; }
    }
    if (!all_ok) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_OVERFLOW(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    for (int64:j in 0i64...out.count) {
        string:one = raw smt_range_axiom(out[j].text, raw type_int_bits(e.types, elem),
                                         raw type_is_signed(e.types, elem));
        if (goal.len == 0i64) { goal = move(one); } else { goal = raw smt_app2("and", goal, one); }
        gs = raw syms_union(gs, out[j].syms);
    }
    drop record(e, raw OK_OVERFLOW(), goal, gs, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, gs); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, gs);
    pass NIL;
};

// The lanes of `a op b` for an overflow row: each lane's term, opaque where
// either side has none.
func:overflow_out_lanes = List<Term>(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:elem,
                                     List<Term>:la, List<Term>:lb, Span:at) never fails {
    List<Term>:out = raw list_init::<Term>(la.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...la.count) {
        if (i < lb.count) {
            drop list_push(@out, raw lane_binop(e, op, elem, la[i], lb[i], at));
        } else {
            drop list_push(@out, raw term_none());
        }
    }
    pass out;
};

// THE LENGTH OF A CONTAINER VALUE (1.5.8b step 5): an UNINTERPRETED function
// of the container's own term, `(|npk.len| s)`, so `s.len` where the program
// writes it and the bound a `bounds` row compares against are ONE term. Equal
// values have equal lengths, which is all a row needs: `for (i in 0...s.len)`
// bounds the index by the same symbol the row names, and the row discharges.
// A fixed array's length is its type's constant instead (DEF-22), known
// exactly. Anything else has no length term and its rows stay `open`.
func:len_term = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:base, int32:bty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, bty)) == (raw TY_ARRAY())) {
        pass (raw term_lit(int_to_string((raw type_array_count(e.types, bty)) => int64), false));
    }
    if (!base.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (base.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    int32:lf = raw sym_new_fun(e, "|npk.len|", "(Int)", false, "");
    List<int32>:lone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@lone, lf);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app1("|npk.len|", base.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(base.syms, lone) };
};

// THE LENGTH OF A CONTAINER A NAME HOLDS (1.5.8b step 5): the binding's own
// length symbol, named at the first read and fresh after every write or
// invalidation. A slice, a `string`, a `cstring`, a `buffer` and a `List` are
// AGGREGATES with no value term, so their length cannot hang off the value the
// way a number's facts do; it hangs off the NAME instead, and the name's
// version discipline is what keeps it honest. An escaped name (DEF-14) gets
// none: a call holding its address could change the container behind the
// walk's back. A base that is not a bare name gets none either.
func:place_len_term = Term(Encoder->:e, ExprId:base, int32:bty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, bty)) == (raw TY_ARRAY())) {
        pass (raw term_lit(int_to_string((raw type_array_count(e.types, bty)) => int64), false));
    }
    ExprNode:bn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, base);
    if (bn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    int32:nm = bn.payload =>! int32;
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, nm);
    if (bi < 0i64) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (raw is_escaped(e, nm)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    // THE SENTINEL IS -1, NEVER 0 (1.5.8b step 5): `sym_new` hands out ids from
    // ZERO, so a first-symbol length -- which is what a function whose first
    // named term is a length gets -- read as "not yet minted" and was re-minted
    // at every use. Two reads of `xs.len` then named two symbols and no row
    // over them could close. DEF-69's rule: a sentinel is a value the domain
    // never produces.
    if (e.binds[bi].lensym < 0i32) {
        string:lt = string_concat("len.", raw intern_get(e.interns, nm));
        string:lnm = raw smt_sym(lt, raw version_next(e, nm));
        // THE RANGE AXIOM GOES IN THE ROOT REGION, not wherever the first read
        // happens to be (1.5.8b step 5). A symbol's range is a fact about its
        // SORT -- true on every path -- while a hypothesis is only in a row's
        // cone when its region dominates the row's. One symbol read from two
        // loops would otherwise carry its axiom in the first loop alone, and a
        // row in the second could not use `i < len <= MAX`: measured, two rows
        // of `nio_normalize` stopped discharging when the length became one
        // symbol, though the facts around them were strictly stronger.
        int32:preg = e.cur_region;
        e.cur_region = 0i32;
        int32:lsy = raw sym_new(e, lnm, raw tt_int(e.types, 64i32, true));
        // THE CEILING IS A FACT ABOUT THE SYMBOL'S SORT (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step
        // 6c), true on every path like its width's range, so it lives here in
        // the root region too. A `List`'s length takes its rule at each read.
        if (raw has_len_term(e, bty)) {
            List<int32>:lsl = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@lsl, lsy);
            drop hyp_push(e, raw len_ceiling_goal(raw sym_text(e, lsy)), lsl);
        }
        e.cur_region = preg;
        e.binds[bi].lensym = lsy;
    }
    List<int32>:ls = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@ls, e.binds[bi].lensym);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
               text: raw sym_text(e, e.binds[bi].lensym), syms: move(ls) };
};

// Does this kind carry a length the encoder can name? A slice, a `string`, a
// `cstring`, a `buffer` and a `List` do; a fixed array's is its type's.
func:has_len_term = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:bty) never fails {
    int32:k = raw type_kind(e.types, bty);
    if (k == (raw TY_ARRAY()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_SLICE()))   { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_STRING()))  { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_CSTRING())) { pass true; }
    if (k == (raw TY_BUFFER()))  { pass true; }
    pass false;
};

// THE `bounds` ROW (D-070; 1.5.8b step 5): the index is inside its bound --
// `0 <= i` and `i < len`, the unsigned compare's own meaning -- at the INDEX
// EXPRESSION's site, the key the emitter guards and elides under. The fact is
// a hypothesis after the site (every continuing path passed the compare), and
// inside a proposition it is the proposition's (DEF-33). A term the walk
// cannot express leaves the row `unencoded`, and the guard stays.
func:record_bounds = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:idx, Term:len, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if (!(idx.ok && len.ok && (!idx.is_bool) && (!len.is_bool))) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_BOUNDS(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    string:goal = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("<=", "0", idx.text),
                               raw smt_app2("<", idx.text, len.text));
    List<int32>:gs = raw syms_union(idx.syms, len.syms);
    drop record(e, raw OK_BOUNDS(), goal, gs, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, gs); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, gs);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE LENGTH CEILING'S ROW (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step 6c): `0 <= len <= 2^47` at a
// call of `string_from_bytes` or `#wild_slice`, the emitter's guard read back
// (one unsigned compare there, the two-sided Int form here), keyed on the
// CALL's own node. A `bounds` row: a length past the address space is a view
// out of bounds, and the guard traps `OutOfBounds`. The fact is a hypothesis
// after the site; inside a proposition it is the proposition's (DEF-33).
func:record_len_ceiling = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:len, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if (!(len.ok && (!len.is_bool))) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_BOUNDS(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    string:goal = raw len_ceiling_goal(len.text);
    drop record(e, raw OK_BOUNDS(), goal, len.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, len.syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, len.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// The ceiling as a proposition over one term.
func:len_ceiling_goal = string(string:t) never fails {
    pass (raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("<=", "0", t),
                       raw smt_app2("<=", t, raw len_ceiling_text())));
};

// THE BUILT-IN LENGTH FACT (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step 6c): a `.len` or `.cap` of a
// `string`, a `cstring`, a slice or a `buffer` lies in [0, 2^47] wherever it is
// read, because the allocator refuses a larger block and the two producers of
// a caller-supplied length are guarded -- and because nothing but the module
// that makes a header may write one (D-313). Pushed at a READ, never inside a
// proposition's own evaluation (DEF-33); a `List`'s `count` and `cap` carry the
// same numbers as a field rule (`ListLen`) and ride D-308 SS3's mechanism.
func:push_len_fact = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:t) never fails {
    if (!(t.ok && (!t.is_bool))) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, raw len_ceiling_goal(t.text), t.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A RANGE VIEW'S ONE ROW (1.5.8b step 5): the emitter's guard is one compare
// of both conditions -- `lo <= hi` and `hi <= len` -- so the row is one too,
// at the range expression's own site. The inclusive form's bound is `hi + 1`,
// exactly as the emitter computes it.
func:record_bounds_range = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:lo, Term:hi, Term:len, int32:site,
                               Span:at) never fails {
    if (!(lo.ok && hi.ok && len.ok && (!lo.is_bool) && (!hi.is_bool) && (!len.is_bool))) {
        List<int32>:none2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_BOUNDS(), "", none2, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    string:goal = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("<=", lo.text, hi.text),
                               raw smt_app2("<=", hi.text, len.text));
    List<int32>:gs2 = raw syms_union(raw syms_union(lo.syms, hi.syms), len.syms);
    drop record(e, raw OK_BOUNDS(), goal, gs2, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, gs2); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, gs2);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE `cast-range` ROW (D-306; 1.5.8b step 5): a float's cast to an integer
// has an integer meaning -- the value is a number (an ordered compare is false
// for NaN) strictly inside the target's range. The goal is the EMITTER's own
// guard, term for term: the two ordered compares against `double` bounds that
// `cast_bounds.npk` renders for both spellings, with a `flt32` operand widened
// exactly, as the emitter's `fpext` widens it. The fact is a hypothesis after
// the site; inside a proposition it is the proposition's (DEF-33).
func:record_cast_range = NIL(Encoder->:e, Term:f, int32:sty, int32:dty, int32:site,
                             Span:at) never fails {
    if (!(f.ok && (!f.is_bool))) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_CAST_RANGE(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    string:d = string_concat(f.text, "");
    if ((raw word_bits(e, sty)) == 32i32) {
        d = raw smt_app2("(_ to_fp 11 53)", "RNE", f.text);
    }
    int32:bits = raw word_bits(e, dty);
    bool:sg = raw word_signed(e, dty);
    string:lo = raw cast_bound_smt(raw cast_lo_const(bits, sg));
    string:hi = raw cast_bound_smt(raw cast_hi_const(bits, sg));
    if ((lo.len == 0i64) || (hi.len == 0i64)) {
        List<int32>:none2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record(e, raw OK_CAST_RANGE(), "", none2, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    e.uses_fp = true;
    string:goal = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2(raw cast_lo_smt_pred(bits, sg), d, lo),
                               raw smt_app2("fp.lt", d, hi));
    drop record(e, raw OK_CAST_RANGE(), goal, f.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, f.syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, f.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A SHIFT BY A COMPUTED AMOUNT (D-277, 1.5.4b step 0): the `shift-range` row
// is the guard's own condition, the amount inside `0..width-1`. A literal
// amount records nothing (the checker held it in range and the emitter
// guards nothing); an amount the folder knows -- a `fixed` constant -- is a
// numeral goal, discharged at once and its guard elided; any other amount's
// term, opaque or not, is the goal's. The fact is a hypothesis after the
// site: every continuing path passed the compare, as `div-zero`'s does not
// need saying because a division's value is defined by its own guard.
func:record_shift = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:lt, Term:b, ExprId:amount, int32:site,
                        Span:at) never fails {
    // INSIDE A PROPOSITION THE CONDITION IS THE PROPOSITION'S (DEF-33,
    // 1.5.4b step 2), gathered by `prop_fact`, never pushed: this function
    // pushed its goal wherever it ran from step 0 until here, so a `requires
    // n < 32` beside a `(x << n)` in the same contract had its bound
    // ASSUMED -- in the caller's context at a call-site row, and in the
    // entry row's own cone at the callee, where the check that runs the
    // guard is what the row's discharge removes. The row is still recorded
    // where the encoding is loud (an entry, a seam, a head: the guard is
    // lowered in the check), and suppressed under quiet (L-1).
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(e.ast, amount);
    if (an.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) { pass NIL; }
    Term:tb = raw term_copy(b);
    if (!(tb.ok && (raw term_is_numeral(tb)))) {
        ConstVal:cv = raw fold_const(e.tr, amount, e.scope);
        if (cv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) { tb = raw term_lit(raw smt_int(cv.num), false); }
    }
    if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    string:w = int_to_string((raw type_int_bits(e.types, lt)) => int64);
    string:goal = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2(">=", tb.text, "0"),
                               raw smt_app2("<", tb.text, w));
    drop record(e, raw OK_SHIFT_RANGE(), goal, tb.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, tb.syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, tb.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the `disjoint` row (D-286, 1.5.5 step 2) ----------------------------------
//
// AT A GUARD SITE -- an access the aliasing analysis paired with live
// parties through computed indices -- the goal is that the access's storage
// and every party's are disjoint: for each party, the `or` over the index
// pairs along the paths' common prefix of `(not (= tP tQ))` (a numeral pair
// that is equal says nothing; one that differs makes the party disjoint
// outright, as does a field step that differs); the row's goal the `and`
// over the parties. `tP` is the party's index term as memoised when its
// claim was walked, `tQ` the access's; a missing term is opaque and the row
// `open`, the guard kept. The fact is a hypothesis after the site (every
// continuing path passed the compare), as `shift-range`'s is; inside a
// proposition it is the proposition's (DEF-33). One row per site: the
// emitter elides the site's one compare on it.
pub struct:PStep = { bool:is_index; bool:is_range; int32:name; int32:ix; };

func:memo_put = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:id, Term:t) never fails {
    if (!t.ok) { pass NIL; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.memo_ids.count) {
        if (e.memo_ids[i] == id) { e.memo_terms[i] = raw term_copy(t); pass NIL; }
    }
    drop list_push(@e.memo_ids, id);
    drop list_push(@e.memo_terms, raw term_copy(t));
    pass NIL;
};

func:memo_get = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:id) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.memo_ids.count) {
        if (e.memo_ids[i] == id) { pass (raw term_copy(e.memo_terms[i])); }
    }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// The steps of a place, root-outward: a field name or an index expression.
func:enc_path = bool(Encoder->:e, ExprId:place, List<PStep>->:out) never fails {
    List<PStep>:rev = raw list_init::<PStep>(8i64);
    ExprId:cur = place;
    for (int32:hop in 0i32...64i32) {
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass false; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, cur);
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
            drop list_push(@rev, PStep{ is_index: false, is_range: false, name: (raw expr_name(n)) =>! int32, ix: 0i32 });
            cur = raw expr_operand(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
            ExprNode:ixn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw expr_rhs(n));
            bool:rg = (ixn.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr);
            drop list_push(@rev, PStep{ is_index: true, is_range: rg, name: 0i32, ix: (raw expr_rhs(n)).index });
            cur = raw expr_lhs(n);
            continue;
        }
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            int64:k = rev.count;
            while (k > 0i64) decreases k { k = k - 1i64; drop list_push(out, rev[k]); }
            pass true;
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

func:index_term = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ix) never fails {
    Term:t = raw memo_get(e, ix);
    if (t.ok) { pass t; }
    pass (raw term_opaque(e, raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: ix })));
};

func:enc_alias_site = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    int32:np = raw exprtypes_alias_count_at(e.et, id.index);
    if (np == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:an = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    List<PStep>:ap = raw list_init::<PStep>(8i64);
    if (!(raw enc_path(e, id, @ap))) { pass NIL; }
    string:goal = "";
    List<int32>:syms = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    bool:have_party = false;
    for (int32:k in 0i32...np) {
        int32:psite = raw exprtypes_alias_party_at(e.et, id.index, k);
        ExprNode:pn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, ExprId{ index: psite });
        List<PStep>:pp = raw list_init::<PStep>(8i64);
        if (!(raw enc_path(e, raw expr_operand(pn), @pp))) { continue; }
        int64:m = ap.count;
        if (pp.count < m) { m = pp.count; }
        string:pg = "";
        bool:pdisjoint = false;
        for (int64:i in 0i64...m) {
            PStep:sa = ap[i];
            PStep:sp = pp[i];
            if ((!sa.is_index) && (!sp.is_index)) {
                if (sa.name != sp.name) { pdisjoint = true; }
                continue;
            }
            if (sa.is_index && sp.is_index) {
                if (sa.is_range || sp.is_range) { continue; }
                Term:tq = raw index_term(e, sa.ix);
                Term:tp = raw index_term(e, sp.ix);
                NumVal:nq = raw numeral_of(e, tq, ExprId{ index: sa.ix });
                NumVal:npv = raw numeral_of(e, tp, ExprId{ index: sp.ix });
                if (nq.ok && npv.ok) {
                    if (nq.v != npv.v) { pdisjoint = true; }
                    continue;
                }
                if (!tq.ok) { tq = raw term_opaque(e, raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: sa.ix })); }
                if (!tp.ok) { tp = raw term_opaque(e, raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: sp.ix })); }
                if (!(tq.ok && tp.ok)) { continue; }
                string:d = raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", tp.text, tq.text));
                if (pg.len == 0i64) { pg = string_concat(d, ""); } else { pg = raw smt_app2("or", pg, d); }
                syms = raw syms_union(syms, raw syms_union(tp.syms, tq.syms));
                continue;
            }
            // a field against an index (typing admits no such pair): the extent overlaps
        }
        if (pdisjoint) { continue; }
        if (pg.len == 0i64) { pg = "false"; }
        if (goal.len == 0i64) { goal = string_concat(pg, ""); } else { goal = raw smt_app2("and", goal, pg); }
        have_party = true;
    }
    if (!have_party) { pass NIL; }
    drop record(e, raw OK_DISJOINT(), goal, syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, an.span, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE `err-exit` ROW (D-278, 1.5.4b step 2): the `TbbErr` guard's own
// condition -- neither operand ERR at a comparison, the operand not ERR at a
// cast out of its family, the value inside the target's range at a checked
// crossing into or within one -- and the fact a hypothesis after the site,
// as `shift-range`'s is (every continuing path passed the trap); inside a
// proposition the condition is the proposition's (DEF-33, above).
func:record_err_exit = NIL(Encoder->:e, string:goal, List<int32>:syms, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    drop record(e, raw OK_ERR_EXIT(), goal, syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A `TbbErr` guard over a value the walk has no term for -- a `frac`, a
// tfp-element `complex`, a float crossing into a twisted family: the row
// exists (P-12), `unencoded` (L-6); step 3 gives the float crossing its goal.
func:record_unencoded_err_exit = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop record(e, raw OK_ERR_EXIT(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the twisted kinds (D-278, 1.5.4b step 2) ----------------------------------------------
//
// EVERY OPERATION IS THE EMITTER'S SHAPE (1.3.2, 1.3.4; `emit_arith_value`):
// any ERR operand makes ERR (`taint`); `+`, `-` and `tbb`'s `*` saturate to
// ERR outside the valid range (a result landing ON the sentinel is ERR by
// the same test -- `LO` is `MIN + 1`); `tfp`'s `*` is the floor of the
// product scaled down by 2^F (`div` by a positive numeral IS the `ashr`),
// its `/` the truncating quotient of the dividend scaled up (`npk_sdiv`),
// each narrowed by the same range test; `/` and `%` at the same scale make
// ERR of a zero divisor and are in range by construction (`tbb_divlike`);
// the ternary kinds compute the same way against their balanced bounds, and
// their single-digit `&`/`|` are min/max (D-197). Each raw result is NAMED
// once (`term_name`) before the test reads it. A comparison records the
// `err-exit` row first (the trap precedes the compare) and is then the plain
// Int predicate. A twisted division records no row: it never traps.

// `(or (= a MIN) (= b MIN))`.
func:tw_taint = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:a, Term:b) never fails {
    string:mn = raw tw_min(e, ty);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true,
               text: raw smt_app2("or", raw smt_app2("=", a.text, mn), raw smt_app2("=", b.text, mn)),
               syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, b.syms) };
};

// `(ite bad MIN v)` with `v` named once.
func:tw_pick = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:bad, Term:v) never fails {
    Term:nv = raw term_name(e, v, "");
    if (!nv.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", bad.text, raw tw_min(e, ty), nv.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(bad.syms, nv.syms) };
};

// The saturation: ERR when tainted or when the named raw value leaves the
// type's valid range.
func:tw_sat = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:taint, Term:v) never fails {
    Term:nv = raw term_name(e, v, "");
    if (!nv.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:lo = raw term_lit(raw tw_lo(e, ty), false);
    Term:hi = raw term_lit(raw tw_hi(e, ty), false);
    Term:oor = raw term_app2("or", raw term_app2("<", nv, lo, true), raw term_app2(">", nv, hi, true), true);
    Term:bad = raw term_app2("or", taint, oor, true);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", bad.text, raw tw_min(e, ty), nv.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(bad.syms, nv.syms) };
};

// "Out of the range whose magnitude is `hi`": both sides for a signed
// source, the top alone for an unsigned one -- the cast matrix's entry test.
func:tw_oor = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:a, string:hi, bool:signed) never fails {
    Term:above = raw term_app2(">", a, raw term_lit(string_concat(hi, ""), false), true);
    if (!signed) { pass above; }
    Term:below = raw term_app2("<", a, raw term_lit(raw smt_app1("-", hi), false), true);
    pass (raw term_app2("or", above, below, true));
};

func:tw_is_cmp = bool(TokenKind:op) never fails {
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpEqEq) || (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq)) { pass true; }
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpLt) || (op == TokenKind.OpLtEq)) { pass true; }
    pass ((op == TokenKind.OpGt) || (op == TokenKind.OpGtEq));
};

func:enc_twisted_binary = Term(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:lt, int32:ty, Term:a, Term:b,
                               int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    Term:ta = raw term_copy(a);
    Term:tb = raw term_copy(b);
    if (!ta.ok) { ta = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    if (!(ta.ok && tb.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    if (ta.is_bool || tb.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    if (raw tw_is_cmp(op)) {
        string:mn = raw tw_min(e, lt);
        string:goal = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", ta.text, mn)),
                                   raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, mn)));
        drop record_err_exit(e, goal, raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms), site, at);
        if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", ta, tb, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", ta, tb, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpLt)    { pass (raw term_app2("<", ta, tb, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpLtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("<=", ta, tb, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpGt)    { pass (raw term_app2(">", ta, tb, true)); }
        pass (raw term_app2(">=", ta, tb, true));
    }
    Term:taint = raw tw_taint(e, lt, ta, tb);
    int32:k = raw type_kind(e.types, lt);
    bool:q = ((k == (raw TY_TFP())) || (k == (raw TY_DIM())));
    if ((k == (raw TY_TERN())) && ((op == TokenKind.OpAmp) || (op == TokenKind.OpPipe))) {
        string:kord = "<";
        if (op == TokenKind.OpPipe) { kord = ">"; }
        Term:kv = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
                        text: raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(kord, ta.text, tb.text), ta.text, tb.text),
                        syms: raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms) };
        pass (raw tw_pick(e, lt, taint, kv));
    }
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercent)) {
        Term:zero = raw term_app2("=", tb, raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:bad = raw term_app2("or", taint, zero, true);
        e.uses_sdiv = true;
        e.nonlinear = true;
        if (op == TokenKind.OpPercent) { pass (raw tw_pick(e, lt, bad, raw term_app2("npk_srem", ta, tb, false))); }
        if (!q) { pass (raw tw_pick(e, lt, bad, raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", ta, tb, false))); }
        Term:up = raw term_app2("*", ta, raw tw_pow2f(e, lt), false);
        pass (raw tw_sat(e, lt, bad, raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", up, tb, false)));
    }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlus)  { pass (raw tw_sat(e, lt, taint, raw term_app2("+", ta, tb, false))); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) { pass (raw tw_sat(e, lt, taint, raw term_app2("-", ta, tb, false))); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStar) {
        if (!((raw term_is_numeral(ta)) || (raw term_is_numeral(tb)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        Term:prod = raw term_app2("*", ta, tb, false);
        if (!q) { pass (raw tw_sat(e, lt, taint, prod)); }
        pass (raw tw_sat(e, lt, taint, raw term_app2("div", prod, raw tw_pow2f(e, lt), false)));
    }
    pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
};

// A TWISTED LITERAL: a `tbb` or ternary literal is its value (the checker
// held it in range); a `tfp`/`dim256` literal is its exact Q value through
// the one conversion the checker range-tested and the emitter spells
// (`tfp_q_decimal`, D-195), from the integer payload or the kept text.
func:twisted_int_literal = Term(Encoder->:e, int64:v, int32:ty) never fails {
    int32:k = raw type_kind(e.types, ty);
    if ((k == (raw TY_TFP())) || (k == (raw TY_DIM()))) {
        pass (raw twisted_text_literal(e, int_to_string(v), ty));
    }
    pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(v), false));
};

func:twisted_text_literal = Term(Encoder->:e, string:text, int32:ty) never fails {
    string:q = raw tfp_q_decimal(text, raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty));
    if (q.len == 0i64) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass (raw term_lit(move(q), false));
};

// A VALUE READ AS THE TARGET WORD -- the `trunc`/`sext` a leaving cast ends
// with: the identity where the target is signed and at least `need` bits
// wide (the value fits by construction), else the two's-complement pattern
// at the target's width, re-signed as the target reads it.
func:wrap_word = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:to, Term:v, int32:need) never fails {
    int32:wb = raw word_bits(e, to);
    if ((raw word_signed(e, to)) && (wb >= need)) { pass (raw term_copy(v)); }
    Term:nv = raw term_name(e, v, "");
    if (!nv.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:full = raw pow2_decimal(wb => int64);
    Term:m = raw term_app2("mod", nv, raw term_lit(string_concat(full, ""), false), false);
    if (!(raw word_signed(e, to))) { pass m; }
    Term:nm = raw term_name(e, m, "");
    if (!nm.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:half = raw pow2_decimal((wb => int64) - 1i64);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
               text: raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(">=", nm.text, half), raw smt_app2("-", nm.text, full), nm.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(nm.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
};

// A CAST WITHIN A FAMILY (D-144 as amended, D-195, D-197): the sentinel
// maps across widths (`(ite (= a MIN_s) MIN_d v)`); a narrowing `=>` traps a
// valid value outside the target's range (the row: ERR, or in range) and
// `=>!` absorbs it as ERR; a `tfp` widens by 2^dF and narrows by the floor
// of the scale-down, out-of-range ERR under both spellings.
func:twisted_within = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:a, int32:from, int32:to, bool:unchecked,
                           int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:sk = raw type_kind(e.types, from);
    string:mnd = raw tw_min(e, to);
    Term:iserr = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app2("=", a.text, raw tw_min(e, from)),
                       syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    if ((sk == (raw TY_TFP())) || (sk == (raw TY_DIM()))) {
        int32:sb = raw type_int_bits(e.types, from);
        int32:db = raw type_int_bits(e.types, to);
        if (db > sb) {
            Term:up = raw term_app2("*", a, raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(((db - sb) / 2i32) => int64), false), false);
            pass (raw tw_pick(e, to, iserr, up));
        }
        if (db < sb) {
            Term:down = raw term_app2("div", a, raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(((sb - db) / 2i32) => int64), false), false);
            pass (raw tw_sat(e, to, iserr, down));
        }
        pass (raw term_copy(a));
    }
    bool:narrow = false;
    if (sk == (raw TY_TBB())) { narrow = ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, to)) < (raw type_int_bits(e.types, from))); }
    else { narrow = ((raw tw_bound(e, to)) < (raw tw_bound(e, from))); }
    if (!narrow) { pass (raw tw_pick(e, to, iserr, a)); }
    Term:lo = raw term_lit(raw tw_lo(e, to), false);
    Term:hi = raw term_lit(raw tw_hi(e, to), false);
    Term:oor = raw term_app2("or", raw term_app2("<", a, lo, true), raw term_app2(">", a, hi, true), true);
    if (!unchecked) {
        string:goal = raw smt_app2("or", iserr.text, raw smt_app1("not", oor.text));
        drop record_err_exit(e, goal, raw syms_union(iserr.syms, oor.syms), site, at);
        pass (raw tw_pick(e, to, iserr, a));
    }
    pass (raw tw_pick(e, to, raw term_app2("or", iserr, oor, true), a));
};

// A CAST TOUCHING A TWISTED FAMILY: the matrix's value maps as terms and its
// `TbbErr` guards as `err-exit` rows (`emit_tbb_cast`/`emit_tfp_cast`/
// `emit_tern_cast`, mirrored). LEAVING: the row `(not (= a MIN))` under both
// spellings; the value the operand's integer (a `tfp`'s truncated toward
// zero) as the target word reads it; a float target has no term (step 3).
// ENTERING from an integer: a source that can exceed the target's range
// traps under `=>` (the row: in range) and absorbs under `=>!`; a `tfp`
// scales up and absorbs under both. From a float: the guard's row
// `unencoded` (the float has no term until step 3), the value opaque.
// `dim256` and `tfp256` are one term (a relabel, D-196). `term_none` for a
// cast that is not this family's.
func:twisted_cast = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:t, int32:from, int32:to, bool:unchecked,
                         int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if ((from == 0i32) || (to == 0i32)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    // THE `frac` MATRIX'S GUARDS (D-198): leaving the family traps ERR under
    // both spellings over an aggregate the walk has no term for -- the row
    // `unencoded`; a checked entry from an integer that can exceed the
    // component's balanced bound traps out of range -- the row over the
    // integer's term, as `tbb`'s entry below. A frac-to-frac cast absorbs.
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, from)) == (raw TY_FRAC())) {
        if ((raw type_kind(e.types, to)) != (raw TY_FRAC())) { drop record_unencoded_err_exit(e, site, at); }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, to)) == (raw TY_FRAC())) {
        if ((!unchecked) && (raw is_int(e, from))) {
            Term:fa = raw term_copy(t);
            if (!(fa.ok && (!fa.is_bool))) { fa = raw term_opaque(e, from); }
            bool:fsig = raw type_is_signed(e.types, from);
            int32:fsw = raw type_int_bits(e.types, from);
            int32:fdb = raw type_int_bits(e.types, to);
            bool:ffits = false;
            if (fsw < 63i32) {
                int64:fsmax = raw pow2_int64(fsw - 1i32);
                if (!fsig) { fsmax = (raw pow2_int64(fsw)) - 1i64; }
                if (fdb >= 63i32) { ffits = true; }
                else { if (fsmax <= ((raw pow2_int64(fdb - 1i32)) - 1i64)) { ffits = true; } }
            }
            if (fa.ok && (!ffits)) {
                Term:foor = raw tw_oor(e, fa, raw pow2_minus_one_decimal((fdb => int64) - 1i64), fsig);
                drop record_err_exit(e, raw smt_app1("not", foor.text), foor.syms, site, at);
            }
        }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    bool:tf = raw is_twisted(e, from);
    bool:tt = raw is_twisted(e, to);
    if (!(tf || tt)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    int32:sk = raw type_kind(e.types, from);
    int32:dk = raw type_kind(e.types, to);
    Term:a = raw term_copy(t);
    if (!(a.ok && (!a.is_bool))) {
        a = raw term_none();
        if (raw is_scalar(e, from)) { a = raw term_opaque(e, from); }
    }
    bool:relabel = ((sk == (raw TY_DIM())) && (dk == (raw TY_TFP())));
    if ((sk == (raw TY_TFP())) && (dk == (raw TY_DIM()))) { relabel = true; }
    if (relabel) {
        if (a.ok) { pass a; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, to));
    }
    if (tf && tt) {
        if (!a.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, to)); }
        pass (raw twisted_within(e, a, from, to, unchecked, site, at));
    }
    if (tf) {
        if (!a.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, to)); }
        drop record_err_exit(e, raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", a.text, raw tw_min(e, from))), a.syms, site, at);
        if (!(raw is_word(e, to))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        Term:v = raw term_copy(a);
        int32:need = raw type_int_bits(e.types, from);
        if ((sk == (raw TY_TFP())) || (sk == (raw TY_DIM()))) {
            Term:p2 = raw tw_pow2f(e, from);
            Term:pos = raw term_app2("div", a, p2, false);
            Term:neg = raw term_app2("div", raw term_app2("-", raw term_lit("0", false), a, false), p2, false);
            v = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
                      text: raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(">=", a.text, "0"), pos.text, raw smt_app2("-", "0", neg.text)),
                      syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
            need = need / 2i32;
        }
        pass (raw wrap_word(e, to, v, need));
    }
    if (sk == (raw TY_FLOAT())) {
        bool:absorbs = ((dk == (raw TY_TFP())) || (dk == (raw TY_DIM())));
        if (absorbs) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, to)); }
        // A FLOAT ENTERING `tbb` OR A TERNARY KIND (D-281 over step 2's
        // handoff): the emitter compares in DOUBLE against strict bounds --
        // `fcmp ogt`/`olt`, false for NaN -- traps under `=>` and absorbs to
        // ERR under `=>!`; the value is the double truncated toward zero.
        // A `flt32` widens first, as the emitter's `fpext` does.
        bool:fok = a.ok && (raw is_float(e, from));
        if (!fok) {
            if (!unchecked) { drop record_unencoded_err_exit(e, site, at); }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, to));
        }
        int32:t64 = raw tt_float(e.types, 64i32);
        Term:f = raw term_copy(a);
        if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, from)) == 32i32) {
            f = raw fp_make(e, "widen", t64, a.text, "", raw smt_app1("(_ to_fp 11 53) RNE", a.text), a.syms);
        }
        string:mag = "";
        if (dk == (raw TY_TBB())) {
            mag = string_concat(raw pow2_decimal(((raw type_int_bits(e.types, to)) => int64) - 1i64), ".0");
        } else {
            mag = string_concat(int_to_string((raw tw_bound(e, to)) + 1i64), ".0");
        }
        string:nmag = raw smt_app1("-", mag);
        Term:hi = raw fp_make(e, "lit", t64, mag, "", raw smt_app1("(_ to_fp 11 53) RNE", mag), raw list_init::<int32>(1i64));
        Term:lo = raw fp_make(e, "lit", t64, nmag, "", raw smt_app1("(_ to_fp 11 53) RNE", nmag), raw list_init::<int32>(1i64));
        if (!(f.ok && hi.ok && lo.ok)) {
            if (!unchecked) { drop record_unencoded_err_exit(e, site, at); }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, to));
        }
        Term:inr = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("fp.gt", f, lo, true), raw term_app2("fp.lt", f, hi, true), true);
        string:r = raw smt_app1("fp.to_real", f.text);
        string:tz = raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(">=", r, "0.0"), raw smt_app1("to_int", r),
                                 raw smt_app2("-", "0", raw smt_app1("to_int", raw smt_app2("-", "0.0", r))));
        Term:val = raw term_name(e, Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(tz),
                                          syms: raw syms_union(f.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) }, "");
        if (!val.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, to)); }
        if (!unchecked) {
            drop record_err_exit(e, inr.text, inr.syms, site, at);
            pass val;
        }
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", inr.text, val.text, raw tw_min(e, to)),
                   syms: raw syms_union(inr.syms, val.syms) };
    }
    if (!(raw is_int(e, from))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (!a.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, to)); }
    string:mnd = raw tw_min(e, to);
    bool:ssig = raw type_is_signed(e.types, from);
    int32:sw = raw type_int_bits(e.types, from);
    if ((dk == (raw TY_TFP())) || (dk == (raw TY_DIM()))) {
        int32:fb = (raw type_int_bits(e.types, to)) / 2i32;
        Term:scaled = raw term_app2("*", a, raw tw_pow2f(e, to), false);
        if (sw < fb) { pass scaled; }
        Term:oor = raw tw_oor(e, a, raw pow2_minus_one_decimal((fb => int64) - 1i64), ssig);
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", oor.text, mnd, scaled.text),
                   syms: raw syms_union(oor.syms, scaled.syms) };
    }
    bool:fits = false;
    if (dk == (raw TY_TBB())) { fits = (sw < (raw type_int_bits(e.types, to))); }
    else {
        if (sw < 63i32) {
            int64:smax = raw pow2_int64(sw - 1i32);
            if (!ssig) { smax = (raw pow2_int64(sw)) - 1i64; }
            if (smax <= (raw tw_bound(e, to))) { fits = true; }
        }
    }
    if (fits) { pass a; }
    Term:oor2 = raw tw_oor(e, a, raw tw_hi(e, to), ssig);
    if (!unchecked) {
        drop record_err_exit(e, raw smt_app1("not", oor2.text), oor2.syms, site, at);
        pass a;
    }
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", oor2.text, mnd, a.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(oor2.syms, a.syms) };
};

// --- floats, tier 1 (D-281, 1.5.4b step 3) ----------------------------------------------
//
// A `flt32`/`flt64` value is a term of the IEEE sort, and every operation is
// the emitter's instruction under SMT-LIB's IEEE semantics: `fadd`/`fsub`/
// `fmul`/`fdiv` are `fp.add`/`fp.sub`/`fp.mul`/`fp.div` under RNE (LLVM's
// default rounding), `fneg` is `fp.neg`, `#sqrt` is `fp.sqrt RNE`, `frem` is
// not `fp.rem` (a truncated fmod against IEEE's remainder) and stays opaque;
// the comparisons are the ORDERED predicates the emitter writes -- `oeq` is
// `fp.eq`, `une` its negation (NaN != NaN is true, as `fcmp une` says),
// `olt`/`ole`/`ogt`/`oge` are `fp.lt`/`fp.leq`/`fp.gt`/`fp.geq`, each false
// on a NaN operand. A literal is `to_fp RNE` of the EXACT rational its
// decimal text denotes -- what LLVM's own parser rounds from, so the two
// agree by IEEE's correct-rounding rule -- and a `flt32` literal takes the
// emitter's road (a double, then `fptrunc`): two roundings, spelled twice.
// An integer entering a float is `to_fp RNE (to_real x)` (`sitofp`/
// `uitofp`); a widening `flt32 => flt64` is exact, a narrowing `=>!` rounds;
// a float LEAVING to an integer stays opaque until 1.5.8's `cast-range`.
// Every float value is NAMED (`fp_make`) and its definition recorded
// (`fpdefs`) for the tier-2 translation. Floats never trap (D-007): no row
// is recorded here; what these terms buy is that a `limit`, a contract, an
// `invariant` and a `prove` over floats are encoded rows.

// The exact rational a decimal literal denotes: `(/ N 10^k)` or `(* N 10^k)`
// from the digits and the exponent, the type suffix cut.
func:decimal_to_real = string(string:txt) never fails {
    string:digits = "";
    int64:frac = 0i64;
    int64:ex = 0i64;
    bool:negex = false;
    int32:st = 0i32;   // 0 whole, 1 fraction, 2 exponent
    for (int64:i in 0i64...txt.len) {
        uint8:c = txt.ptr[i];
        if (c == 102u8) { break; }                      // 'f': the suffix
        if (c == 46u8) { st = 1i32; continue; }           // '.'
        if ((c == 101u8) || (c == 69u8)) { st = 2i32; continue; }   // 'e' / 'E'
        if (c == 45u8) { negex = true; continue; }        // '-'
        if (c == 43u8) { continue; }                      // '+'
        if ((c < 48u8) || (c > 57u8)) { continue; }
        if (st == 2i32) { ex = ex * 10i64 + ((c - 48u8) => int64); continue; }
        if (st == 1i32) { frac = frac + 1i64; }
        if ((digits.len == 0i64) && (c == 48u8)) { continue; }   // leading zeros
        digits = string_concat(digits, raw slice_proven(txt, i, i + 1i64));
    }
    if (digits.len == 0i64) { digits = "0"; }
    if (negex) { ex = 0i64 - ex; }
    int64:scale = ex - frac;
    if (scale == 0i64) { pass (string_concat(digits, ".0")); }
    string:p = "1";
    int64:mag = scale;
    if (mag < 0i64) { mag = 0i64 - mag; }
    for (int64:z in 0i64...mag) { p = string_concat(p, "0"); }
    if (scale > 0i64) { pass (raw smt_app2("*", string_concat(digits, ".0"), string_concat(p, ".0"))); }
    pass (raw smt_app2("/", string_concat(digits, ".0"), string_concat(p, ".0")));
};

// A float value, named and recorded.
func:fp_make = Term(Encoder->:e, string:op, int32:ty, string:a, string:b, string:text,
                    List<int32>:syms) never fails {
    e.uses_fp = true;
    Term:raw_t = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: string_concat(text, ""),
                       syms: raw syms_union(syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    Term:nm = raw term_name(e, raw_t, raw fp_sort(e, ty));
    if (!nm.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    FpDef:d = FpDef{ sym: string_concat(nm.text, ""), op: string_concat(op, ""),
                     a: string_concat(a, ""), b: string_concat(b, ""), ty: ty };
    drop list_push(@e.fpdefs, move(d));
    pass nm;
};

func:fp_literal = Term(Encoder->:e, string:txt, int32:ty) never fails {
    string:r = raw decimal_to_real(txt);
    List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    string:d64 = raw smt_app1("(_ to_fp 11 53) RNE", r);
    if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) == 64i32) { pass (raw fp_make(e, "lit", ty, r, "", d64, none)); }
    // `flt32`: the emitter parses a double and truncates it (D-143).
    int32:t64 = raw tt_float(e.types, 64i32);
    Term:wide = raw fp_make(e, "lit", t64, r, "", d64, none);
    if (!wide.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass (raw fp_make(e, "narrow", ty, wide.text, "", raw smt_app1("(_ to_fp 8 24) RNE", wide.text), wide.syms));
};

func:enc_float_binary = Term(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:lt, int32:ty, Term:a, Term:b) never fails {
    Term:ta = raw term_copy(a);
    Term:tb = raw term_copy(b);
    if (!ta.ok) { ta = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
    if (!(ta.ok && tb.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    if (ta.is_bool || tb.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    e.uses_fp = true;
    if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("fp.eq", ta, tb, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_not(raw term_app2("fp.eq", ta, tb, true))); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpLt)    { pass (raw term_app2("fp.lt", ta, tb, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpLtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("fp.leq", ta, tb, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpGt)    { pass (raw term_app2("fp.gt", ta, tb, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpGtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("fp.geq", ta, tb, true)); }
    string:fop = "";
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlus)  { fop = "add"; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) { fop = "sub"; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStar)  { fop = "mul"; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { fop = "div"; }
    if (fop.len == 0i64) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    string:text = raw smt_app3(string_concat("fp.", fop), "RNE", ta.text, tb.text);
    pass (raw fp_make(e, fop, lt, ta.text, tb.text, text, raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms)));
};

// A CAST TOUCHING A FLOAT: `term_none` when it is not one of the three
// shapes with a term.
func:float_cast = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:t, int32:from, int32:to) never fails {
    if ((from == 0i32) || (to == 0i32)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    bool:ff = raw is_float(e, from);
    bool:ft = raw is_float(e, to);
    if (!(ff || ft)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:a = raw term_copy(t);
    if (!(a.ok && (!a.is_bool))) {
        a = raw term_none();
        if (raw is_termed(e, from)) { a = raw term_opaque(e, from); }
    }
    if (!a.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:head = string_concat("(_ to_fp ", raw fp_eb_sb(e, to));
    head = string_concat(head, ") RNE");
    if (ff && ft) {
        int32:sb = raw type_int_bits(e.types, from);
        int32:db = raw type_int_bits(e.types, to);
        if (sb == db) { pass a; }
        string:op = "widen";
        if (db < sb) { op = "narrow"; }
        pass (raw fp_make(e, op, to, a.text, "", raw smt_app1(head, a.text), a.syms));
    }
    if (ft && (raw is_word(e, from))) {
        pass (raw fp_make(e, "int", to, a.text, "", raw smt_app1(head, raw smt_app1("to_real", a.text)), a.syms));
    }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// --- floats, tier 2: the Real-interval abstraction (D-281, 1.5.4b step 3) ----------------
//
// D-218 (5) verbatim: "Real-interval abstraction for heavy non-linear ...
// undischarged = retained runtime guard". For every encoded row whose tier
// is `fp` the encoder ALSO writes a twin query into `NNNN.t2.smt2` -- the
// runner asks it only when tier 1 answered `unknown`, and only `unsat` there
// discharges (tier `real`). In the twin every float is a Real: an input
// symbol is a free Real; a NAMED operation (`fpdefs`) is a fresh Real `r`
// with the axiom `|r - v| <= eps*|v| + eta`, `v` the exact Real of the
// operation over its operands' Reals -- the standard model of a correctly
// rounded operation, `eps = 2^-53` / `2^-24`, `eta = 2^-1074` / `2^-149`
// covering the subnormals; a `fp.sqrt` is `r >= 0` and `r^2` within
// `v*(1 -+ eps)^2`; a negation and a widening are exact; a comparison is the
// Real comparison. THREE CONDITIONS make it sound, checked here, and no
// twin is written where one fails: (i) every float symbol in the cone that
// no hypothesis DEFINES is bounded below AND above by hypotheses that are
// float comparisons against literals (a `limit` rule, a `requires` clause,
// a path condition) -- such a hypothesis is false for NaN and, with both
// bounds, for the infinities, so the abstraction's "inputs are finite
// reals" premise is the hypotheses' own; (ii) every operation's magnitude
// is within the normal range -- `|v| <= MAX_NORMAL` per operation, a
// divisor nonzero, a square root's argument non-negative -- CONJOINED TO
// THE GOAL, so an `unsat` proves no overflow, no infinity and no NaN arise
// along with the property; (iii) the goal is a comparison or a Boolean
// combination of comparisons, the fragment the translation preserves (an
// `fp.eq`, with its NaN reading, stays tier 1 only). A negated comparison
// is not a bound (it holds of NaN); an uninterpreted function in the cone
// excludes the row (its float sorts have no Real twin).

// A small s-expression reader over the encoder's own texts: atoms (quoted
// symbols read to their closing bar) and lists, flat in two tables.
struct:SxNode = { bool:atom; string:text; int64:kid0; int64:nkids; };
pub struct:SxP = { string:s; int64:pos; List<SxNode>:nodes; List<int64>:kids; };

func:sxp_init = SxP(string:s) never fails {
    pass SxP{ s: string_concat(s, ""), pos: 0i64,
              nodes: raw list_init::<SxNode>(16i64), kids: raw list_init::<int64>(16i64) };
};

func:sx_skip = NIL(SxP->:p) never fails {
    while (p.pos < p.s.len) decreases p.s.len - p.pos {
        if (p.s.ptr[p.pos] != 32u8) { break; }
        p.pos = p.pos + 1i64;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Parse the node at the cursor; its index, or -1 at the end of the text.
func:sx_node = int64(SxP->:p) never fails {
    drop sx_skip(p);
    if (p.pos >= p.s.len) { pass (0i64 - 1i64); }
    uint8:c = p.s.ptr[p.pos];
    if (c == 40u8) {
        p.pos = p.pos + 1i64;
        List<int64>:mine = raw list_init::<int64>(4i64);
        bool:go = true;
        while (go) decreases p.s.len - p.pos {
            drop sx_skip(p);
            if (p.pos >= p.s.len) { go = false; continue; }
            if (p.s.ptr[p.pos] == 41u8) { p.pos = p.pos + 1i64; go = false; continue; }
            int64:k = raw sx_node(p);
            if (k < 0i64) { go = false; continue; }
            drop list_push(@mine, k);
        }
        int64:k0 = p.kids.count;
        for (int64:i in 0i64...mine.count) { drop list_push(@p.kids, mine[i]); }
        drop list_push(@p.nodes, SxNode{ atom: false, text: "", kid0: k0, nkids: mine.count });
        pass (p.nodes.count - 1i64);
    }
    int64:start = p.pos;
    if (c == 124u8) {
        p.pos = p.pos + 1i64;
        bool:go2 = true;
        while (go2) decreases p.s.len - p.pos {
            if (p.pos >= p.s.len) { go2 = false; continue; }
            uint8:d = p.s.ptr[p.pos];
            p.pos = p.pos + 1i64;
            if (d == 124u8) { go2 = false; }
        }
    } else {
        while (p.pos < p.s.len) decreases p.s.len - p.pos {
            uint8:d2 = p.s.ptr[p.pos];
            if ((d2 == 32u8) || (d2 == 40u8) || (d2 == 41u8)) { break; }
            p.pos = p.pos + 1i64;
        }
    }
    drop list_push(@p.nodes, SxNode{ atom: true, text: raw slice_proven(p.s, start, p.pos), kid0: 0i64, nkids: 0i64 });
    pass (p.nodes.count - 1i64);
};

func:sx_kid = int64(SxP:p, int64:k, int64:i) never fails {
    pass p.kids[p.nodes[k].kid0 + i];
};

func:sx_is = bool(SxP:p, int64:k, string:text) never fails {
    if (k < 0i64) { pass false; }
    if (!p.nodes[k].atom) { pass false; }
    pass (string_equals(p.nodes[k].text, text));
};

func:sx_text = string(SxP:p, int64:k) never fails {
    pass (string_concat(p.nodes[k].text, ""));
};

// The head of a list node as an atom text, or "" for an atom or a list head.
func:sx_head = string(SxP:p, int64:k) never fails {
    if (p.nodes[k].atom) { pass ""; }
    if (p.nodes[k].nkids == 0i64) { pass ""; }
    int64:h = raw sx_kid(p, k, 0i64);
    if (!p.nodes[h].atom) { pass ""; }
    pass (raw sx_text(p, h));
};

// The float definition a symbol text names, as its index in `fpdefs`, or -1.
func:fpdef_of = int64(Encoder->:e, string:sym) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.fpdefs.count) {
        if (string_equals(e.fpdefs[i].sym, sym)) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

func:fpsym_is = bool(Encoder->:e, string:text) never fails {
    int32:si = raw sym_find(e, text);
    if (si < 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass (e.syms[si => int64].fsort.len > 0i64);
};

// The error model's constants per width: eps, eta, MAX_NORMAL as Reals.
func:t2_eps = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) == 32i32) { pass "(/ 1.0 16777216.0)"; }
    pass "(/ 1.0 9007199254740992.0)";
};
func:t2_eta = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) == 32i32) { pass (raw smt_app2("/", "1.0", string_concat(raw pow2_decimal(149i64), ".0"))); }
    pass (raw smt_app2("/", "1.0", string_concat(raw pow2_decimal(1074i64), ".0")));
};
func:t2_maxn = string(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, ty)) == 32i32) { pass (raw smt_app2("*", string_concat(raw pow2_decimal(104i64), ".0"), "16777215.0")); }
    pass (raw smt_app2("*", string_concat(raw pow2_decimal(971i64), ".0"), "9007199254740991.0"));
};

// The translation's state for one row: the side conditions gathered from
// the definitions, and whether every text was in the fragment.
struct:T2 = { bool:ok; List<string>:sides; };

// A term's Real twin: the float comparisons and operations to their Real
// forms, `to_fp` to its argument, everything else verbatim over its twins.
func:t2_term = string(Encoder->:e, SxP:p, T2->:t, int64:k) never fails {
    if (p.nodes[k].atom) { pass (raw sx_text(p, k)); }
    int64:nk = p.nodes[k].nkids;
    if (nk == 0i64) { pass "()"; }
    int64:h = raw sx_kid(p, k, 0i64);
    if (!p.nodes[h].atom) {
        // ((_ to_fp E S) RNE X): the argument's own Real.
        if ((raw sx_is(p, raw sx_kid(p, h, 0i64), "_")) && (raw sx_is(p, raw sx_kid(p, h, 1i64), "to_fp")) && (nk == 3i64)) {
            pass (raw t2_term(e, p, t, raw sx_kid(p, k, 2i64)));
        }
        t.ok = false;
        pass "false";
    }
    string:head = raw sx_text(p, h);
    string:nh = string_concat(head, "");
    int64:from = 1i64;
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.lt"))  { nh = "<"; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.leq")) { nh = "<="; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.gt"))  { nh = ">"; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.geq")) { nh = ">="; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.eq"))  { nh = "="; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.add")) { nh = "+"; from = 2i64; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.sub")) { nh = "-"; from = 2i64; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.mul")) { nh = "*"; from = 2i64; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.div")) { nh = "/"; from = 2i64; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.neg")) { nh = "-"; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.sqrt")) { t.ok = false; pass "false"; }
    if (string_equals(head, "fp.isNaN")) { t.ok = false; pass "false"; }
    string:out = string_concat("(", nh);
    for (int64:i in from...nk) {
        out = string_concat(out, " ");
        out = string_concat(out, raw t2_term(e, p, t, raw sx_kid(p, k, i)));
    }
    pass (string_concat(out, ")"));
};

// A hypothesis's twin: a float DEFINITION `(= SYM rhs)` becomes the error
// model's axiom (and its side conditions), anything else its Real twin.
func:t2_hyp = string(Encoder->:e, T2->:t, string:text) never fails {
    SxP:p = raw sxp_init(text);
    int64:root = raw sx_node(@p);
    if (root < 0i64) { t.ok = false; pass "false"; }
    if ((raw sx_head(p, root)).len > 0i64) {
        if ((raw sx_is(p, raw sx_kid(p, root, 0i64), "=")) && (p.nodes[root].nkids == 3i64)) {
            int64:sk = raw sx_kid(p, root, 1i64);
            if (p.nodes[sk].atom) {
                string:sym = raw sx_text(p, sk);
                if (raw fpsym_is(e, sym)) {
                    int64:rhs = raw sx_kid(p, root, 2i64);
                    int64:di = raw fpdef_of(e, sym);
                    if (di < 0i64) {
                        pass (raw smt_app2("=", sym, raw t2_term(e, p, t, rhs)));
                    }
                    string:op = string_concat(e.fpdefs[di].op, "");
                    int32:ty = e.fpdefs[di].ty;
                    if ((string_equals(op, "neg")) || (string_equals(op, "widen"))) {
                        pass (raw smt_app2("=", sym, raw t2_term(e, p, t, rhs)));
                    }
                    string:eps = raw t2_eps(e, ty);
                    if (string_equals(op, "sqrt")) {
                        // (fp.sqrt RNE X): X is kid 2
                        string:v = raw t2_term(e, p, t, raw sx_kid(p, rhs, 2i64));
                        drop list_push(@t.sides, raw smt_app2(">=", v, "0.0"));
                        string:km = raw smt_app2("*", raw smt_app2("-", "1.0", eps), raw smt_app2("-", "1.0", eps));
                        string:kp = raw smt_app2("*", raw smt_app2("+", "1.0", eps), raw smt_app2("+", "1.0", eps));
                        string:sq = raw smt_app2("*", sym, sym);
                        pass (raw smt_app3("and", raw smt_app2(">=", sym, "0.0"),
                                           raw smt_app2(">=", sq, raw smt_app2("*", v, km)),
                                           raw smt_app2("<=", sq, raw smt_app2("*", v, kp))));
                    }
                    string:v2 = raw t2_term(e, p, t, rhs);
                    drop list_push(@t.sides, raw smt_app2("<=", raw smt_app1("absr", v2), raw t2_maxn(e, ty)));
                    if (string_equals(op, "div")) {
                        string:b = raw t2_term(e, p, t, raw sx_kid(p, rhs, 3i64));
                        drop list_push(@t.sides, raw smt_app2("distinct", b, "0.0"));
                    }
                    string:err = raw smt_app1("absr", raw smt_app2("-", sym, v2));
                    string:bound = raw smt_app2("+", raw smt_app2("*", eps, raw smt_app1("absr", v2)), raw t2_eta(e, ty));
                    pass (raw smt_app2("<=", err, bound));
                }
            }
        }
    }
    pass (raw t2_term(e, p, t, root));
};

// (iii): comparisons and their Boolean combinations, over symbols and the
// Int fragment; no `fp.eq`, no predicate on NaN, no raw float operation.
func:t2_goal_ok = bool(Encoder->:e, SxP:p, int64:k) never fails {
    if (p.nodes[k].atom) { pass true; }
    string:h = raw sx_head(p, k);
    if (h.len == 0i64) { pass false; }
    bool:known = false;
    if (string_equals(h, "fp.lt") || string_equals(h, "fp.leq") || string_equals(h, "fp.gt") || string_equals(h, "fp.geq")) { known = true; }
    if (string_equals(h, "and") || string_equals(h, "or") || string_equals(h, "not") || string_equals(h, "ite")) { known = true; }
    if (string_equals(h, "<") || string_equals(h, "<=") || string_equals(h, ">") || string_equals(h, ">=")) { known = true; }
    if (string_equals(h, "+") || string_equals(h, "-") || string_equals(h, "*") || string_equals(h, "div") || string_equals(h, "mod")) { known = true; }
    if (string_equals(h, "npk_sdiv") || string_equals(h, "npk_srem") || string_equals(h, "to_real")) { known = true; }
    if (string_equals(h, "=") || string_equals(h, "distinct")) {
        known = true;
        for (int64:i in 1i64...p.nodes[k].nkids) {
            int64:c = raw sx_kid(p, k, i);
            if (p.nodes[c].atom) { if (raw fpsym_is(e, raw sx_text(p, c))) { pass false; } }
        }
    }
    if (!known) { pass false; }
    for (int64:i2 in 1i64...p.nodes[k].nkids) {
        if (!(raw t2_goal_ok(e, p, raw sx_kid(p, k, i2)))) { pass false; }
    }
    pass true;
};

// (i): the bounds of an undefined float symbol among a hypothesis's
// top-level conjuncts -- `lo`/`hi` set where a comparison against a
// literal-defined symbol bounds it from that side.
func:t2_bounds_in = int32(Encoder->:e, SxP:p, int64:k, string:sym) never fails {
    string:h = raw sx_head(p, k);
    if (h.len == 0i64) { pass 0i32; }
    if (string_equals(h, "and")) {
        int32:acc = 0i32;
        for (int64:i in 1i64...p.nodes[k].nkids) { acc = acc | (raw t2_bounds_in(e, p, raw sx_kid(p, k, i), sym)); }
        pass acc;
    }
    if (p.nodes[k].nkids != 3i64) { pass 0i32; }
    int64:a = raw sx_kid(p, k, 1i64);
    int64:b = raw sx_kid(p, k, 2i64);
    if (!(p.nodes[a].atom && p.nodes[b].atom)) { pass 0i32; }
    bool:ge = (string_equals(h, "fp.geq")) || (string_equals(h, "fp.gt"));
    bool:le = (string_equals(h, "fp.leq")) || (string_equals(h, "fp.lt"));
    if (!(ge || le)) { pass 0i32; }
    bool:a_sym = raw sx_is(p, a, sym);
    bool:b_sym = raw sx_is(p, b, sym);
    int64:da = raw fpdef_of(e, raw sx_text(p, a));
    int64:db = raw fpdef_of(e, raw sx_text(p, b));
    bool:a_lit = false;
    bool:b_lit = false;
    if (da >= 0i64) { a_lit = string_equals(e.fpdefs[da].op, "lit"); }
    if (db >= 0i64) { b_lit = string_equals(e.fpdefs[db].op, "lit"); }
    int32:m = 0i32;
    if (a_sym && b_lit) { if (ge) { m = m | 1i32; } else { m = m | 2i32; } }
    if (b_sym && a_lit) { if (ge) { m = m | 2i32; } else { m = m | 1i32; } }
    pass m;
};

// The twin file for this function -- "" when no row qualifies; `ks` the
// 1-based ordinals of the rows it decides, in file order.
pub func:enc_t2_text = string(Encoder->:e, List<int64>->:ks) never fails {
    List<string>:blocks = raw list_init::<string>(4i64);
    List<int32>:decl = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if (!e.obls[oi].encoded) { continue; }
        if (!(string_equals(e.obls[oi].tier, "fp"))) { continue; }
        // (iii) the goal's shape
        SxP:gp = raw sxp_init(e.obls[oi].goal);
        int64:groot = raw sx_node(@gp);
        if (groot < 0i64) { continue; }
        if (!(raw t2_goal_ok(e, gp, groot))) { continue; }
        // the cone's hypotheses, parsed once
        List<SxP>:hp = raw list_init::<SxP>(8i64);
        List<int64>:hr = raw list_init::<int64>(8i64);
        for (int64:hi in 0i64...e.obls[oi].cone_hyps.count) {
            SxP:one = raw sxp_init(e.hyps[e.obls[oi].cone_hyps[hi] => int64].text);
            int64:r1 = raw sx_node(@one);
            drop list_push(@hr, r1);
            drop list_push(@hp, move(one));
        }
        // (i) every float symbol defined or bounded; no uninterpreted function
        bool:elig = true;
        for (int64:ci in 0i64...e.obls[oi].cone_syms.count) {
            int32:si = e.obls[oi].cone_syms[ci];
            if (e.syms[si => int64].sorts.len > 0i64) { elig = false; }
            if (e.syms[si => int64].fsort.len == 0i64) { continue; }
            string:st = raw sym_text(e, si);
            bool:defined = false;
            int32:bm = 0i32;
            for (int64:hj in 0i64...hp.count) {
                int64:root = hr[hj];
                if (root < 0i64) { continue; }
                if ((raw sx_is(hp[hj], raw sx_kid(hp[hj], root, 0i64), "=")) && (hp[hj].nodes[root].nkids == 3i64)) {
                    if (raw sx_is(hp[hj], raw sx_kid(hp[hj], root, 1i64), st)) { defined = true; }
                }
                bm = bm | (raw t2_bounds_in(e, hp[hj], root, st));
            }
            if (!(defined || (bm == 3i32))) { elig = false; }
        }
        if (!elig) { continue; }
        // the translation
        T2:t = T2{ ok: true, sides: raw list_init::<string>(4i64) };
        SmtBuf:blk = raw smtbuf_init();
        drop smtbuf_line(@blk, "(push)");
        for (int64:hk in 0i64...e.obls[oi].cone_hyps.count) {
            string:tw = raw t2_hyp(e, @t, e.hyps[e.obls[oi].cone_hyps[hk] => int64].text);
            if (!t.ok) { break; }
            drop smtbuf_line(@blk, raw smt_app1("assert", tw));
        }
        if (!t.ok) { continue; }
        string:goal_r = raw t2_term(e, gp, @t, groot);
        if (!t.ok) { continue; }
        string:conj = string_concat(goal_r, "");
        for (int64:sd in 0i64...t.sides.count) { conj = raw smt_app2("and", raw strlist_view_enc(t.sides, sd), conj); }
        drop smtbuf_line(@blk, raw smt_app1("assert", raw smt_app1("not", conj)));
        drop smtbuf_line(@blk, "(check-sat)");
        drop smtbuf_line(@blk, "(pop)");
        drop list_push(@blocks, raw smtbuf_text(move(blk)));
        drop list_push(ks, oi + 1i64);
        for (int64:ci2 in 0i64...e.obls[oi].cone_syms.count) {
            int32:s2 = e.obls[oi].cone_syms[ci2];
            if (!(raw has_sym(decl, s2))) { drop list_push(@decl, s2); }
        }
    }
    if (blocks.count == 0i64) { pass ""; }
    SmtBuf:out = raw smtbuf_init();
    drop smtbuf_line(@out, string_concat("; t2 ", e.symbol));
    drop smtbuf_line(@out, "(set-logic ALL)");
    drop smtbuf_line(@out, "(define-fun absr ((t Real)) Real (ite (>= t 0.0) t (- t)))");
    for (int64:si2 in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
        if (!(raw has_sym(decl, si2 =>! int32))) { continue; }
        if (e.syms[si2].fsort.len > 0i64) {
            drop smtbuf_line(@out, raw smt_app2("declare-const", raw sym_text(e, si2 =>! int32), "Real"));
        } else {
            drop smtbuf_line(@out, raw sym_declaration(e, si2 =>! int32));
        }
    }
    string:text = raw smtbuf_text(move(out));
    for (int64:bi in 0i64...blocks.count) { text = string_concat(text, raw strlist_view_enc(blocks, bi)); }
    pass text;
};

// A list element viewed without a copy (the string's bytes, borrowed).
func:strlist_view_enc = string(List<string>:l, int64:i) never fails {
    pass (string_from_bytes(l[i].ptr, l[i].len));
};

// --- bitwise operations: the Int forms and the bounded crossing (D-279, D-280) ------------

// A NUMERAL A TERM OR AN EXPRESSION KNOWS: the term's digits when it is a
// plain numeral that fits, else the folder's value for the expression (a
// `fixed` constant, a folded literal). `ok` false when neither knows.
struct:NumVal = { bool:ok; int64:v; };

func:numeral_of = NumVal(Encoder->:e, Term:t, ExprId:x) never fails {
    if (t.ok && (raw term_is_numeral(t)) && (t.text.len <= 18i64)) {
        int64:v = 0i64;
        for (int64:i in 0i64...t.text.len) { v = v * 10i64 + ((t.text.ptr[i] - 48u8) => int64); }
        pass NumVal{ ok: true, v: v };
    }
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(x))) {
        ConstVal:cv = raw fold_const(e.tr, x, e.scope);
        if (cv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) { pass NumVal{ ok: true, v: cv.num }; }
    }
    pass NumVal{ ok: false, v: 0i64 };
};

// Is `v` exactly 2^j for some 0 <= j < bits? The exponent, or -1.
func:pow2_exp = int32(int64:v, int32:bits) never fails {
    if (v <= 0i64) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
    int64:p = 1i64;
    for (int32:j in 0i32...bits) {
        if (p == v) { pass j; }
        if (j >= 62i32) { pass (0i32 - 1i32); }
        p = p * 2i64;
    }
    pass (0i32 - 1i32);
};

// A SHIFT BY A NUMERAL, IN Int (D-279): `x << k` is the product taken modulo
// 2^W -- and, for a signed word, re-signed: the wrap the machine's `shl`
// performs (measured 1,287 rlimit at 64 bits); `x >> k` is `(div x 2^k)`,
// which SMT-LIB defines as floor division by a positive numeral -- `ashr`
// on a signed value, `lshr` on an unsigned one. Any width: the numerals are
// text, and z3 decides these at a few hundred rlimit at 2048 bits.
func:int_form_shift = Term(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:ty, Term:a, int64:k) never fails {
    int32:wb = raw word_bits(e, ty);
    string:p = raw pow2_decimal(k);
    if (op == TokenKind.OpShr) { pass (raw term_app2("div", a, raw term_lit(move(p), false), false)); }
    Term:prod = raw term_app2("*", a, raw term_lit(move(p), false), false);
    pass (raw wrap_to_word(e, ty, prod));
};

// A TERM BROUGHT INTO ITS WORD, EXACTLY (D-279's `<<` form, and D-312's
// wrapping family since 1.5.8b step 4): `(mod t 2^N)` for an unsigned word,
// and the two's-complement reading for a signed one -- the value at or past
// 2^(N-1) is that value less 2^N. The term is captured first, so the `ite`
// names it twice and writes it once.
func:wrap_to_word = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:t) never fails {
    if (!t.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    int32:wb = raw word_bits(e, ty);
    Term:wrapped = raw term_app2("mod", t, raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(wb => int64), false), false);
    if (!(raw word_signed(e, ty))) { pass wrapped; }
    Term:s = raw term_capture(e, ty, wrapped);
    if (!s.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:half = raw pow2_decimal((wb => int64) - 1i64);
    string:full = raw pow2_decimal(wb => int64);
    string:txt = raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(">=", s.text, half),
                              raw smt_app2("-", s.text, full), s.text);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(txt), syms: raw syms_union(s.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
};

// `a op% b` AS A TERM (D-312, 1.5.8b step 4): the operation, brought into the
// word. No row and no guard: the operator's meaning IS the wrap, so there is
// nothing to prove and nothing to elide.
func:wrap_binop = Term(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:ty, Term:a, Term:b) never fails {
    if (!(a.ok && b.ok)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (a.is_bool || b.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:raw_t = raw term_none();
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlusWrap)  { raw_t = raw term_app2("+", a, b, false); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinusWrap) { raw_t = raw term_app2("-", a, b, false); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStarWrap) {
        if (!((raw term_is_numeral(a)) || (raw term_is_numeral(b)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        raw_t = raw term_app2("*", a, b, false);
    }
    pass (raw wrap_to_word(e, ty, raw_t));
};

// `x & m` WITH A NUMERAL MASK, IN Int (D-279) -- the three shapes the tree
// writes: the low bits (`2^j - 1` is `(mod x 2^j)`: two's-complement low bits
// ARE the non-negative residue), one bit (`2^j` is `(* (mod (div x 2^j) 2)
// 2^j)`), the low bits cleared (a signed `-(2^j)` or an unsigned `2^W - 2^j`
// is `(- x (mod x 2^j))`). Any other mask is the crossing's (`term_none`).
func:int_form_and = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:a, int64:m) never fails {
    int32:wb = raw word_bits(e, ty);
    if (m == 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("0", false)); }
    if (m > 0i64) {
        int32:j = raw pow2_exp(m + 1i64, wb + 1i32);
        if (j >= 0i32) {   // 2^j - 1
            pass (raw term_app2("mod", a, raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(j => int64), false), false));
        }
        int32:jb = raw pow2_exp(m, wb);
        if (jb >= 0i32) {  // 2^jb
            string:pj = raw pow2_decimal(jb => int64);
            Term:q = raw term_app2("div", a, raw term_lit(string_concat(pj, ""), false), false);
            Term:bit = raw term_app2("mod", q, raw term_lit("2", false), false);
            pass (raw term_app2("*", bit, raw term_lit(move(pj), false), false));
        }
        if (!(raw word_signed(e, ty))) {
            if (wb <= 62i32) {   // 2^W - 2^j, only where the value fits the folder's int64
                int64:full = 1i64;
                for (int32:i in 0i32...wb) { full = full * 2i64; }
                int32:jc = raw pow2_exp(full - m, wb);
                if (jc >= 0i32) {
                    Term:low = raw term_app2("mod", a, raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(jc => int64), false), false);
                    pass (raw term_app2("-", a, low, false));
                }
            }
        }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if (raw word_signed(e, ty)) {
        int32:jn = raw pow2_exp(0i64 - m, wb);   // -(2^jn): the low jn bits cleared
        if (jn >= 0i32) {
            Term:low2 = raw term_app2("mod", a, raw term_lit(raw pow2_decimal(jn => int64), false), false);
            pass (raw term_app2("-", a, low2, false));
        }
    }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// THE CROSSING (D-218 (4), D-280): both operands into bit-vectors of the
// word's width, the operation there, the result back as a natural and
// re-signed for a signed word -- `int2bv` of a negative Int is its
// two's-complement pattern by SMT-LIB's definition, so the crossing is
// exact. `term_none` above `BV_CROSS_MAX_BITS`. The result is captured in a
// fresh symbol so the re-sign names it once.
func:cross_bin = Term(Encoder->:e, string:bvop, int32:ty, Term:a, Term:b) never fails {
    int32:wb = raw word_bits(e, ty);
    if (wb > (raw BV_CROSS_MAX_BITS())) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:wtxt = int_to_string(wb => int64);
    string:tobv = string_concat(string_concat("(_ int2bv ", wtxt), ")");
    string:inner = raw smt_app2(bvop, raw smt_app1(string_concat(tobv, ""), a.text),
                                raw smt_app1(string_concat(tobv, ""), b.text));
    Term:nat = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app1("bv2nat", inner),
                     syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, b.syms) };
    e.uses_bv = true;
    Term:r = raw term_capture(e, ty, nat);
    if (!r.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (!(raw word_signed(e, ty))) { pass r; }
    string:half = raw pow2_decimal((wb => int64) - 1i64);
    string:full = raw pow2_decimal(wb => int64);
    string:txt = raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(">=", r.text, half),
                              raw smt_app2("-", r.text, full), r.text);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(txt), syms: raw syms_union(r.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
};

// EVERY BITWISE OPERATION IS ENCODED (D-279): a shift records its row first
// (D-277); then a numeral amount or a numeral mask takes the Int form, and
// the rest the crossing, opaque only above its width. `a`/`b` may be
// unencodable (a call's value): an opaque operand still crosses -- an opaque
// symbol has a range axiom, which is what a crossing needs.
func:enc_bitwise = Term(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:ty, Term:a, Term:b,
                        ExprId:lhs, ExprId:rhs, int32:site, Span:at, bool:rows) never fails {
    Term:ta = raw term_copy(a);
    Term:tb = raw term_copy(b);
    if (!ta.ok) { ta = raw term_opaque(e, ty); }
    if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, ty); }
    if (!(ta.ok && tb.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    if (ta.is_bool || tb.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpShl) || (op == TokenKind.OpShr)) {
        if (rows) { drop record_shift(e, ty, tb, rhs, site, at); }
        NumVal:k = raw numeral_of(e, tb, rhs);
        if (k.ok && (k.v >= 0i64) && (k.v < ((raw word_bits(e, ty)) => int64))) {
            Term:f = raw int_form_shift(e, op, ty, ta, k.v);
            if (f.ok) { pass f; }
        }
        string:bvs = "bvshl";
        if (op == TokenKind.OpShr) { bvs = "bvlshr"; if (raw word_signed(e, ty)) { bvs = "bvashr"; } }
        Term:c = raw cross_bin(e, bvs, ty, ta, tb);
        if (c.ok) { pass c; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpAmp) {
        NumVal:mb = raw numeral_of(e, tb, rhs);
        if (mb.ok) { Term:f1 = raw int_form_and(e, ty, ta, mb.v); if (f1.ok) { pass f1; } }
        NumVal:ma = raw numeral_of(e, ta, lhs);
        if (ma.ok) { Term:f2 = raw int_form_and(e, ty, tb, ma.v); if (f2.ok) { pass f2; } }
        Term:c1 = raw cross_bin(e, "bvand", ty, ta, tb);
        if (c1.ok) { pass c1; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    string:bvo = "bvor";
    if (op == TokenKind.OpCaret) { bvo = "bvxor"; }
    Term:c2 = raw cross_bin(e, bvo, ty, ta, tb);
    if (c2.ok) { pass c2; }
    pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
};

// A FLAG WORD AND ITS `int32` CARRIER (D-230, 1.5.4b step 1): one 32-bit
// pattern. Into the word: a negative int reads as `i + 2^32`; out of it: a
// word at or past 2^31 reads as `f - 2^32`. Anything else is not this cast.
func:flag_word_cast = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:t, int32:from, int32:to) never fails {
    if (!(t.ok && (!t.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if ((from == 0i32) || (to == 0i32)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    bool:from_flags = ((raw type_kind(e.types, from)) == (raw TY_FLAGS()));
    bool:to_flags = ((raw type_kind(e.types, to)) == (raw TY_FLAGS()));
    bool:from_i32 = (raw is_int(e, from)) && ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, from)) == 32i32);
    bool:to_i32 = (raw is_int(e, to)) && ((raw type_int_bits(e.types, to)) == 32i32);
    if (from_i32 && to_flags) {
        if (!(raw type_is_signed(e.types, from))) { pass (raw term_copy(t)); }
        string:up = raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2("<", t.text, "0"),
                                 raw smt_app2("+", t.text, "4294967296"), t.text);
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(up), syms: raw syms_union(t.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    }
    if (from_flags && to_i32) {
        if (!(raw type_is_signed(e.types, to))) { pass (raw term_copy(t)); }
        string:down = raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2(">=", t.text, "2147483648"),
                                   raw smt_app2("-", t.text, "4294967296"), t.text);
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(down), syms: raw syms_union(t.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// --- `simd` lanes (D-282, 1.5.4b step 4) --------------------------------------------------
//
// A `simd<T, N>` EXPRESSION'S VALUE IS N SCALAR TERMS, kept in a side table
// by expression (`lane_tab`) and built by the walk: the constructor's
// arguments (a splat's one term N times), an elementwise operation
// lane-wise under the scalar rule of the element's kind (a word's
// arithmetic, bitwise and compares; a float's IEEE operations; a `bool`
// lane's `==`/`!=`/`&`/`|`/`^`), `[i]` with a numeral index the lane's
// term, `.len` the count, `.any()`/`.all()` the disjunction/conjunction, the
// ordered reductions folded in the emitter's order (`sum` left to right;
// `min`/`max` as its `select` over the strict compare -- `fcmp olt`/`ogt`
// for floats, false on NaN, so a NaN lane is passed over as the machine
// does), an elementwise cast the scalar cast per lane; anything else -- a
// local's read, a call's value, a computed index -- N opaque lanes of the
// element type (D-282 as ratified: lanes ride expressions, not bindings).
// The vector itself has no scalar term. THE ROWS: a `simd` division's
// any-lane guard is ONE `div-zero` row over the conjunction of the lanes'
// conditions and, for a signed element, one `div-min` row likewise; a
// `simd` shift's any-lane guard one `shift-range` row over its conjunction
// -- the emitter's one trap per site, one group -- and its fact a hypothesis
// as a scalar shift's is. The `unencoded` producers of 1.5.0 and step 0
// (`record_unencoded_division`, `record_unencoded_shift`) retire here.

func:lanes_find = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:id) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.lane_tab.count) {
        if (e.lane_tab[i].id == id) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

// The lanes of a `simd`-typed expression: the recorded ones, else N opaque
// lanes of the element type.
func:lanes_of = List<Term>(Encoder->:e, ExprId:x, int32:vt) never fails {
    int32:n = (raw tt_get(e.types, vt)).b;
    int32:elem = raw type_elem(e.types, vt);
    List<Term>:out = raw list_init::<Term>((n => int64) + 1i64);
    int64:li = raw lanes_find(e, x.index);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        if (li >= 0i64) {
            if ((i => int64) < e.lane_tab[li].lanes.count) {
                drop list_push(@out, raw term_copy(e.lane_tab[li].lanes[i => int64]));
                continue;
            }
        }
        Term:o = raw term_opaque(e, elem);
        drop list_push(@out, move(o));
    }
    pass out;
};

func:lanes_put = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:id, move List<Term>:lanes) never fails {
    drop list_push(@e.lane_tab, LaneEntry{ id: id, lanes: move(lanes) });
    pass NIL;
};

func:is_simd = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ty == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass ((raw type_kind(e.types, ty)) == (raw TY_SIMD()));
};

// LANES THROUGH BINDINGS: a `simd` binding's lanes are N symbols of the
// element type (`|v#i.k|`, one version `k` per write), so a local's lanes
// flow from its initialiser through its reads -- defined at a declaration
// and an assignment from the written value's lanes, fresh and opaque at an
// invalidation, at a restore to an earlier state and at a merge (the
// conservative answer wherever the versions could differ by path).
func:lane_syms_new = List<int32>(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:ty) never fails {
    int32:n = (raw tt_get(e.types, ty)).b;
    int32:elem = raw type_elem(e.types, ty);
    int64:ver = raw version_next(e, name);
    List<int32>:out = raw list_init::<int32>((n => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        string:stem = string_concat(raw intern_get(e.interns, name), "#");
        stem = string_concat(stem, int_to_string(i => int64));
        drop list_push(@out, raw sym_new(e, raw smt_sym(stem, ver), elem));
    }
    pass out;
};

// The binding's lanes defined equal to a value's lanes, where known.
func:bind_lanes_from = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:bi, ExprId:src) never fails {
    if (e.binds[bi].lanes.count == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw expr_is_none(src)) { pass NIL; }
    List<Term>:sl = raw lanes_of(e, src, e.binds[bi].type_id);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds[bi].lanes.count) {
        if (i >= sl.count) { break; }
        if (!sl[i].ok) { continue; }
        int32:ls = e.binds[bi].lanes[i];
        if (sl[i].is_bool != e.syms[ls => int64].is_bool) { continue; }
        List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one, ls);
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", raw sym_text(e, ls), sl[i].text), raw syms_union(one, sl[i].syms));
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A write to a `simd` binding: a new version of every lane.
func:bind_lanes_assign = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, ExprId:src) never fails {
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (bi < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.binds[bi].lanes.count == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    e.binds[bi].lanes = raw lane_syms_new(e, name, e.binds[bi].type_id);
    drop bind_lanes_from(e, bi, src);
    pass NIL;
};

// Every `simd` binding's lanes fresh and opaque.
func:lanes_refresh_all = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds.count) {
        if (e.binds[i].lanes.count == 0i64) { continue; }
        e.binds[i].lanes = raw lane_syms_new(e, e.binds[i].name, e.binds[i].type_id);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A binding's lanes as terms, recorded for the read.
func:lanes_of_binding = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:bi, int32:id) never fails {
    List<Term>:out = raw list_init::<Term>(e.binds[bi].lanes.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.binds[bi].lanes.count) {
        int32:ls = e.binds[bi].lanes[i];
        List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop list_push(@one, ls);
        drop list_push(@out, Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms[ls => int64].is_bool, text: raw sym_text(e, ls), syms: move(one) });
    }
    drop lanes_put(e, id, move(out));
    pass NIL;
};

// One lane of an elementwise operation: the scalar rule, terms only (the
// any-lane guards' rows are recorded once, over every lane, by the caller).
func:lane_binop = Term(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:elem, Term:a, Term:b, Span:at) never fails {
    if (!(a.ok && b.ok)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    bool:cmp = raw tw_is_cmp(op);
    int32:rty = elem;
    if (cmp) { rty = e.types.t_bool; }
    if (raw is_float(e, elem)) { pass (raw enc_float_binary(e, op, elem, rty, a, b)); }
    if (raw is_bool(e, elem)) {
        if (!(a.is_bool && b.is_bool)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpAmp)   { pass (raw term_app2("and", a, b, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpPipe)  { pass (raw term_app2("or", a, b, true)); }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpCaret) { pass (raw term_app2("xor", a, b, true)); }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if (!(raw is_int(e, elem))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (a.is_bool || b.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    bool:bitop = ((op == TokenKind.OpAmp) || (op == TokenKind.OpPipe) || (op == TokenKind.OpCaret));
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpShl) || (op == TokenKind.OpShr)) { bitop = true; }
    if (bitop) {
        pass (raw enc_bitwise(e, op, elem, a, b, ExprId{ index: 0i32 }, ExprId{ index: 0i32 }, 0i32, at, false));
    }
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercent)) {
        if (!(raw term_is_numeral(b))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, elem)) {
            e.uses_sdiv = true;
            e.nonlinear = true;
            if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { pass (raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", a, b, false)); }
            pass (raw term_app2("npk_srem", a, b, false));
        }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { pass (raw term_app2("div", a, b, false)); }
        pass (raw term_app2("mod", a, b, false));
    }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlus)  { pass (raw term_app2("+", a, b, false)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) { pass (raw term_app2("-", a, b, false)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStar) {
        if (!((raw term_is_numeral(a)) || (raw term_is_numeral(b)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        pass (raw term_app2("*", a, b, false));
    }
    // The wrapping family on a lane (D-312): the operation inside the element's
    // word, and no any-lane row -- the lanes wrap by the operator's meaning.
    if (raw wrap_arith_op(op)) { pass (raw wrap_binop(e, op, elem, a, b)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpLt)    { pass (raw term_app2("<", a, b, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpLtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("<=", a, b, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpGt)    { pass (raw term_app2(">", a, b, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpGtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2(">=", a, b, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// The any-lane D-007 pair, ONE row each over every lane (the emitter's one
// trap per code at the site).
func:record_division_lanes = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:elem, List<Term>:la, List<Term>:lb,
                                 int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    string:zero = "";
    string:both = "";
    List<int32>:zs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    List<int32>:bs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    string:mn = raw smt_int_min(raw type_int_bits(e.types, elem));
    for (int64:i in 0i64...lb.count) {
        Term:tb = raw term_copy(lb[i]);
        Term:ta = raw term_copy(la[i]);
        if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, elem); }
        if (!ta.ok) { ta = raw term_opaque(e, elem); }
        string:z = raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, "0"));
        if (zero.len == 0i64) { zero = move(z); } else { zero = raw smt_app2("and", zero, z); }
        zs = raw syms_union(zs, tb.syms);
        string:pair = raw smt_app1("not", raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2("=", ta.text, mn), raw smt_app2("=", tb.text, "(- 1)")));
        if (both.len == 0i64) { both = move(pair); } else { both = raw smt_app2("and", both, pair); }
        bs = raw syms_union(bs, raw syms_union(ta.syms, tb.syms));
    }
    drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_ZERO(), zero, zs, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, zero, zs); }
    if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, elem)) {
        drop record(e, raw OK_DIV_MIN(), both, bs, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, both, bs); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The any-lane shift guard: one `shift-range` row over every lane's amount,
// and its fact a hypothesis as a scalar shift's (D-277).
func:record_shift_lanes = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:elem, List<Term>:lb, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    string:w = int_to_string((raw type_int_bits(e.types, elem)) => int64);
    string:goal = "";
    List<int32>:gs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...lb.count) {
        Term:tb = raw term_copy(lb[i]);
        if (!tb.ok) { tb = raw term_opaque(e, elem); }
        string:one = raw smt_app2("and", raw smt_app2(">=", tb.text, "0"), raw smt_app2("<", tb.text, w));
        if (goal.len == 0i64) { goal = move(one); } else { goal = raw smt_app2("and", goal, one); }
        gs = raw syms_union(gs, tb.syms);
    }
    drop record(e, raw OK_SHIFT_RANGE(), goal, gs, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, goal, gs); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, goal, gs);
    pass NIL;
};

// An elementwise operation on two vectors: the rows first, then the lanes.
func:enc_simd_binary = NIL(Encoder->:e, TokenKind:op, int32:vt, ExprId:id, ExprId:lhs, ExprId:rhs, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:elem = raw type_elem(e.types, vt);
    int32:n = (raw tt_get(e.types, vt)).b;
    int32:rvt = raw ty_of(e, rhs);
    if (!(raw is_simd(e, rvt))) { rvt = vt; }
    List<Term>:la = raw lanes_of(e, lhs, vt);
    List<Term>:lb = raw lanes_of(e, rhs, rvt);
    if (((op == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercent)) && (raw is_int(e, elem))) {
        drop record_division_lanes(e, elem, la, lb, id.index, at);
    }
    if (((op == TokenKind.OpShl) || (op == TokenKind.OpShr)) && (raw is_word(e, elem))) {
        drop record_shift_lanes(e, elem, lb, id.index, at);
    }
    // `+ - *` ON INTEGER LANES: the any-lane `overflow` row over the result
    // lanes (1.5.8b step 3), the emitter's one guard at the site.
    bool:lov = ((op == TokenKind.OpPlus) || (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) || (op == TokenKind.OpStar));
    if (lov && (raw is_int(e, elem))) {
        drop record_overflow_lanes(e, elem, raw overflow_out_lanes(e, op, elem, la, lb, at), id.index, at);
    }
    List<Term>:out = raw list_init::<Term>((n => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        if (((i => int64) < la.count) && ((i => int64) < lb.count)) {
            drop list_push(@out, raw lane_binop(e, op, elem, la[i => int64], lb[i => int64], at));
        } else {
            drop list_push(@out, raw term_none());
        }
    }
    drop lanes_put(e, id.index, move(out));
    pass NIL;
};

// An elementwise cast: the scalar cast per lane -- `=>` between integers the
// identity (value-preserving by the checker's rule), a float's the float
// cast; anything else opaque lanes.
func:enc_simd_cast = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:operand, int32:st, int32:vt, int32:id, bool:unchecked) never fails {
    int32:se = raw type_elem(e.types, st);
    int32:de = raw type_elem(e.types, vt);
    int32:n = (raw tt_get(e.types, vt)).b;
    List<Term>:src = raw lanes_of(e, operand, st);
    List<Term>:out = raw list_init::<Term>((n => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        Term:t = raw term_none();
        if ((i => int64) < src.count) {
            if ((!unchecked) && (raw is_int(e, se)) && (raw is_int(e, de)) && src[i => int64].ok && (!src[i => int64].is_bool)) {
                t = raw term_copy(src[i => int64]);
            } else {
                t = raw float_cast(e, src[i => int64], se, de);
            }
        }
        if (!t.ok) { t = raw term_opaque(e, de); }
        drop list_push(@out, move(t));
    }
    drop lanes_put(e, id, move(out));
    pass NIL;
};

// The reductions and the verdict collapses, in the emitter's order.
func:enc_simd_method = Term(Encoder->:e, string:m, ExprId:recv, int32:rt, int32:ty,
                             int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:elem = raw type_elem(e.types, rt);
    List<Term>:l = raw lanes_of(e, recv, rt);
    // AN INTEGER `.sum()` IS N-1 GUARDED `+` STEPS AT ONE SITE (D-284): ONE
    // `overflow` row there whose goal is every partial sum in range, with
    // N-1 traps (`record_at`'s traps field) -- `unencoded` where a lane has
    // no term (1.5.8b step 3).
    if ((raw string_eq(m, "sum")) && (raw is_int(e, elem)) && (l.count > 1i64)) {
        bool:sok = true;
        for (int64:sc in 0i64...l.count) { if (!(l[sc].ok && (!l[sc].is_bool))) { sok = false; } }
        int32:straps = (l.count - 1i64) =>! int32;
        if (!sok) {
            List<int32>:snone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_OVERFLOW(), "", snone, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), site, straps);
            if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        } else {
            Term:sacc = raw term_copy(l[0i64]);
            string:sgoal = "";
            List<int32>:sgs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
            for (int64:si in 1i64...l.count) {
                sacc = raw term_app2("+", sacc, l[si], false);
                string:sone = raw smt_range_axiom(sacc.text, raw type_int_bits(e.types, elem),
                                                  raw type_is_signed(e.types, elem));
                if (sgoal.len == 0i64) { sgoal = move(sone); } else { sgoal = raw smt_app2("and", sgoal, sone); }
                sgs = raw syms_union(sgs, sacc.syms);
            }
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_OVERFLOW(), sgoal, sgs, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), site, straps);
            if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, sgoal, sgs); }
            if ((e.in_prop == 0i32) && (e.quiet == 0i32)) { drop hyp_push(e, sgoal, sgs); }
        }
    }
    if (l.count == 0i64) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    for (int64:c in 0i64...l.count) { if (!l[c].ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); } }
    if ((raw string_eq(m, "any")) || (raw string_eq(m, "all"))) {
        string:hd = "or";
        if (raw string_eq(m, "all")) { hd = "and"; }
        Term:acc = raw term_copy(l[0i64]);
        if (!acc.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
        for (int64:i in 1i64...l.count) {
            if (!l[i].is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            acc = raw term_app2(hd, acc, l[i], true);
        }
        pass acc;
    }
    Term:acc2 = raw term_copy(l[0i64]);
    if (acc2.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
    for (int64:i2 in 1i64...l.count) {
        if (l[i2].is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
        if (raw string_eq(m, "sum")) {
            if (raw is_float(e, elem)) {
                acc2 = raw fp_make(e, "add", elem, acc2.text, l[i2].text, raw smt_app3("fp.add", "RNE", acc2.text, l[i2].text),
                                   raw syms_union(acc2.syms, l[i2].syms));
                if (!acc2.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            } else {
                acc2 = raw term_app2("+", acc2, l[i2], false);
            }
            continue;
        }
        string:pred = "<";
        if (raw string_eq(m, "max")) { pred = ">"; }
        if (raw is_float(e, elem)) {
            pred = "fp.lt";
            if (raw string_eq(m, "max")) { pred = "fp.gt"; }
        }
        Term:c2 = raw term_app2(pred, acc2, l[i2], true);
        acc2 = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", c2.text, acc2.text, l[i2].text),
                     syms: raw syms_union(c2.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    }
    pass acc2;
};

// A `limit` write point whose subject has no term (1.5.2 step 2; P-12; L-6):
// the row exists from the first commit that emits the guard, so the manifest
// stays an inventory of guards. A twisted subject has a term since 1.5.4b
// step 2 (D-278); a float subject takes its term at step 3; a string, a
// struct or an array subject stays here.
func:record_limit_unencoded = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop record(e, raw OK_LIMIT(), "", none, space, site, at, false);
    pass NIL;
};

// The `Rules` declaration a limit node resolved to, as an index; 0 for none.
func:limit_rule_of = int32(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:v) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(v)) { pass 0i32; }
    pass ((raw limit_target(raw ast_verify(e.ast, v))).index);
};

// The NAME of the local a place is rooted at (1.5.2 step 2, D-251), or 0:
// through member and index bases whose type is not a pointer, slice or
// handle (that storage is not the binding's own) to the identifier -- the
// emitter's `place_root_local`, in the walk's terms.
func:limited_root_name = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    int32:fuel = 64i32;
    while (fuel > 0i32) decreases fuel {
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, cur);
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, n.payload =>! int32);
            if (bi < 0i64) { pass 0i32; }
            pass n.payload =>! int32;
        }
        ExprId:base = ExprId{ index: 0i32 };
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
            base = raw expr_operand(n);
        } else {
            if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
                base = raw expr_lhs(n);
            } else {
                pass 0i32;
            }
        }
        int32:bt = raw ty_of(e, base);
        if (bt != 0i32) {
            int32:bk = raw type_kind(e.types, bt);
            if (bk == (raw TY_POINTER())) { pass 0i32; }
            if (bk == (raw TY_SLICE()))   { pass 0i32; }
            if (bk == (raw TY_HANDLE()))  { pass 0i32; }
        }
        cur = base;
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

// A binding's current version as a term; `term_none` when it has no symbol
// (an address-taken name, or a type outside the fragment).
func:bind_term = Term(Encoder->:e, int64:bi) never fails {
    int32:sym = e.binds[bi].sym;
    if (sym < 0i32) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, sym);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms[sym => int64].is_bool,
               text: raw sym_text(e, sym), syms: move(one) };
};

// A CLAUSE THE ENCODER CANNOT EXPRESS (L-8): a fresh opaque Bool named for
// the rule and the clause (`|r_call.c1.7|`, P-5's shape with the anonymous
// counter as k). As a goal conjunct it makes the row `open`; as a hypothesis
// it asserts nothing usable -- fail-closed either way (P-8).
func:clause_opaque = Term(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d, int32:j) never fails {
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:base = string_concat(raw intern_get(e.interns, raw decl_name(d)), ".c");
    base = string_concat(base, int_to_string((j + 1i32) => int64));
    string:nm = raw smt_sym(base, e.anon => int64);
    int32:idx = raw sym_new(e, nm, e.types.t_bool);
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

// THE RULE OVER A TERM (1.5.2 step 3, L-8): the conjunction, in source order,
// of every refinement's rule (recursively -- resolve refused cycles,
// RESOLVE-006; the fuel is a belt) and every clause encoded with `$` bound
// to the subject. `term_none` only when the SUBJECT has no term (a type
// outside the fragment); an inexpressible clause is an opaque conjunct. The
// clauses are encoded QUIET: a guard inside one is the predicate function's
// own site and is recorded there (L-1), never here -- and its CONDITION is
// the clause's (DEF-33): `$ != 0tbb32` holds only where `$` is not ERR.
func:enc_rule = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:rule, Term:subject, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (!subject.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: rule });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclRuleDecl) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    int32:rn = raw rule_refine_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...rn) {
        VerifyNode:rv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw rule_refine(e.ast, d, i));
        Term:sub = raw enc_rule(e, (raw limit_target(rv)).index, raw term_copy(subject), fuel - 1i32);
        if (!sub.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (first) { acc = move(sub); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, sub, true); }
    }
    int32:cn = raw rule_clause_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:j in 0i32...cn) {
        Term:saved = raw term_copy(e.subject);
        e.subject = raw term_copy(subject);
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        int64:pm = raw prop_begin(e);
        Term:c = raw prop_end(e, pm, raw enc_expr(e, raw rule_clause(e.ast, d, j)));
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        e.subject = move(saved);
        if (!(c.ok && c.is_bool)) { c = raw clause_opaque(e, d, j); }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if (first) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    pass acc;
};

// A STRUCT FIELD'S `limit<Rules>` (D-308, 1.5.8b step 6), as its declaration's
// index or 0. The base is read THROUGH a pointer (`.` auto-dereferences,
// D-098): the rule is the field's wherever its struct lives.
func:field_rule_of = int32(Encoder->:e, int32:bty, int32:fname) never fails {
    int32:bt = bty;
    if (bt == 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    if ((raw type_kind(e.types, bt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { bt = raw type_elem(e.types, bt); }
    int32:fdecl = raw struct_field_decl_of(e.ast, e.types, bt, fname);
    if (fdecl == 0i32) { pass 0i32; }
    VerifyId:fl = raw field_limit(raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: fdecl }));
    if (raw verify_is_none(fl)) { pass 0i32; }
    pass ((raw limit_target(raw ast_verify(e.ast, fl))).index);
};

// THE FIELD'S RULE OVER A TERM, pushed as a hypothesis (D-308 SS3). Nothing
// for an unlimited field, and nothing inside a proposition's own evaluation
// (DEF-33: a guard met inside a clause is the clause's, never a free fact).
func:assert_field_rule = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:bty, int32:fname, Term:v) never fails {
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (!v.ok) { pass NIL; }
    int32:rule = raw field_rule_of(e, bty, fname);
    if (rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:r = raw enc_rule(e, rule, v, 64i32);
    if (!r.ok) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, r.text, r.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A `limit` ROW AT A LIMITED FIELD'S WRITE POINT (D-308 SS2): the rule over
// the WRITTEN value, at the site the emitter guards under -- the member
// access for an assignment, the value expression for a struct literal.
// `unencoded` when the written value has no term (L-6's rule for a binding).
pub func:record_field_limit = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:bty, int32:fname, Term:v,
                                  int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:rule = raw field_rule_of(e, bty, fname);
    if (rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (!v.ok) { drop record_limit_unencoded(e, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at); pass NIL; }
    Term:g = raw enc_rule(e, rule, v, 64i32);
    if (!g.ok) { drop record_limit_unencoded(e, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at); pass NIL; }
    drop record(e, raw OK_LIMIT(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), site, at, true);
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, g.text, g.syms);      // ... and a fact after it (L-7's order)
    pass NIL;
};

// THE RULE AS A HYPOTHESIS on a binding's current version (L-7): pushed
// after a write point's own obligation (so the goal is never in its own
// cone) and at every invalidation. Sound because every write to the binding
// is guarded by this rule or discharged under these same hypotheses (P-8).
func:assert_rule = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:bi) never fails {
    int32:rule = e.binds[bi].rule;
    if (rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:v = raw bind_term(e, bi);
    if (!v.ok) { pass NIL; }
    Term:r = raw enc_rule(e, rule, v, 64i32);
    if (!r.ok) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, r.text, r.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A `limit` ROW at a write point of binding `bi`: the rule over the new
// version, encoded; `unencoded` when the version has no term (L-6).
func:record_limit = NIL(Encoder->:e, int64:bi, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    int32:rule = e.binds[bi].rule;
    if (rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:v = raw bind_term(e, bi);
    if (!v.ok) { drop record_limit_unencoded(e, space, site, at); pass NIL; }
    Term:g = raw enc_rule(e, rule, v, 64i32);
    if (!g.ok) { drop record_limit_unencoded(e, space, site, at); pass NIL; }
    drop record(e, raw OK_LIMIT(), g.text, g.syms, space, site, at, true);
    pass NIL;
};

// AFTER A WRITE to `name` (L-7's order): the site's obligation, then the rule
// as a hypothesis. Nothing for an unlimited or unbound name.
func:after_write = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:space, int32:site, Span:at) never fails {
    if (name == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (bi < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.binds[bi].rule == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop record_limit(e, bi, space, site, at);
    drop assert_rule(e, bi);
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL, ENCODED ONCE (1.5.2 step 3, L-10; 1.5.3 step 2): the receiver or
// callee expression and every argument (their sites recorded, their terms
// kept), and the callee the checker recorded -- a method call's declaration
// (`exprtypes_set_callee`), a free call's identifier's symbol as `emit_call`
// resolves it; a local or parameter holding a function value is an indirect
// call and has no rows (its entry check covers it). `terms`/`types`/`names`
// are per PARAMETER position: the receiver is parameter 0 when the method
// takes one more parameter than the call passes arguments.
struct:CallEnc = {
    int32:cd;              // the callee's declaration, 0 for none usable
    bool:coroutine;        // `async` or `thread`: the entry check runs at state 0, never bypassed
    bool:through_dyn;      // the receiver is a `dyn`: the vtable's target is the entry, never bypassed
    List<int32>:names;
    List<int32>:types;
    List<Term>:terms;
};

// THE CALLEE'S DECLARATION (1.5.2 step 3; factored at 1.5.8c step 4): the one
// the checker recorded, or -- a free call records none -- the identifier's
// own symbol when it is a declaration. 0 when nothing is known.
func:call_decl_of = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    int32:cd = raw exprtypes_callee(e.et, id);
    if ((cd == 0i32) && (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) && (n.a != 0i32)) {
        ExprNode:cn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        if ((cn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) && (cn.a != 0i32)) {
            Symbol:cs = raw symtab_get(e.tab, cn.a);
            if (cs.origin_kind == (raw SYM_DECL())) { cd = cs.origin; }
        }
    }
    pass cd;
};

func:enc_call = CallEnc(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    Term:rcv = raw term_none();
    int32:rty = 0i32;
    // A NAMESPACE CALL (D-273, 1.5.4c): the receiver names a module -- no
    // site, no term, no parameter -- and the call is the direct call the
    // checker recorded, its rows the direct call's.
    bool:ns_call = false;
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        if ((raw exprtypes_ns_decl(e.et, id)) != 0i32) { ns_call = true; }
    }
    if ((n.a != 0i32) && (!ns_call)) {
        rcv = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        rty = raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
    }
    int32:g = 0i32;
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) { g = raw expr_generic_count(n); }
    int32:argc = n.c - g;
    List<Term>:args = raw list_init::<Term>((argc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<int32>:atys = raw list_init::<int32>((argc => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...argc) {
        ExprId:aid = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, g + i) };
        drop list_push(@args, raw enc_expr(e, aid));
        drop list_push(@atys, raw ty_of(e, aid));
    }
    // `string_from_bytes(p, len)` (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step 6c): the one runtime
    // producer of a caller-supplied length -- its `bounds` row at the call's
    // own node, over the argument term encoded above. The callee is the
    // builtin's own name (D-294 keeps it from every other declaration).
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) && (argc == 2i32) && (n.a != 0i32)) {
        ExprNode:lcn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        if (lcn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            if (raw builtin_caller_len(raw intern_get(e.interns, lcn.payload =>! int32))) {
                drop record_len_ceiling(e, raw term_copy(args[1i64]), id.index, n.span);
            }
        }
    }
    CallEnc:none = CallEnc{ cd: 0i32, coroutine: false, through_dyn: false,
                            names: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64), types: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64),
                            terms: raw list_init::<Term>(1i64) };
    int32:cd = raw call_decl_of(e, id, n);
    if (cd == 0i32) { pass none; }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: cd });
    if (cdn.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass none; }
    if (!(raw decl_is_none(raw fn_variadic(e.ast, cdn)))) { pass none; }
    int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(e.ast, cdn);
    int32:off = 0i32;
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) && (!ns_call)) {
        if (pc == (argc + 1i32)) { off = 1i32; }
        else { if (pc != argc) { pass none; } }
    } else {
        if (pc != argc) { pass none; }
    }
    List<int32>:names = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<int32>:types = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<Term>:terms = raw list_init::<Term>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:p in 0i32...pc) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw fn_param(e.ast, cdn, p));
        drop list_push(@names, raw decl_name(pd));
        if ((off == 1i32) && (p == 0i32)) {
            drop list_push(@types, rty);
            drop list_push(@terms, raw term_copy(rcv));
        } else {
            int64:ai = (p - off) => int64;
            drop list_push(@types, atys[ai]);
            drop list_push(@terms, raw term_copy(args[ai]));
        }
    }
    bool:co = (raw decl_has(cdn, raw DECL_ASYNC())) || (raw decl_has(cdn, raw DECL_THREAD()));
    bool:dy = false;
    if (rty != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(e.types, rty)) == (raw TY_DYN())) { dy = true; } }
    pass CallEnc{ cd: cd, coroutine: co, through_dyn: dy, names: move(names),
                  types: move(types), terms: move(terms) };
};

// The two call-site rows of a recorded callee (L-10, D-268): its role is
// `bypass` at a direct sync call -- discharged with every other bypass row of
// the call, the call names the body -- and `held` at an `await` or through a
// `dyn`, where the guard is the callee's own entry and no build can remove it.
func:record_call_rows = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce) never fails {
    // THE RECURSIVE CALL'S ROW FIRST (D-304 (5), 1.5.8c step 4): it needs the
    // callee even where `enc_call` bound nothing (a variadic callee).
    drop record_terminate_call(e, id, n, ce);
    if (ce.cd == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:role = raw ROLE_BYPASS();
    if (ce.coroutine || ce.through_dyn) { role = raw ROLE_HELD(); }
    drop record_subsume_ce(e, id, n, ce, role);
    drop record_requires(e, id, n, ce, role);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE CALLEE'S MEASURE OVER THE ACTUALS (D-304 (5), 1.5.8c step 4): its
// `decreases E` with the parameters bound by position to the argument terms
// (the receiver first), QUIET -- the guards inside `E` are the callee's own
// rows, recorded at ITS entry under its parameters' types and lowered once in
// its predicate -- a fresh version of each name equal to its term, released
// after; `enc_under`'s shape for a term that is not a proposition.
func:measure_under = Term(Encoder->:e, CallEnc:ce, DeclNode:cdn) never fails {
    VerifyId:mv = raw fn_measure(e.ast, cdn);
    if (raw verify_is_none(mv)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...ce.names.count) {
        drop bind_define(e, ce.names[i], ce.types[i], raw term_copy(ce.terms[i]), 0i32, true);
    }
    e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
    Term:t = raw enc_expr(e, raw contract_cond(raw ast_verify(e.ast, mv)));
    e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
    drop scope_release(e, mark);
    if (!(t.ok && (!t.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass t;
};

// THE RECURSIVE CALL'S ROW (D-304 (5), 1.5.8c step 4): at a call whose callee
// shares the caller's cyclic group, both stating a measure -- the goal
// `(and (>= m0 0) (< m1 m0))`, `m1` the callee's measure over the actuals,
// `m0` the caller's at entry (`fn_m0`): the check the emitter puts before the
// call (`emit_measure_call_check`), kind `terminate`, a `guard` row of the
// CALLER's (the trap is at the call site whatever the callee's kind -- at an
// `await` and a spawn too), group the call, one trap; its condition a
// hypothesis after the site as every guard's is (inside a proposition, the
// proposition's own -- DEF-33). Recorded only while the BODY is walked
// (`in_body`): a generated predicate has no snapshot and emits no check, so a
// recursive call inside a `requires` clause has no row either. A measure the
// walk cannot express leaves the row `unencoded` and the check stays; a callee
// `enc_call` could not bind (a variadic) is found by the same resolution and
// its row is `unencoded` too, so the check is never a trap no row accounts
// for. A call through a `dyn` is no edge and no row (P-7).
func:record_terminate_call = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (ce.through_dyn) { pass NIL; }
    int32:cd = ce.cd;
    if (cd == 0i32) {
        cd = raw call_decl_of(e, id, n);
        if (cd == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) && (n.a != 0i32)) {
            if ((raw exprtypes_ns_decl(e.et, id)) == 0i32) {
                int32:rty = raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
                if (rty != 0i32) { if ((raw type_kind(e.types, rty)) == (raw TY_DYN())) { pass NIL; } }
            }
        }
    }
    if (!(raw exprtypes_same_cyclic_group(e.et, e.fn_decl, cd))) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: cd });
    if (cdn.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass NIL; }
    if (raw verify_is_none(raw fn_measure(e.ast, cdn))) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:fdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    if (raw verify_is_none(raw fn_measure(e.ast, fdn))) { pass NIL; }
    // OUTSIDE THE BODY -- a recursive call inside a `requires` clause or the
    // measure itself -- the predicate that evaluates it has no snapshot and
    // emits no check: an `unencoded` row with NO trap, so the group's
    // `stack-depth` row stays `open` (a recursion the group's measures do not
    // bound) and the belts expect no trap for it.
    if (!e.in_body) {
        List<int32>:none0 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), "", none0, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, false,
                       raw ROLE_GUARD(), id.index, 0i32);
        pass NIL;
    }
    Term:m1 = raw term_none();
    if (ce.cd != 0i32) { m1 = raw measure_under(e, ce, cdn); }
    if (!(m1.ok && e.fn_m0.ok)) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, false,
                       raw ROLE_GUARD(), id.index, 1i32);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    Term:nn = raw term_app2(">=", raw term_copy(e.fn_m0), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
    Term:lt = raw term_app2("<", m1, raw term_copy(e.fn_m0), true);
    Term:g = raw term_app2("and", nn, lt, true);
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, true,
                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), id.index, 1i32);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, g.text, g.syms); pass NIL; }
    if (e.quiet > 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    drop hyp_push(e, g.text, g.syms);
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL's `limit-subsume` ROW (L-10): for a callee whose declaration has
// limited parameters, ONE row per call site -- the conjunction over those
// parameters of their rules over the argument terms, with the caller's cone
// as the hypotheses (a limited-binding argument brings its rule: the spec's
// "one `Rules` implies another at a boundary"). An argument the encoder
// cannot name is opaque (the row is `open`); one whose type is outside the
// fragment makes the row `unencoded`. A `dyn` call's trait method has no
// limited parameter (TYPE-064), and a coroutine callee's row is `held`
// (D-268 amending D-252): recorded, never elided.
func:record_subsume_ce = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce, int32:role) never fails {
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(e.ast, cdn);
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    bool:has_limited = false;
    bool:broken = false;
    for (int32:i2 in 0i32...pc) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw fn_param(e.ast, cdn, i2));
        VerifyId:pl = raw param_limit(pd);
        if (raw verify_is_none(pl)) { continue; }
        has_limited = true;
        int32:rule = (raw limit_target(raw ast_verify(e.ast, pl))).index;
        Term:a = raw term_copy(ce.terms[i2 => int64]);
        if (!a.ok) { a = raw term_opaque(e, ce.types[i2 => int64]); }
        if (!a.ok) { broken = true; continue; }
        Term:c = raw enc_rule(e, rule, a, 64i32);
        if (!c.ok) { broken = true; continue; }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if (!has_limited) { pass NIL; }
    if (broken) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_LIMIT_SUBSUME(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, false,
                       role, id.index, 0i32);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_LIMIT_SUBSUME(), acc.text, acc.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, true,
                   role, id.index, 0i32);
    // A call inside a proposition: the callee's entry check is a guard of
    // the proposition's evaluation (DEF-33).
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, acc.text, acc.syms); }
    pass NIL;
};

// A CALL's `requires` ROW (1.5.3 step 2; L-7, D-268): the callee's clauses
// conjoined over the argument terms -- the parameters bound to them by
// position (the receiver first), QUIET, since a guard inside a clause is
// the callee's own (L-5). ONE row per call, whatever the callee's kind: the
// only place the call is ever proven.
func:record_requires = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, ExprNode:n, CallEnc:ce, int32:role) never fails {
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    if ((raw contract_count(e, cdn, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES())) == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:g = raw enc_under(e, ce.names, ce.types, ce.terms, cdn, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), false,
                           raw term_none());
    if (!g.ok) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), "", none, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, false,
                       role, id.index, 0i32);
        if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_opaque(e); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span, true,
                   role, id.index, 0i32);
    if (e.in_prop > 0i32) { drop prop_fact(e, g.text, g.syms); }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE CALLEE'S `ensures` AS KNOWLEDGE (L-4): under the arguments and the
// unwrapped value, quiet; the clauses the encoder cannot express are
// dropped (assuming less is sound), the rest one hypothesis.
func:push_callee_ensures = NIL(Encoder->:e, CallEnc:ce, Term:val) never fails {
    if (ce.cd == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (!val.ok) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    if ((raw contract_count(e, cdn, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES())) == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:h = raw enc_under(e, ce.names, ce.types, ce.terms, cdn, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), true,
                           raw term_copy(val));
    if (h.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h.text, h.syms); }
    pass NIL;
};

// A `pure never fails` CALLEE'S VALUE (L-3): the application of its
// uninterpreted function to the argument terms -- `|uf.<name>.<decl>|`, one
// symbol per declaration -- when every argument and the result are in the
// fragment and the callee is not a coroutine; its result's range axiom is a
// hypothesis (the value IS of that type). `term_none` otherwise.
func:uf_value = Term(Encoder->:e, CallEnc:ce, int32:ty) never fails {
    if (ce.cd == 0i32) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (ce.coroutine) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    DeclNode:cdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: ce.cd });
    if (!(raw fn_is_pure_never_fails(e, cdn))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (!(raw is_termed(e, ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    string:sorts = "(";
    string:app = "";
    List<int32>:syms = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...ce.terms.count) {
        if (!ce.terms[i].ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        int32:pt = ce.types[i];
        if (!(raw is_termed(e, pt))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (ce.terms[i].is_bool != (raw is_bool(e, pt))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (i > 0i64) { sorts = string_concat(sorts, " "); app = string_concat(app, " "); }
        if (raw is_bool(e, pt)) { sorts = string_concat(sorts, "Bool"); }
        else { if (raw is_float(e, pt)) { sorts = string_concat(sorts, raw fp_sort(e, pt)); }
               else { sorts = string_concat(sorts, "Int"); } }
        app = string_concat(app, ce.terms[i].text);
        syms = raw syms_union(syms, ce.terms[i].syms);
    }
    sorts = string_concat(sorts, ")");
    string:fname = string_concat("uf.", raw intern_get(e.interns, raw decl_name(cdn)));
    string:fsym = raw smt_sym(fname, ce.cd => int64);
    int32:fi = raw sym_new_fun(e, fsym, sorts, raw is_bool(e, ty), raw fp_sort(e, ty));
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, fi);
    syms = raw syms_union(syms, one);
    string:text = raw smt_app1(fsym, app);
    if (ce.terms.count == 0i64) { text = string_concat(fsym, ""); }
    if (raw is_word(e, ty)) {
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_range_axiom(text, raw word_bits(e, ty),
                                              raw word_signed(e, ty)), syms);
    }
    if (raw is_twisted(e, ty)) { drop hyp_push(e, raw twisted_axiom(e, text, ty), syms); }
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: raw is_bool(e, ty), text: move(text), syms: move(syms) };
};

// --- contracts (1.5.3 step 2; D-221, D-241, D-243, D-245, D-267, D-268) -------

// The clauses of one kind on a declaration: their count, and their
// conjunction over the current bindings -- every clause a term, or
// `term_none` when one is not (a GOAL needs every clause; a HYPOTHESIS may
// drop the ones it cannot express, `partial`, and asserts the rest).
func:contract_count = int32(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d, int32:kind) never fails {
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass 0i32; }
    int32:n = 0i32;
    int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cc) {
        VerifyNode:cv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_contract(e.ast, d, i));
        if (cv.kind != VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) { continue; }
        if ((raw contract_kind(cv)) == kind) { n = n + 1i32; }
    }
    pass n;
};

func:fn_is_pure_never_fails = bool(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d) never fails {
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass false; }
    bool:is_pure = false;
    bool:nf = false;
    int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cc) {
        VerifyNode:cv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_contract(e.ast, d, i));
        if (cv.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyPure) { is_pure = true; }
        if (cv.kind == VerifyKind.VerifyNeverFails) { nf = true; }
    }
    pass (is_pure && nf);
};

func:contract_conj = Term(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d, int32:kind, bool:partial) never fails {
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    bool:saw_any = false;
    int32:cc = raw fn_contract_count(e.ast, d);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...cc) {
        VerifyNode:cv = raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_contract(e.ast, d, i));
        if (cv.kind != VerifyKind.VerifyContractNode) { continue; }
        if ((raw contract_kind(cv)) != kind) { continue; }
        saw_any = true;
        int64:pm = raw prop_begin(e);
        Term:c = raw prop_end(e, pm, raw enc_expr(e, raw contract_cond(cv)));
        if (!(c.ok && c.is_bool)) {
            if (partial) { continue; }
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if (!saw_any) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    if (first) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass acc;
};

// A loop invariant's clauses, likewise.
func:invariant_conj = Term(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:inv, bool:partial) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(inv)) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    VerifyNode:v = raw ast_verify(e.ast, inv);
    Term:acc = raw term_none();
    bool:first = true;
    for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw invariant_count(v))) {
        int64:pm = raw prop_begin(e);
        Term:c = raw prop_end(e, pm, raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, v.b, i) }));
        if (!(c.ok && c.is_bool)) {
            if (partial) { continue; }
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
        if (first) { acc = move(c); first = false; }
        else { acc = raw term_app2("and", acc, c, true); }
    }
    if ((raw invariant_count(v)) == 0i32) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
    if (first) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass acc;
};

// Does a loop's termination clause CHECK anything (a `decreases E` with an
// expression): the emitter's `measure_checks`, for the encoder.
func:enc_measure_checks = bool(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:meas) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(meas)) { pass false; }
    VerifyNode:v = raw ast_verify(e.ast, meas);
    if (raw measure_is_unbounded(v)) { pass false; }
    pass (!(raw expr_is_none(raw measure_expr(v))));
};

func:invariant_clauses = int32(Encoder->:e, VerifyId:inv) never fails {
    if (raw verify_is_none(inv)) { pass 0i32; }
    pass (raw invariant_count(raw ast_verify(e.ast, inv)));
};

// SUBSTITUTION (L-2, L-4): the declaration's contract clauses of `kind`
// encoded with its parameters bound, by position, to the given terms -- a
// fresh version of each name equal to its term (an inexpressible term an
// opaque version), so a compound argument is named once -- and `result`
// bound to `result_term`. QUIET: the clauses' own guards are the callee's
// (L-5), never this function's sites. The bindings are released after.
func:enc_under = Term(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:names, List<int32>:types, List<Term>:terms,
                      DeclNode:d, int32:kind, bool:partial, Term:result_term) never fails {
    int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...names.count) {
        drop bind_define(e, names[i], types[i], raw term_copy(terms[i]), 0i32, true);
    }
    Term:saved_res = raw term_copy(e.result);
    e.result = raw term_copy(result_term);
    e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
    Term:t = raw contract_conj(e, d, kind, partial);
    e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
    e.result = move(saved_res);
    drop scope_release(e, mark);
    pass t;
};

// THE FUNCTION'S OWN ENTRY (L-7; D-252 as amended by D-268): its `requires`
// row -- kind `requires`, SITE_DECL the declaration, the conjunction over the
// parameters' first versions, hypotheses the range axioms -- discharged, the
// entry check is elided in place (the `.req` predicate stays uncalled). The
// clauses are encoded LOUD: a guard inside one is this function's site
// (L-5), lowered once in the predicate. Then the conjunction as a hypothesis
// (the body may assume its precondition), after the row so the goal is never
// in its own cone. One trap per clause in the predicate: the row's `traps`.
pub func:enc_entry_contracts = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    // THE CONFORMANCE ROWS FIRST: the impl's own `requires` is their goal,
    // and the hypothesis pushed below would prove it of itself.
    drop enc_conformance(e, d);
    int32:rn = raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES());
    if (rn > 0i32) {
        Term:g = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), false);
        if (!g.ok) {
            List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), "", none, raw SITE_DECL(), e.fn_decl, d.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.fn_decl, rn);
            e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
            Term:h = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), true);
            e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
            if (h.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h.text, h.syms); }
        } else {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_DECL(), e.fn_decl, d.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.fn_decl, rn);
            drop hyp_push(e, g.text, g.syms);
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// CONFORMANCE (L-6): an impl method against its trait's method of the same
// name, in regions of their own so nothing leaks into the body. `requires`:
// the trait's clauses as a hypothesis over this method's parameters, the
// impl's own as the goal -- an impl may WEAKEN a precondition (trait implies
// impl). `ensures`: the impl's clauses as a hypothesis over an opaque result,
// the trait's as the goal -- an impl may STRENGTHEN a postcondition (impl
// implies trait). Both rows `conform`: no guard, an open row is reported
// (the impl's own entry and seam checks are the runtime), never a refusal.
func:enc_conformance = NIL(Encoder->:e, DeclNode:d) never fails {
    if (e.impl_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.trait_ty == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:tdecl = raw type_decl_of(e.types, e.trait_ty);
    if (tdecl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:td = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: tdecl });
    int32:tmi = 0i32;
    int32:mn = raw item_member_count(e.ast, td);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...mn) {
        DeclId:mid = raw item_member(e.ast, td, i);
        DeclNode:m = raw ast_decl(e.ast, mid);
        if (m.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { continue; }
        if ((raw decl_name(m)) == (raw decl_name(d))) { tmi = mid.index; }
    }
    if (tmi == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (tmi == e.fn_decl) { pass NIL; }   // an inherited default IS the trait's method
    DeclNode:tm = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: tmi });
    int32:pc = raw fn_param_count(e.ast, d);
    if (pc != (raw fn_param_count(e.ast, tm))) { pass NIL; }
    if ((pc => int64) > e.binds.count) { pass NIL; }
    List<int32>:names = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<int32>:types = raw list_init::<int32>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    List<Term>:terms = raw list_init::<Term>((pc => int64) + 1i64);
    for (int32:p in 0i32...pc) {
        DeclNode:tp = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw fn_param(e.ast, tm, p));
        drop list_push(@names, raw decl_name(tp));
        drop list_push(@types, e.binds[p => int64].type_id);
        drop list_push(@terms, raw bind_term(e, p => int64));
    }
    int32:tr_n = raw contract_count(e, tm, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES());
    int32:im_n = raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES());
    if ((tr_n > 0i32) || (im_n > 0i32)) {
        drop region_enter(e);
        Term:th = raw enc_under(e, names, types, terms, tm, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), true, raw term_none());
        if (th.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, th.text, th.syms); }
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:ig = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), false);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (ig.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), ig.text, ig.syms, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_REQUIRES(), "", none, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        }
        drop region_leave(e);
    }
    int32:te_n = raw contract_count(e, tm, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES());
    int32:ie_n = raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES());
    if ((te_n > 0i32) || (ie_n > 0i32)) {
        drop region_enter(e);
        // The trait's precondition is knowledge here too: the trait's
        // postcondition is claimed only for calls that satisfied it.
        Term:th2 = raw enc_under(e, names, types, terms, tm, raw CONTRACT_REQUIRES(), true, raw term_none());
        if (th2.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, th2.text, th2.syms); }
        Term:r = raw term_opaque(e, e.ret_type);
        Term:saved_res = raw term_copy(e.result);
        e.result = raw term_copy(r);
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:ih = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), true);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        e.result = move(saved_res);
        if (ih.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, ih.text, ih.syms); }
        Term:tg = raw enc_under(e, names, types, terms, tm, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), false, raw term_copy(r));
        if (tg.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), tg.text, tg.syms, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), "", none2, raw SITE_CONF(), e.fn_decl, d.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_CONFORM(), e.fn_decl, 0i32);
        }
        drop region_leave(e);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE SEAM (L-7, L-12): at a `pass v` or a successful `return Result{...}`,
// kind `ensures`, SITE_STMT the statement, the clauses conjoined with
// `result` the value's term (opaque when the value has none; `term_none` for
// a bare `pass`, where `result` is NIL) -- encoded LOUD under the seam's
// clause context, so a guard inside a clause is this seam's own site. One
// trap per return point: `traps` 1.
func:record_seam = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, Span:at, Term:v, int32:vty, bool:has_value) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    if ((raw contract_count(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES())) == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    Term:saved_res = raw term_copy(e.result);
    e.result = raw term_none();
    if (has_value) {
        if (v.ok) { e.result = raw term_copy(v); }
        else { e.result = raw term_opaque(e, vty); }
    }
    e.clause_ctx = sid.index;
    Term:g = raw contract_conj(e, d, raw CONTRACT_ENSURES(), false);
    e.clause_ctx = 0i32;
    e.result = move(saved_res);
    if (!g.ok) {
        List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
        drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, at, false,
                       raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop record_at(e, raw OK_ENSURES(), g.text, g.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, at, true,
                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
    pass NIL;
};

// The loop frame a `continue` or `break` re-enters or leaves: the innermost
// for an unlabelled one, the one carrying the label otherwise; -1 for none.
func:loop_frame = int64(Encoder->:e, int32:label) never fails {
    if (e.loop_sids.count == 0i64) { pass (0i64 - 1i64); }
    if (label == 0i32) { pass (e.loop_sids.count - 1i64); }
    int64:i = e.loop_sids.count;
    while (i > 0i64) decreases i {
        i = i - 1i64;
        if (e.loop_labels[i] == label) { pass i; }
    }
    pass (0i64 - 1i64);
};

// Does a `break` leave the loop whose body this is? An unlabelled one
// directly in the body, a labelled one naming the loop anywhere in it.
func:loop_has_break = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:label, bool:nested, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    // A `break` INSIDE A PICK EXPRESSION'S ARM (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): the
    // arms are statements inside an expression, found through the one
    // enumeration of a statement's expressions.
    List<int32>:xs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop stmt_expr_ids(e.ast, s, @xs);
    for (int64:xi in 0i64...xs.count) {
        if (raw expr_has_break(e, ExprId{ index: xs[xi] }, label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt) {
        if ((raw stmt_label(s)) == 0i32) { pass (!nested); }
        pass ((raw stmt_label(s)) == label);
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw loop_has_break(e, ch, label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_then(s), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_else(s), label, nested, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)); }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), label, true, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw loop_has_break(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), label, true, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw arm_body(arm), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass false;
};

// The `break` finder's descent into an EXPRESSION: a pick expression's arms
// are statements (DEF-26); every other kind is searched for nested ones.
func:expr_has_break = bool(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, int32:label, bool:nested, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...n.c) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, n.b, a));
            if (raw expr_has_break(e, raw arm_guard(arm), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
            if (raw loop_has_break(e, raw arm_body(arm), label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
    }
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) {
        if (raw expr_has_break(e, ExprId{ index: kids[i] }, label, nested, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

// A LOOP'S COUNTER as `walk_loop` receives it (L-11, L-12): kind 0 none, 1 a
// `for` binding by name (`ranged` when the iterable is a range: `start` and
// `limit` its captured bounds, the limit exclusive, the step 1, ascending),
// 2 a counted loop's `$` (`start`, `limit`, `step` captured, `asc` the
// direction term, `lit_step` the numeral step's value or 0).
struct:Counter = {
    int32:kind;
    int32:name;
    bool:ranged;
    Term:start;
    Term:limit;
    Term:step;
    Term:asc;
    int64:lit_step;
};

func:counter_none = Counter() never fails {
    pass Counter{ kind: 0i32, name: 0i32, ranged: false, start: raw term_none(), limit: raw term_none(),
                  step: raw term_none(), asc: raw term_none(), lit_step: 0i64 };
};

// CAPTURE a term at entry (L-11; D-234's rule): a fresh anonymous symbol of
// the type, defined equal to the term when the term exists -- what the
// body assigns later cannot move it, exactly as the emitter's slots hold the
// bound and the step across iterations.
func:term_capture = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:ty, Term:t) never fails {
    Term:s = raw term_opaque(e, ty);
    if (!s.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (t.ok && (t.is_bool == s.is_bool)) {
        drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", s.text, t.text), raw syms_union(s.syms, t.syms));
    }
    pass s;
};

// A fresh `$` symbol (`|$.k|`, the anonymous counter as k), int64 -- the
// checker's type for a counter.
func:dollar_fresh = Term(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    int32:i64t = raw tt_int(e.types, 64i32, true);
    e.anon = e.anon + 1i32;
    string:nm = raw smt_sym("$", e.anon => int64);
    int32:idx = raw sym_new(e, nm, i64t);
    List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
    drop list_push(@one, idx);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: move(nm), syms: move(one) };
};

func:term_not = Term(Term:t) never fails {
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", t.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(t.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
};

// THE COUNTER'S RANGE IN THE BODY (L-11): `start <= $ < limit` ascending,
// `limit < $ <= start` descending, each under the direction; on a numeral
// step the residue class (`mod` by a numeral is linear).
func:push_dollar_range = NIL(Encoder->:e, Counter:c, Term:d) never fails {
    if (!(d.ok && c.start.ok && c.limit.ok && c.asc.ok)) { pass NIL; }
    Term:up = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<=", c.start, d, true), raw term_app2("<", d, c.limit, true), true);
    Term:down = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<", c.limit, d, true), raw term_app2("<=", d, c.start, true), true);
    Term:nasc = raw term_not(c.asc);
    Term:h1 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, up, true);
    Term:h2 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, down, true);
    drop hyp_push(e, h1.text, h1.syms);
    drop hyp_push(e, h2.text, h2.syms);
    if (c.lit_step > 0i64) {
        Term:s = raw term_lit(int_to_string(c.lit_step), false);
        Term:ru = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", d, c.start, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:rd = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", c.start, d, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:h3 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, ru, true);
        Term:h4 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, rd, true);
        drop hyp_push(e, h3.text, h3.syms);
        drop hyp_push(e, h4.text, h4.syms);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE COUNTER AFTER THE LOOP (L-11): past the limit -- by less than a numeral
// step -- and past the start, under the direction; the residue class again.
// A zero-iteration loop (`start == limit`) exits with the start, which
// satisfies every one of these.
func:push_dollar_exit = NIL(Encoder->:e, Counter:c, Term:x) never fails {
    if (!(x.ok && c.start.ok && c.limit.ok && c.asc.ok)) { pass NIL; }
    Term:nasc = raw term_not(c.asc);
    Term:up = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2(">=", x, c.limit, true), raw term_app2(">=", x, c.start, true), true);
    Term:down = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<=", x, c.limit, true), raw term_app2("<=", x, c.start, true), true);
    Term:h1 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, up, true);
    Term:h2 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, down, true);
    drop hyp_push(e, h1.text, h1.syms);
    drop hyp_push(e, h2.text, h2.syms);
    if (c.lit_step > 0i64) {
        Term:s = raw term_lit(int_to_string(c.lit_step), false);
        Term:lu = raw term_app2("<", x, raw term_app2("+", c.limit, s, false), true);
        Term:ld = raw term_app2(">", x, raw term_app2("-", c.limit, s, false), true);
        Term:ru = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", x, c.start, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:rd = raw term_app2("=", raw term_app2("mod", raw term_app2("-", c.start, x, false), s, false), raw term_lit("0", false), true);
        Term:h3 = raw term_app2("=>", c.asc, raw term_app2("and", lu, ru, true), true);
        Term:h4 = raw term_app2("=>", nasc, raw term_app2("and", ld, rd, true), true);
        drop hyp_push(e, h3.text, h3.syms);
        drop hyp_push(e, h4.text, h4.syms);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE INCREMENTED COUNTER the head will see (L-11): `$ + step` ascending,
// `$ - step` descending; a range binding's is `i + 1`.
func:counter_next = Term(Encoder->:e, Term:cur, Term:step, Term:asc) never fails {
    if (!(cur.ok && step.ok)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:up = raw term_app2("+", cur, step, false);
    if (!asc.ok) { pass up; }
    Term:down = raw term_app2("-", cur, step, false);
    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app3("ite", asc.text, up.text, down.text),
               syms: raw syms_union(asc.syms, raw syms_union(up.syms, down.syms)) };
};

// SUBSTITUTE the incremented counter for a head-visit row (the preservation
// row, a `continue`'s): `$`'s entry in `dollars` set to the next value, a
// range binding given a new version equal to `i + 1` (L-11, L-12).
func:counter_advance = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:kind, int32:name, Term:step, Term:asc, int64:dollar) never fails {
    if (kind == 2i32) {
        if ((dollar >= 0i64) && (dollar < e.dollars.count)) {
            Term:cur = raw term_copy(e.dollars[dollar]);
            e.dollars[dollar] = raw counter_next(e, cur, step, asc);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (kind == 1i32) {
        int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
        if (bi < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
        Term:cur = raw bind_term(e, bi);
        if (!cur.ok) { pass NIL; }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("+", cur, raw term_lit("1", false), false));
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A LOOP (L-8, L-9): the ENTRY row -- kind `invariant`, SITE_STMT the loop
// statement, the conjunction over the versions before any havoc, LOUD under
// the loop's clause context (a guard inside a clause is the head's site,
// lowered once, and run at every visit: the preservation and `continue`
// encodings record its rows too, DEF-81) -- then the body's assigned names havoced, and inside the
// body's region the invariant as a hypothesis over the havoced versions and,
// for `while`/`when`, the condition too (both dominate only the body); at
// the body's end the PRESERVATION row keyed at the body block, and one at
// every `continue` that re-enters this loop (`walk_stmt`); after the loop
// the names havoced again and, when nothing `break`s out, the invariant as a
// hypothesis once more -- it holds at every head visit and the exit is one.
// The condition's negation is NOT pushed (1.5.4's path condition). All of a
// loop's rows share its group and its clause count: the head's check elides
// only when every one is discharged, and keeps one trap per clause.
func:walk_loop = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, VerifyId:inv, StmtId:body, ExprId:cond,
                     int32:label, Counter:ctr, VerifyId:meas) never fails {
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    List<int32>:assigned = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop collect_assigned(e, body, @assigned);
    // THE COUNTER (L-11, L-12): a `for` binding is an assigned name of its
    // loop (havoced with the rest); `$` starts at its start for the entry row.
    if (ctr.kind == 1i32) { drop list_push(@assigned, ctr.name); }
    int64:dollar = 0i64 - 1i64;
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) {
        dollar = e.dollars.count;
        drop list_push(@e.dollars, raw term_copy(ctr.start));
    }
    int32:nc = raw invariant_clauses(e, inv);
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        e.clause_ctx = sid.index;
        Term:g0 = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, false);
        e.clause_ctx = 0i32;
        if (g0.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), g0.text, g0.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        }
    }
    drop invalidate(e, assigned);
    drop region_enter(e);
    // THE COUNTER IN THE BODY (L-11, L-12): a fresh `$` inside its range; a
    // range binding's havoced version inside its bounds.
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) {
        Term:d = raw dollar_fresh(e);
        e.dollars[dollar] = raw term_copy(d);
        drop push_dollar_range(e, ctr, d);
    }
    if ((ctr.kind == 1i32) && ctr.ranged) {
        int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, ctr.name);
        if (bi >= 0i64) {
            Term:iv = raw bind_term(e, bi);
            if (iv.ok && ctr.start.ok && ctr.limit.ok) {
                Term:rf = raw term_app2("and", raw term_app2("<=", ctr.start, iv, true), raw term_app2("<", iv, ctr.limit, true), true);
                drop hyp_push(e, rf.text, rf.syms);
            }
        }
    }
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:h = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, true);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (h.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h.text, h.syms); }
    }
    if (!(raw expr_is_none(cond))) {
        Term:wc = raw enc_expr(e, cond);
        if (wc.ok && wc.is_bool) { drop hyp_push(e, wc.text, wc.syms); }
    }
    // THE MEASURE (D-304, 1.5.8c step 1; the `terminate` rows): the check runs
    // at the top of the body, each time the condition holds, so its rows sit
    // INSIDE the body's region with the invariant and the condition as
    // hypotheses. `E` is encoded LOUD here -- its own guards (an overflow in
    // `bound - i`) record their rows in this context, at the body's end and at
    // each `continue`, one row per context the head's evaluation runs in
    // (DEF-81's rule), all at clause context 0 since the evaluation is never
    // removed. The ENTRY row, signed measures only: `E >= 0` (an unsigned
    // measure cannot go below zero and records no row); the PRESERVATION row
    // at the body block, `E' < E` over the versions at the body's end against
    // those at its start; one per `continue` (`walk_stmt`). All share the
    // loop's group and the check's trap count: two for a signed measure, one
    // for an unsigned one.
    bool:has_meas = raw enc_measure_checks(e, meas);
    Term:m0 = raw term_none();
    bool:msigned = false;
    int32:mtraps = 1i32;
    if (has_meas) {
        ExprId:me0 = raw measure_expr(raw ast_verify(e.ast, meas));
        msigned = raw type_is_signed(e.types, raw exprtypes_get(e.et, me0));
        if (msigned) { mtraps = 2i32; }
        m0 = raw enc_expr(e, me0);
        if (msigned) {
            if (m0.ok) {
                Term:nn = raw term_app2(">=", m0, raw term_lit("0", false), true);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), nn.text, nn.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, mtraps);
            } else {
                List<int32>:mnone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), "", mnone, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, mtraps);
            }
        }
    }
    drop list_push(@e.loop_meas, meas.index);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_mstart, raw term_copy(m0));
    drop list_push(@e.loop_msigned, msigned);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_sids, sid.index);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_labels, label);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_invs, inv.index);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_ckind, ctr.kind);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_cname, ctr.name);
    drop list_push(@e.loop_cstep, raw term_copy(ctr.step));
    drop list_push(@e.loop_casc, raw term_copy(ctr.asc));
    drop list_push(@e.loop_cdollar, dollar);
    drop walk_block(e, body);
    // THE PRESERVATION ROW OF THE MEASURE: the value at the body's end is below
    // the value at its start.
    if (has_meas) {
        StmtNode:mbs = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
        ExprId:me1 = raw measure_expr(raw ast_verify(e.ast, meas));
        Term:m1 = raw enc_expr(e, me1);
        if (m0.ok && m1.ok) {
            Term:lt = raw term_app2("<", m1, m0, true);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), lt.text, lt.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), body.index, mbs.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, mtraps);
        } else {
            List<int32>:pnone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), "", pnone, raw SITE_STMT(), body.index, mbs.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, mtraps);
        }
    }
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_meas));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_mstart));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_msigned));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_sids));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_labels));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_invs));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_ckind));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_cname));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_cstep));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_casc));
    discard(raw list_pop(@e.loop_cdollar));
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        StmtNode:bs = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
        // THE PRESERVATION ROW SEES THE INCREMENTED COUNTER (L-11, L-12).
        if ((ctr.kind == 2i32) || ((ctr.kind == 1i32) && ctr.ranged)) {
            drop counter_advance(e, ctr.kind, ctr.name, ctr.step, ctr.asc, dollar);
        }
        // THE HEAD CHECK RUNS HERE TOO (DEF-81, 1.5.8b step 3): the check at
        // the head is lowered once and runs at every visit, and this is the
        // context of every visit after the first -- so a guard inside a
        // clause records its row here as it does at the entry, under the
        // same clause context, and the emitter elides it only when every
        // one of its rows is discharged (`obl_finish`). This encoding was
        // QUIET until then: the entry's row alone decided a guard that runs
        // again with `$` advanced, and a verified build elided a division
        // at the head on the proof for its first visit (`inv_inner_guard`).
        int32:pctx = e.clause_ctx;
        e.clause_ctx = sid.index;
        Term:gp = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, false);
        e.clause_ctx = pctx;
        if (gp.ok) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), gp.text, gp.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), body.index, bs.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        } else {
            List<int32>:none2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), "", none2, raw SITE_STMT(), body.index, bs.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, nc);
        }
    }
    drop region_leave(e);
    drop invalidate(e, assigned);
    bool:no_break = !(raw loop_has_break(e, body, label, false, 64i32));
    // THE COUNTER AFTER THE LOOP (L-11, L-12): `$`'s exit value; a range
    // binding's fresh version exactly at its bound (`ite (< lo hi) hi lo`).
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) {
        Term:x = raw dollar_fresh(e);
        e.dollars[dollar] = raw term_copy(x);
        drop push_dollar_exit(e, ctr, x);
    }
    if ((ctr.kind == 1i32) && ctr.ranged) {
        int64:bi2 = raw bind_find(e, ctr.name);
        if (bi2 >= 0i64) {
            Term:iv2 = raw bind_term(e, bi2);
            if (iv2.ok && ctr.start.ok && ctr.limit.ok) {
                Term:xv = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
                                text: raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2("<", ctr.start.text, ctr.limit.text), ctr.limit.text, ctr.start.text),
                                syms: raw syms_union(ctr.start.syms, ctr.limit.syms) };
                Term:xe = raw term_app2("=", iv2, xv, true);
                drop hyp_push(e, xe.text, xe.syms);
            }
        }
    }
    if (nc > 0i32) {
        if (no_break) {
            e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
            Term:h2 = raw invariant_conj(e, inv, true);
            e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
            if (h2.ok) { drop hyp_push(e, h2.text, h2.syms); }
        }
    }
    // THE CONDITION IS FALSE AFTER A LOOP NOTHING `break`s OUT OF (L-4): the
    // exit is a head visit that found it false, over the post-havoc versions.
    // Encoded QUIET: its sites were recorded once, inside the body region.
    if (no_break && (!(raw expr_is_none(cond)))) {
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:wc2 = raw enc_expr(e, cond);
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (wc2.ok && wc2.is_bool) { drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app1("not", wc2.text), wc2.syms); }
    }
    if (ctr.kind == 2i32) { discard(raw list_pop(@e.dollars)); }
    pass NIL;
};

// An assignment to a NAME: the new version, defined by the operator's term
// where the operands are encodable (the compound spellings through the
// truncating definitions, P-17; a `/=` or `%=` records its division first).
// The caller records the write point AFTER this (L-7's order).
// The plain operator behind a bitwise compound assignment, or the operator itself.
func:arith_base = TokenKind(TokenKind:op) never fails {
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlusAssign)    { pass TokenKind.OpPlus; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinusAssign)   { pass TokenKind.OpMinus; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStarAssign)    { pass TokenKind.OpStar; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign)   { pass TokenKind.OpSlash; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPercentAssign) { pass TokenKind.OpPercent; }
    pass (raw bitwise_base(op));
};

func:bitwise_base = TokenKind(TokenKind:op) never fails {
    if (op == TokenKind.OpAmpAssign)   { pass TokenKind.OpAmp; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPipeAssign)  { pass TokenKind.OpPipe; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpCaretAssign) { pass TokenKind.OpCaret; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlusWrapAssign)  { pass TokenKind.OpPlusWrap; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinusWrapAssign) { pass TokenKind.OpMinusWrap; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStarWrapAssign)  { pass TokenKind.OpStarWrap; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpShlAssign)   { pass TokenKind.OpShl; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpShrAssign)   { pass TokenKind.OpShr; }
    pass op;
};

func:assign_ident = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtNode:s, TokenKind:op, ExprId:target,
                        int32:name, Term:rhs) never fails {
    // A `simd` BINDING (D-282): a plain assignment carries the value's lanes;
    // a compound one is a fresh opaque set (the elementwise operation's
    // lanes were recorded at the expression, the binding's not yet).
    int64:sb = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (sb >= 0i64) {
        int32:svt = e.binds[sb].type_id;
        if (raw is_simd(e, svt)) {
            if (op == TokenKind.OpAssign) { drop bind_lanes_assign(e, name, raw stmt_assigned(s)); pass NIL; }
            // A COMPOUND ON A `simd` BINDING (D-284, 1.5.4e step 0; DEF-39):
            // the emitter lowers `v op= w` through the vector path now, so
            // its any-lane guards have rows here as the expression form's
            // do -- at the target's site, the key the emitter elides under.
            // The binding's lanes are the current value, the right-hand
            // side's were recorded by its walk; the new set stays opaque.
            int32:selem = raw type_elem(e.types, svt);
            TokenKind:sbop = raw arith_base(op);
            if ((sbop == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (sbop == TokenKind.OpPercent)) {
                drop lanes_of_binding(e, sb, target.index);
                List<Term>:sla = raw lanes_of(e, target, svt);
                List<Term>:slb = raw lanes_of(e, raw stmt_assigned(s), svt);
                drop record_division_lanes(e, selem, sla, slb, target.index, s.span);
            }
            if ((sbop == TokenKind.OpShl) || (sbop == TokenKind.OpShr)) {
                List<Term>:slb2 = raw lanes_of(e, raw stmt_assigned(s), svt);
                drop record_shift_lanes(e, selem, slb2, target.index, s.span);
            }
            bool:sov = ((sbop == TokenKind.OpPlus) || (sbop == TokenKind.OpMinus) || (sbop == TokenKind.OpStar));
            if (sov && (raw is_int(e, selem))) {
                drop lanes_of_binding(e, sb, target.index);
                List<Term>:sla3 = raw lanes_of(e, target, svt);
                List<Term>:slb3 = raw lanes_of(e, raw stmt_assigned(s), svt);
                drop record_overflow_lanes(e, selem, raw overflow_out_lanes(e, sbop, selem, sla3, slb3, s.span),
                                           target.index, s.span);
            }
            drop bind_lanes_assign(e, name, ExprId{ index: 0i32 });
            pass NIL;
        }
    }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, rhs); pass NIL; }
    // Compound: the current value op the right-hand side.
    Term:prior = raw enc_expr(e, target);
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
    int32:lt = 0i32;
    if (bi >= 0i64) { lt = e.binds[bi].type_id; }
    // A TWISTED COMPOUND (D-278): the one twisted encoder, as `x = x op v`.
    if (raw is_twisted(e, lt)) {
        TokenKind:tbop = raw arith_base(op);
        drop bind_assign(e, name, raw enc_twisted_binary(e, tbop, lt, lt, prior, rhs, target.index, s.span));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (!(raw is_word(e, lt))) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none()); pass NIL; }
    // THE BITWISE COMPOUNDS (D-279, D-277): `x op= v` IS `x = x op v`, through
    // the one bitwise encoder -- the shift's row recorded there, the Int forms
    // and the crossing its.
    TokenKind:bop = raw bitwise_base(op);
    bool:isbit = ((bop == TokenKind.OpAmp) || (bop == TokenKind.OpPipe) || (bop == TokenKind.OpCaret));
    if ((bop == TokenKind.OpShl) || (bop == TokenKind.OpShr)) { isbit = true; }
    if (isbit) {
        drop bind_assign(e, name, raw enc_bitwise(e, bop, lt, prior, rhs, target,
                                                  raw stmt_assigned(s), target.index, s.span, true));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercentAssign)) {
        drop record_division(e, lt, prior, rhs, target.index, s.span);
        if (!(prior.ok && rhs.ok)) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none()); pass NIL; }
        if (!(raw term_is_numeral(rhs))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, lt)) {
            e.uses_sdiv = true;
            e.nonlinear = true;
            if (op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", prior, rhs, false)); }
            else { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("npk_srem", prior, rhs, false)); }
            pass NIL;
        }
        if (op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("div", prior, rhs, false)); }
        else { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("mod", prior, rhs, false)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `x +%= v`, `-%=`, `*%=` ON A PLAIN INTEGER (D-312, 1.5.8b step 4): the
    // modular term, no row and no guard.
    if (raw wrap_arith_op(raw arith_base(op))) {
        Term:wct = raw wrap_binop(e, raw arith_base(op), lt, prior, rhs);
        if (!wct.ok) { wct = raw term_opaque(e, lt); }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, move(wct));
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `x += v`, `-=`, `*=` ON A PLAIN INTEGER: the term and the `overflow`
    // row at the TARGET's site (K-9), the key the emitter guards under.
    bool:ovc = ((op == TokenKind.OpPlusAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpMinusAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpStarAssign));
    if (ovc && (raw is_int(e, lt))) {
        Term:ct = raw term_none();
        if (prior.ok && rhs.ok && (!prior.is_bool) && (!rhs.is_bool)) {
            if (op == TokenKind.OpPlusAssign)  { ct = raw term_app2("+", prior, rhs, false); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpMinusAssign) { ct = raw term_app2("-", prior, rhs, false); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpStarAssign) {
                if (!((raw term_is_numeral(prior)) || (raw term_is_numeral(rhs)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
                ct = raw term_app2("*", prior, rhs, false);
            }
        }
        drop record_overflow(e, lt, ct, target.index, s.span);
        drop bind_assign(e, name, move(ct));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (!(prior.ok && rhs.ok)) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none()); pass NIL; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlusAssign)  { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("+", prior, rhs, false)); pass NIL; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinusAssign) { drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("-", prior, rhs, false)); pass NIL; }
    if (op == TokenKind.OpStarAssign) {
        if (!((raw term_is_numeral(prior)) || (raw term_is_numeral(rhs)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_app2("*", prior, rhs, false));
        pass NIL;
    }
    drop bind_assign(e, name, raw term_none());
    pass NIL;
};

func:term_copy = Term(Term:t) never fails {
    List<int32>:s = raw list_init::<int32>(t.syms.count + 1i64);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...t.syms.count) { drop list_push(@s, t.syms[i]); }
    pass Term{ ok: t.ok, is_bool: t.is_bool, text: string_concat(t.text, ""), syms: move(s) };
};

// --- the expression walk -------------------------------------------------------------------

// The child expressions of a node, by kind -- ONE place knows the layouts
// (AST_REFERENCE §3; the parser's construction sites). A kind not listed here
// has no expression children the walk can see, which for a kind that DOES
// have some would be a missed site: the harness's every-guard-has-a-row
// cross-check is what catches that class.
func:expr_children = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprNode:n, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    ExprKind:k = n.kind;
    if ((k == ExprKind.ExprBinaryExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprSafeUnwrapExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprNullCoalesceExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprDefaultsExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprPipeExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprResultLiteralExpr)) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        if (n.b != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.b); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprTernaryExpr) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        if (n.b != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.b); }
        if (n.c != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.c); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((k == ExprKind.ExprUnaryExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprPostfixExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprSpreadExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprIsErrExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprComptimeExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprDropExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprDynCastExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprAwaitExpr)) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) {
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        int32:g = raw expr_generic_count(n);
        for (int32:i in g...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        // A NAMESPACE CALL'S RECEIVER (D-273, 1.5.4c) names a module and is
        // still pushed: a walk for SITES finds none in an identifier or in a
        // path of member accesses, and the term is discarded. (Threading the
        // node's id through here to skip it moved this function's own
        // `div-min` row in `nitpick.obligations` -- a parameter is a symbol
        // of the encoding -- which 1.5.4c must not do.)
        if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
        for (int32:i2 in 0i32...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i2)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        int32:g2 = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
        for (int32:i3 in g2...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i3)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if ((k == ExprKind.ExprArrayLiteralExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprTemplateLiteral)
        || (k == ExprKind.ExprVectorCtorExpr) || (k == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr)) {
        if (k == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
            // a value-pick's arms are statements; its selector is the one expression
            if (n.a != 0i32) { drop list_push(out, n.a); }
            pass NIL;
        }
        for (int32:i4 in 0i32...n.c) { drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, i4)); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (k == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:pairs = n.c / 2i32;
        for (int32:i5 in 0i32...pairs) {
            drop list_push(out, raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, (i5 * 2i32) + 1i32));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Walk the children for sites only; the value is opaque.
func:walk_children = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprNode:n) never fails {
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) {
        Term:t = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: kids[i] });
    }
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:enc_expr = Term(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    int32:ty = raw ty_of(e, id);

    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) {
        if (raw is_twisted(e, ty)) { pass (raw twisted_int_literal(e, n.payload, ty)); }
        if (!(raw is_int(e, ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, ty)) { pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(n.payload), false)); }
        pass (raw term_lit(raw u64_decimal(n.payload =>! uint64), false));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBoolLiteral) {
        if (n.payload != 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
        pass (raw term_lit("false", true));
    }
    // A `tfp`/`dim256` literal in the fractional form (D-278); a float's
    // literal has no term until step 3.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprFloatLiteral) {
        if (raw is_twisted(e, ty)) {
            pass (raw twisted_text_literal(e, raw intern_get(e.interns, n.payload =>! int32), ty));
        }
        if (raw is_float(e, ty)) {
            pass (raw fp_literal(e, raw intern_get(e.interns, n.payload =>! int32), ty));
        }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    // `ERR` (D-008) at a twisted type is the sentinel; `NIL`, `NULL` and an
    // aggregate family's ERR (a `complex`, a `frac`) have no term.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSentinelLiteral) {
        if ((n.payload >= 2i64) && (raw is_twisted(e, ty))) { pass (raw term_lit(raw tw_min(e, ty), false)); }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
        int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, n.payload =>! int32);
        if (bi >= 0i64) {
            // A `simd` binding's read: its lane symbols (D-282), no scalar term.
            if (e.binds[bi].lanes.count > 0i64) {
                drop lanes_of_binding(e, bi, id.index);
                pass (raw term_none());
            }
            // UNDER `old(...)` (D-243): the binding's entry version.
            int32:want = e.binds[bi].sym;
            if (e.at_entry) { want = e.binds[bi].entry; }
            if (want >= 0i32) {
                int32:si = want;
                List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop list_push(@one, si);
                pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms[si => int64].is_bool,
                           text: raw sym_text(e, si), syms: move(one) };
            }
        }
        // A `fixed` GLOBAL IS ITS CONSTANT (1.5.4b step 1): the folder's value
        // as a numeral wherever it is read, so a flag member or a named mask
        // takes the Int forms of D-279. A local the folder cannot fold (every
        // local) answers nothing here, and the read stays opaque.
        if ((raw is_word(e, ty)) && (bi < 0i64)) {
            ConstVal:gcv = raw fold_const(e.tr, id, e.scope);
            if (gcv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) { pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(gcv.num), false)); }
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBinaryExpr) {
        TokenKind:op = raw expr_op(n);
        Term:a = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        // THE RIGHT-HAND SIDE OF `&&`/`||` IS AN ARM (1.5.4 step 2, L-10): it
        // runs only when the left decided nothing, so its sites and its
        // symbols live under `a` (or `(not a)`), in a region of their own
        // whose facts come back guarded.
        Term:b = raw term_none();
        if (((op == TokenKind.OpAndAnd) || (op == TokenKind.OpOrOr)) && a.ok && a.is_bool) {
            Term:ac = raw term_copy(a);
            if (op == TokenKind.OpOrOr) {
                ac = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", a.text),
                           syms: raw syms_union(a.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
            }
            drop region_enter_cond(e, ac);
            drop hyp_push(e, ac.text, ac.syms);
            b = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(n));
            drop region_leave(e);
        } else {
            b = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(n));
        }
        int32:lt = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        if ((op == TokenKind.OpAndAnd) || (op == TokenKind.OpOrOr)) {
            if (a.ok && b.ok && a.is_bool && b.is_bool) {
                if (op == TokenKind.OpAndAnd) { pass (raw term_app2("and", a, b, true)); }
                pass (raw term_app2("or", a, b, true));
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        // A WORD'S BITWISE OPERATORS (D-279, D-280; a flag family's `|`/`&`
        // too): the Int forms, the bounded crossing, the shift's row.
        if (raw is_word(e, lt)) {
            bool:bitop = ((op == TokenKind.OpAmp) || (op == TokenKind.OpPipe) || (op == TokenKind.OpCaret));
            if ((op == TokenKind.OpShl) || (op == TokenKind.OpShr)) { bitop = true; }
            if (bitop) {
                pass (raw enc_bitwise(e, op, lt, a, b, raw expr_lhs(n), raw expr_rhs(n), id.index, n.span, true));
            }
            if ((raw type_kind(e.types, lt)) == (raw TY_FLAGS())) {
                if (a.ok && b.ok && (!a.is_bool) && (!b.is_bool)) {
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
                }
                pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
            }
        }
        // A FLOAT OPERAND (D-281): the IEEE operations and the ordered
        // predicates, no row (floats never trap).
        if (raw is_float(e, lt)) {
            pass (raw enc_float_binary(e, op, lt, ty, a, b));
        }
        // A TWISTED OPERAND (D-278): the operations as the emitter's `ite`
        // shapes, a comparison the `err-exit` row.
        if (raw is_twisted(e, lt)) {
            pass (raw enc_twisted_binary(e, op, lt, ty, a, b, id.index, n.span));
        }
        if (raw is_int(e, lt)) {
            bool:divlike = ((op == TokenKind.OpSlash) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercent));
            if (divlike) {
                drop record_division(e, lt, a, b, id.index, n.span);
                if (!(a.ok && b.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
                if (!(raw term_is_numeral(b))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
                if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, lt)) {
                    e.uses_sdiv = true;
                    e.nonlinear = true;
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { pass (raw term_app2("npk_sdiv", a, b, false)); }
                    pass (raw term_app2("npk_srem", a, b, false));
                }
                if (op == TokenKind.OpSlash) { pass (raw term_app2("div", a, b, false)); }
                pass (raw term_app2("mod", a, b, false));
            }
            // THE WRAPPING FAMILY (D-312, 1.5.8b step 4): the exact modular
            // term, no row and no guard -- and the folder's constant where the
            // node has one, as the trapping twins take theirs.
            if (raw wrap_arith_op(op)) {
                ConstVal:wcv = raw fold_node_constant(e.tr, id, e.scope, ty);
                if (wcv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) {
                    pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(wcv.num), false));
                }
                Term:wt = raw wrap_binop(e, op, ty, a, b);
                if (!wt.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
                pass wt;
            }
            // `+ - *`: the term, and the `overflow` row at the guard's site --
            // none where the node is written as its constant (step 2, no guard).
            bool:ovop = ((op == TokenKind.OpPlus) || (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) || (op == TokenKind.OpStar));
            if (ovop) {
                ConstVal:bcv = raw fold_node_constant(e.tr, id, e.scope, ty);
                if (bcv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) {
                    pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(bcv.num), false));
                }
                Term:bt = raw term_none();
                if (a.ok && b.ok && (!a.is_bool) && (!b.is_bool)) {
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpPlus)  { bt = raw term_app2("+", a, b, false); }
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpMinus) { bt = raw term_app2("-", a, b, false); }
                    if (op == TokenKind.OpStar) {
                        if (!((raw term_is_numeral(a)) || (raw term_is_numeral(b)))) { e.nonlinear = true; }
                        bt = raw term_app2("*", a, b, false);
                    }
                }
                drop record_overflow(e, ty, bt, id.index, n.span);
                if (!bt.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
                pass bt;
            }
            if (!(a.ok && b.ok)) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            if (a.is_bool || b.is_bool) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpLt)    { pass (raw term_app2("<", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpLtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("<=", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpGt)    { pass (raw term_app2(">", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpGtEq)  { pass (raw term_app2(">=", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
            if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        if (raw is_bool(e, lt)) {
            if (a.ok && b.ok && a.is_bool && b.is_bool) {
                if (op == TokenKind.OpEqEq)  { pass (raw term_app2("=", a, b, true)); }
                if (op == TokenKind.OpNotEq) { pass (raw term_app2("distinct", a, b, true)); }
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        if (lt != 0i32) {
            int32:lk = raw type_kind(e.types, lt);
            // A `simd` OPERATION (D-282): the lanes, and the any-lane rows.
            if (lk == (raw TY_SIMD())) {
                drop enc_simd_binary(e, op, lt, id, raw expr_lhs(n), raw expr_rhs(n), n.span);
            }
            // A `frac` or a tfp-element `complex` comparison traps on ERR too
            // (D-198, D-199), over an aggregate the walk has no term for: its
            // `err-exit` row is `unencoded` (L-6).
            if (((lk == (raw TY_FRAC())) || (lk == (raw TY_COMPLEX()))) && (raw tw_is_cmp(op))) {
                bool:taints = true;
                if (lk == (raw TY_COMPLEX())) {
                    taints = ((raw type_kind(e.types, raw type_elem(e.types, lt))) == (raw TY_TFP()));
                }
                if (taints) { drop record_unencoded_err_exit(e, id.index, n.span); }
            }
        }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUnaryExpr) {
        TokenKind:uop = raw expr_op(n);
        Term:o = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        // AN INTEGER NEGATION IS `0 - x` AND ITS GUARD'S ROW (1.5.8b step 3),
        // at the unary node's own site (K-9) -- none where it is written as its
        // constant, `unencoded` where the operand has no term.
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpMinus) && (raw is_int(e, ty))) {
            ConstVal:ucv = raw fold_node_constant(e.tr, id, e.scope, ty);
            if (ucv.kind == (raw CV_INT())) { pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(ucv.num), false)); }
            Term:ut = raw term_none();
            if (o.ok && (!o.is_bool)) { ut = raw term_app2("-", raw term_lit("0", false), o, false); }
            drop record_overflow(e, ty, ut, id.index, n.span);
            if (!ut.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
            pass ut;
        }
        if (!o.ok) { pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty)); }
        // A float negation is `fneg` (D-143): `fp.neg`, exact.
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpMinus) && (raw is_float(e, ty)) && (!o.is_bool)) {
            pass (raw fp_make(e, "neg", ty, o.text, "", raw smt_app1("fp.neg", o.text), o.syms));
        }
        // A twisted negation (D-008): ERR in, ERR out; `0 - x` is in range
        // for every valid `x`, the valid range being symmetric.
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpMinus) && (raw is_twisted(e, ty)) && (!o.is_bool)) {
            string:tmn = raw tw_min(e, ty);
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false,
                       text: raw smt_app3("ite", raw smt_app2("=", o.text, tmn), tmn, raw smt_app2("-", "0", o.text)),
                       syms: raw syms_union(o.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpBang) && o.is_bool) {
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", o.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(o.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        // `~x` IN Int (D-279): `-x - 1` on a signed word, `2^W - 1 - x` on an
        // unsigned one -- the complement is arithmetic, no crossing needed.
        if ((uop == TokenKind.OpTilde) && (raw is_word(e, ty)) && (!o.is_bool)) {
            if (raw word_signed(e, ty)) {
                string:neg = raw smt_app1("-", o.text);
                pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app2("-", neg, "1"),
                           syms: raw syms_union(o.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
            }
            string:top = raw pow2_minus_one_decimal((raw word_bits(e, ty)) => int64);
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app2("-", top, o.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(o.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprTernaryExpr) {
        // THE TWO BRANCHES ARE ARMS (L-10): each under its condition, in a
        // region of its own (the emitter runs only the taken one, D-145).
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        bool:tc = c.ok && c.is_bool;
        Term:nc = raw term_none();
        if (tc) {
            nc = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", c.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(c.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        if (tc) { drop region_enter_cond(e, c); drop hyp_push(e, c.text, c.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        Term:t1 = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.b });
        drop region_leave(e);
        if (tc) { drop region_enter_cond(e, nc); drop hyp_push(e, nc.text, nc.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        Term:t2 = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.c });
        drop region_leave(e);
        if (c.ok && t1.ok && t2.ok && c.is_bool && (t1.is_bool == t2.is_bool)) {
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: t1.is_bool,
                       text: raw smt_app3("ite", c.text, t1.text, t2.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(c.syms, raw syms_union(t1.syms, t2.syms)) };
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCastExpr) {
        // `=>` between integers is value-preserving by the checker's own rule
        // (a lossy `=>` is refused), so the term is the operand's.
        Term:ct = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        int32:st = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (ct.ok && (raw is_int(e, st)) && (raw is_int(e, ty)) && (!ct.is_bool)) { pass ct; }
        Term:fw = raw flag_word_cast(e, ct, st, ty);
        if (fw.ok) { pass fw; }
        Term:tw = raw twisted_cast(e, ct, st, ty, false, id.index, n.span);
        if (tw.ok) { pass tw; }
        // A FLOAT LEAVING TO AN INTEGER IS A GUARD (D-306): its row here, its
        // value opaque -- the truncation is not a term the fragment holds.
        if ((raw is_float(e, st)) && (raw is_int(e, ty))) {
            drop record_cast_range(e, ct, st, ty, id.index, n.span);
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        Term:fc = raw float_cast(e, ct, st, ty);
        if (fc.ok) { pass fc; }
        // An elementwise `simd` cast (D-282): the scalar cast per lane.
        if ((raw is_simd(e, st)) && (raw is_simd(e, ty))) {
            drop enc_simd_cast(e, raw expr_operand(n), st, ty, id.index, false);
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `=>!` (1.5.4b step 1): a flag word and its `int32` carrier are one bit
    // pattern -- the word re-signed one way, the int re-signed the other; a
    // float leaving to an integer is a `cast-range` row (D-306, 1.5.8b step
    // 5), and every other unchecked cast stays opaque.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUncheckedCastExpr) {
        Term:ut = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        int32:ust = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        Term:fw2 = raw flag_word_cast(e, ut, ust, ty);
        if (fw2.ok) { pass fw2; }
        Term:tw2 = raw twisted_cast(e, ut, ust, ty, true, id.index, n.span);
        if (tw2.ok) { pass tw2; }
        if ((raw is_float(e, ust)) && (raw is_int(e, ty))) {
            drop record_cast_range(e, ut, ust, ty, id.index, n.span);
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        Term:fc2 = raw float_cast(e, ut, ust, ty);
        if (fc2.ok) { pass fc2; }
        if ((raw is_simd(e, ust)) && (raw is_simd(e, ty))) {
            drop enc_simd_cast(e, raw expr_operand(n), ust, ty, id.index, true);
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `is_err(x)` (D-008 section 5) on a twisted value is `(= x MIN)`; on a
    // `frac` or a `complex` the look is opaque (their ERR is a pair, L-6).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIsErrExpr) {
        Term:iet = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        int32:iety = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (iet.ok && (!iet.is_bool) && (raw is_twisted(e, iety))) {
            pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app2("=", iet.text, raw tw_min(e, iety)),
                       syms: raw syms_union(iet.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMoveExpr) {
        Term:mt = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (mt.ok) { pass mt; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `$` -- THE RULE'S SUBJECT (1.5.2 step 3, L-8): inside `enc_rule` it is
    // the term the rule is being instantiated over; outside one it is the
    // innermost counted loop's counter (1.5.4 step 3, L-11): its start at
    // the entry row, a fresh in-range symbol in the body, the incremented
    // value at the preservation and `continue` rows, the exit value after.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIterationVarExpr) {
        if (e.subject.ok) { pass (raw term_copy(e.subject)); }
        if (e.dollars.count > 0i64) {
            Term:top = raw term_copy(e.dollars[e.dollars.count - 1i64]);
            if (top.ok) { pass top; }
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // A CALL (1.5.2 step 3, L-10; 1.5.3 step 2, D-268): the receiver and
    // every argument are sites, encoded ONCE; a callee the checker recorded
    // gets its `limit-subsume` row and its `requires` row over the argument
    // terms; the value -- a `Result`, or a bare value nothing unwrapped -- is
    // opaque. The unwrap arms below are where a known callee's value becomes
    // an uninterpreted function and its `ensures` becomes knowledge.
    // `v.sum()`/`.min()`/`.max()`/`.all()`/`.any()` on a `simd` (D-282): the
    // receiver walked, the lanes folded in the emitter's order.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr) {
        int32:mrt = raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        if ((raw is_simd(e, mrt)) && (n.c == 0i32)) {
            string:mname = raw intern_get(e.interns, n.payload =>! int32);
            if (raw simd_own_method(mname)) {
                Term:mrecv = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
                pass (raw enc_simd_method(e, mname, ExprId{ index: n.a }, mrt, ty, id.index, n.span));
            }
        }
    }
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr)) {
        CallEnc:ce = raw enc_call(e, id, n);
        drop record_call_rows(e, id, n, ce);
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `result` (D-245): the value being passed, while an `ensures` is
    // encoded at a seam; `old(e)` (D-243): the operand over the entry
    // versions. Outside those contexts each is opaque -- and the checker
    // admits them nowhere else.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprResultValueExpr) {
        if (e.result.ok) { pass (raw term_copy(e.result)); }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprOldExpr) {
        bool:saved_entry = e.at_entry;
        e.at_entry = true;
        Term:ot = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        e.at_entry = saved_entry;
        if (ot.ok) { pass ot; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // AN UNWRAP THAT CONTINUES ONLY ON SUCCESS (1.5.3 step 2, L-3, L-4):
    // `raw f(...)`, `f(...) ?! E`, `relay f(...)`, each over a plain or an
    // awaited call. The call's rows are recorded as above; the VALUE is an
    // uninterpreted function application when the callee is `pure never
    // fails` over the fragment (a `raw` call: equal inputs, equal outputs,
    // D-242), else a fresh opaque symbol; and the callee's `ensures` is
    // pushed as a hypothesis over the arguments and that value -- sound
    // because the callee's seam guards or proves it before any continuing
    // execution reaches here. `?|` pushes nothing: its value may be the
    // default.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr)
        || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRelayExpr)) {
        ExprId:inner = ExprId{ index: n.a };
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(inner))) {
            ExprNode:inn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, inner);
            if (inn.kind == ExprKind.ExprAwaitExpr) {
                inner = ExprId{ index: inn.a };
                if (!(raw expr_is_none(inner))) { inn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, inner); }
            }
            if ((!(raw expr_is_none(inner)))
                && ((inn.kind == ExprKind.ExprCallExpr) || (inn.kind == ExprKind.ExprMethodCallExpr))) {
                CallEnc:uce = raw enc_call(e, inner, inn);
                drop record_call_rows(e, inner, inn, uce);
                if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr) {
                    Term:eb = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.b });
                }
                Term:val = raw term_none();
                if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprRawUnwrapExpr) { val = raw uf_value(e, uce, ty); }
                if (!val.ok) { val = raw term_opaque(e, ty); }
                drop push_callee_ensures(e, uce, val);
                pass val;
            }
        }
        drop walk_children(e, n);
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // A PICK EXPRESSION (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): the selector a site, every
    // arm walked as the statement form's (their guard sites, their bodies'
    // sites and definitions, in regions of their own), the names the arms
    // assign invalidated after; the value opaque until 1.5.4 step 2.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        drop record_checker(e, raw OK_EXHAUSTIVE(), raw SITE_EXPR(), id.index, n.span);
        Term:psel = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: n.a });
        Term:pval = raw walk_pick_arms(e, n.b, n.c, psel, raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: n.a }), true);
        if (pval.ok && (pval.is_bool == (raw is_bool(e, ty))) && (raw is_termed(e, ty))) { pass pval; }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // `simd(a, ...)` (D-282): the lanes are the arguments' terms, a splat's
    // one term N times; `complex(re, im)` shares the node and stays opaque.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprVectorCtorExpr) {
        if ((((n.payload =>! int32) =>! TokenKind) != TokenKind.KwComplex) && (raw is_simd(e, ty))) {
            int32:velem = raw type_elem(e.types, ty);
            int32:vlanes = (raw tt_get(e.types, ty)).b;
            int32:vcnt = raw expr_list_count(n);
            int32:vstart = raw expr_list_start(n);
            List<Term>:vout = raw list_init::<Term>((vlanes => int64) + 1i64);
            if (vcnt == 1i32) {
                Term:one = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, vstart, 0i32) });
                if (!one.ok) { one = raw term_opaque(e, velem); }
                for (int32:vi in 0i32...vlanes) { drop list_push(@vout, raw term_copy(one)); }
            } else {
                for (int32:vj in 0i32...vlanes) {
                    Term:lt2 = raw term_none();
                    if (vj < vcnt) { lt2 = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, vstart, vj) }); }
                    if (!lt2.ok) { lt2 = raw term_opaque(e, velem); }
                    drop list_push(@vout, move(lt2));
                }
            }
            drop lanes_put(e, id.index, move(vout));
            pass (raw term_none());
        }
    }
    // `v[i]` on a `simd` with a numeral index is the lane's term (D-282); a
    // computed index is opaque (its bounds row is 1.5.8's).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        int32:ibt = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        if (raw is_simd(e, ibt)) {
            Term:ibase = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
            Term:iix = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(n));
            int32:ielem = raw type_elem(e.types, ibt);
            // THE LANE'S OWN `bounds` ROW (1.5.8b step 5): the emitter guards a
            // lane place against the LANE COUNT, which is the type's own
            // constant -- so a numeral index discharges outright and a
            // computed one decides against whatever bounds the path gives it.
            // This arm returns before the general element arm below, so the
            // row has to be recorded here: without it the guard was a trap the
            // belts could not account for (three verify programs, caught by
            // step 5's own full harness).
            drop record_bounds(e, iix,
                               raw term_lit(int_to_string(((raw tt_get(e.types, ibt)).b) => int64), false),
                               (raw expr_rhs(n)).index, n.span);
            NumVal:ik = raw numeral_of(e, iix, raw expr_rhs(n));
            if (ik.ok && (ik.v >= 0i64) && (ik.v < (((raw tt_get(e.types, ibt)).b) => int64))) {
                List<Term>:il = raw lanes_of(e, raw expr_lhs(n), ibt);
                if (ik.v < il.count) { pass (raw term_copy(il[ik.v])); }
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ielem));
        }
    }
    // `v.len` on a `simd` is its lane count (D-282).
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
        int32:mbt = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if ((raw is_simd(e, mbt)) && (raw string_eq(raw intern_get(e.interns, n.payload =>! int32), "len"))) {
            Term:mbase = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
            pass (raw term_lit(int_to_string(((raw tt_get(e.types, mbt)).b) => int64), false));
        }
    }
    // AN ELEMENT READ (D-286, 1.5.5 step 2): the base and the index are
    // sites, the index's term is memoised for the `disjoint` rows, and the
    // access is a guard site when the aliasing analysis marked it. The
    // element's `bounds` row is recorded here since 1.5.8b step 5, at the
    // INDEX EXPRESSION's site -- the emitter's own key -- against the
    // container's length term; a range view's ONE row is the pair's. The
    // value read out stays opaque: what an element HOLDS is nobody's fact.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
        int32:bty2 = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        Term:ibase = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(n));
        ExprNode:rn2 = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw expr_rhs(n));
        if (rn2.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) {
            Term:rlo = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(rn2));
            Term:rhi = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(rn2));
            if (rn2.payload == 1i64) {
                if (rhi.ok && (!rhi.is_bool)) {
                    rhi = raw term_app2("+", rhi, raw term_lit("1", false), false);
                }
            }
            Term:rlen = raw term_none();
            if ((raw has_len_term(e, bty2)) || (raw type_is_list(e.tr, bty2))) {
                rlen = raw place_len_term(e, raw expr_lhs(n), bty2);
            }
            drop record_bounds_range(e, rlo, rhi, rlen, (raw expr_rhs(n)).index, n.span);
            drop enc_alias_site(e, id);
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        Term:iidx = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(n));
        drop memo_put(e, (raw expr_rhs(n)).index, iidx);
        Term:ilen = raw term_none();
        if ((raw has_len_term(e, bty2)) || (raw type_is_list(e.tr, bty2))) {
            ilen = raw place_len_term(e, raw expr_lhs(n), bty2);
        }
        // A POINTER's element has no bound at all (D-038: pointers are thin),
        // and the emitter guards nothing there -- so no row either.
        if ((raw type_kind(e.types, bty2)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) {
            drop record_bounds(e, iidx, ilen, (raw expr_rhs(n)).index, n.span);
        }
        drop enc_alias_site(e, id);
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // A FIELD READ: the base a site, the access a guard site when marked.
    // A CONTAINER'S LENGTH IS THE SAME TERM ITS `bounds` ROWS COMPARE AGAINST
    // (1.5.8b step 5): `.len` on a slice, a `string`, a `cstring` or a
    // `buffer`, and `.count` on a `List`, are `(|npk.len| base)` -- so a loop
    // written over the length bounds the index by the row's own symbol. A
    // fixed array's `.len` is its type's constant (DEF-22). `.cap` and
    // `.ptr` stay opaque: neither bounds anything.
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr)) {
        Term:mbase2 = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        int32:mbt2 = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        string:mfld = raw intern_get(e.interns, n.payload =>! int32);
        bool:mlen = ((raw string_eq(mfld, "len")) && (raw has_len_term(e, mbt2)));
        if ((raw string_eq(mfld, "count")) && (raw type_is_list(e.tr, mbt2))) { mlen = true; }
        if (mlen) {
            Term:lt2 = raw place_len_term(e, raw expr_operand(n), mbt2);
            if (lt2.ok) {
                // A `List`'s `count` is limited (`ListLen`, D-308 SS6): the rule
                // over the length SYMBOL, at this read, as at every read.
                if (raw type_is_list(e.tr, mbt2)) {
                    drop assert_field_rule(e, mbt2, n.payload =>! int32, lt2);
                }
                drop enc_alias_site(e, id);
                pass lt2;
            }
        }
        drop enc_alias_site(e, id);
        // A BUILT-IN LENGTH OR CAPACITY READ OFF ANYTHING ELSE -- a call's
        // result, an element, an escaped name, a container behind a POINTER
        // (`b.cap` on a `buffer->`: D-098 dereferences the read, so the
        // operand's type is the pointer's) -- is opaque, and bounded by the
        // ceiling (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step 6c).
        int32:mvt = mbt2;
        if ((raw type_kind(e.types, mvt)) == (raw TY_POINTER())) { mvt = raw type_elem(e.types, mvt); }
        if ((raw has_len_term(e, mvt)) && ((raw string_eq(mfld, "len")) || (raw string_eq(mfld, "cap")))) {
            Term:mo2 = raw term_opaque(e, ty);
            drop push_len_fact(e, mo2);
            pass mo2;
        }
        // A LIMITED FIELD'S RULE IS A FACT AT EVERY READ (D-308 SS3; 1.5.8b
        // step 6): the read's own opaque term satisfies the rule, because
        // every write to the field was checked against it (or discharged
        // under these same hypotheses) and the vacant value was proven to
        // satisfy it at the declaration (TYPE-077). That is what lets a row
        // over `l.count - 1` decide where a bare opaque term could not.
        Term:mo = raw term_opaque(e, ty);
        drop assert_field_rule(e, mbt2, n.payload =>! int32, mo);
        pass mo;
    }
    // `#sqrt(x)` (D-200) is the instruction, `fp.sqrt RNE` (D-281); every
    // other builtin's value is opaque, its arguments sites.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBuiltinExpr) {
        string:bname = raw intern_get(e.interns, raw builtin_name(n));
        if ((raw string_eq(bname, "sqrt")) && (raw is_float(e, ty)) && (n.c > (raw builtin_generic_count(n)))) {
            Term:sq = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), raw builtin_generic_count(n)) });
            if (!sq.ok) { sq = raw term_opaque(e, ty); }
            if (sq.ok && (!sq.is_bool)) {
                pass (raw fp_make(e, "sqrt", ty, sq.text, "", raw smt_app2("fp.sqrt", "RNE", sq.text), sq.syms));
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
        // `#wild_slice<T>(p, len)` (D-308 SS7, 1.5.8b step 6c): the pointer a
        // site, the count the ceiling's `bounds` row at the builtin's own node.
        if (raw builtin_caller_len(bname)) {
            int32:wg = raw builtin_generic_count(n);
            if (n.c > (wg + 1i32)) {
                Term:wp = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), wg) });
                Term:wl = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw expr_list_start(n), wg + 1i32) });
                drop record_len_ceiling(e, wl, id.index, n.span);
            }
            pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
        }
    }
    // A STRUCT LITERAL IS A WRITE POINT FOR EVERY LIMITED FIELD IT NAMES
    // (D-308 SS2, 1.5.8b step 6): each value encoded once, its row recorded at
    // the VALUE expression's site -- the emitter's own key, which checks the
    // value in register before it enters the aggregate. The literal's own
    // value stays opaque.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprStructLiteralExpr) {
        int32:lpairs = n.c / 2i32;
        for (int32:li in 0i32...lpairs) {
            int32:lfn = raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, li * 2i32);
            ExprId:lvid = ExprId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, n.b, (li * 2i32) + 1i32) };
            Term:lv = raw enc_expr(e, lvid);
            drop record_field_limit(e, ty, lfn, lv, lvid.index, n.span);
        }
        pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
    }
    // Everything else: the value is opaque, the children are still sites.
    drop walk_children(e, n);
    pass (raw term_opaque(e, ty));
};

// --- the statement walk --------------------------------------------------------------------

// Names an assignment statement inside `sid` targets (recursively), so a
// construct's exit can invalidate exactly what it may have changed.
func:collect_assigned = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, List<int32>->:out) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    // THE STATEMENT'S EXPRESSIONS FIRST (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): a pick
    // EXPRESSION's arms are statements that assign, and they sit inside an
    // initialiser, a right-hand side, an operand -- `stmt_expr_ids` is the
    // one enumeration of where.
    List<int32>:xs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop stmt_expr_ids(e.ast, s, @xs);
    for (int64:xi in 0i64...xs.count) {
        drop collect_assigned_expr(e, ExprId{ index: xs[xi] }, out, 64i32);
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        ExprNode:t = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw stmt_target(s));
        if (t.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { drop list_push(out, t.payload =>! int32); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop collect_assigned(e, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) }, out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_then(s), out);
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_else(s), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), out); pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), out); pass NIL; }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), out);
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), out);
        drop collect_assigned(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            drop collect_assigned(e, raw arm_body(arm), out);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        drop collect_assigned(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index }, out);
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// A PICK EXPRESSION'S ARMS assign like a statement's (DEF-26): every arm's
// body collected, its guard and the selector searched for nested ones.
func:collect_assigned_expr = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, List<int32>->:out, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...n.c) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, n.b, a));
            drop collect_assigned_expr(e, raw arm_guard(arm), out, fuel - 1i32);
            drop collect_assigned(e, raw arm_body(arm), out);
        }
    }
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) {
        drop collect_assigned_expr(e, ExprId{ index: kids[i] }, out, fuel - 1i32);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The root name of a place (`x`, `x.f`, `x[i]`, …), or 0.
func:place_root_name = int32(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    ExprId:cur = id;
    int32:fuel = 64i32;
    while (fuel > 0i32) decreases fuel {
        fuel = fuel - 1i32;
        if (raw expr_is_none(cur)) { pass 0i32; }
        ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, cur);
        if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) { pass (n.payload =>! int32); }
        if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr)
            || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprSafeNavExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprDerefExpr)) {
            cur = ExprId{ index: n.a };
            continue;
        }
        pass 0i32;
    }
    pass 0i32;
};

// Every name whose address is taken (`@x`, `$$m x`, `$$i x`, through any
// place path) anywhere under `id`.
func:collect_escaped_expr = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass NIL; }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if ((n.kind == ExprKind.ExprAddressOfExpr) || (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBorrowExpr)) {
        int32:root = raw place_root_name(e, raw expr_operand(n));
        if (root != 0i32) { drop list_push(@e.escaped, root); }
    }
    // A PICK EXPRESSION's arms are statements (DEF-26): walked as a statement's.
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprPickExpr) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...n.c) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, n.b, a));
            drop collect_escaped_expr(e, raw arm_guard(arm));
            drop collect_escaped(e, raw arm_body(arm));
        }
    }
    List<int32>:kids = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop expr_children(e, n, @kids);
    for (int64:i in 0i64...kids.count) { drop collect_escaped_expr(e, ExprId{ index: kids[i] }); }
    pass NIL;
};

func:collect_escaped = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    // THE EXPRESSIONS THROUGH THE ONE ENUMERATION (DEF-26), then the bodies.
    List<int32>:xs = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
    drop stmt_expr_ids(e.ast, s, @xs);
    for (int64:xi in 0i64...xs.count) { drop collect_escaped_expr(e, ExprId{ index: xs[xi] }); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            drop collect_escaped(e, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) });
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_then(s));
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_else(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s)); pass NIL; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) { drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s)); pass NIL; }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s));
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s));
        drop collect_escaped(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            drop collect_escaped(e, raw arm_body(arm));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        drop collect_escaped(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index });
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Register a pattern's bindings as symbol-less bindings for the arm's scope.
func:bind_pattern = NIL(Encoder->:e, PatNode:p) never fails {
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatStructDestructure) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw pat_bind_count(p))) {
            Bind:b = Bind{ name: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw pat_bind_start(p), i), sym: 0i32 - 1i32, type_id: 0i32, rule: 0i32, entry: 0i32 - 1i32, lanes: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64), lensym: 0i32 };
            drop list_push(@e.binds, move(b));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatEnumDestructure) {
        for (int32:j in 0i32...(raw pat_enum_bind_count(e.ast, p))) {
            Bind:b2 = Bind{ name: raw pat_enum_bind(e.ast, p, j), sym: 0i32 - 1i32, type_id: 0i32, rule: 0i32, entry: 0i32 - 1i32, lanes: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64), lensym: 0i32 };
            drop list_push(@e.binds, move(b2));
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE ARMS OF A `pick`, EITHER FORM (DEF-26, 1.5.4 step 0): each in a region
// of its own with its pattern's names bound symbol-less, its guard a site,
// its body walked, the bindings restored between arms. The statement form
// had this inline since 1.5.0; the expression form's arms were never walked,
// so a guard site inside one had no row (P-12 broken) -- one helper, both
// spellings (1.5.2c's lesson).
//
// THE ARMS' CONDITIONS (1.5.4 step 1, L-3): a value pattern is `(= sel v)`,
// a range `(and (<= lo sel) (< sel hi))` (`<=` when inclusive), a wildcard
// the negation of every arm before it when each has a condition; a
// destructure, an ERR pattern, a selector outside the fragment: none. Inside
// arm i's region its own condition holds and, since arms are tried in
// order, so does the negation of every earlier arm's. A `where` guard is a
// fact inside its arm once encoded there (it ran only when the pattern
// matched). When ANY arm carries a guard, only each arm's own pattern is
// pushed -- a guarded arm's failure is not something the patterns alone
// express -- and when a `fall` sits anywhere in the pick, no arm gets a
// condition at all: a target arm is entered from another arm.
func:walk_pick_arms = Term(Encoder->:e, int32:start, int32:count, Term:sel, int32:sel_ty, bool:want_value) never fails {
    bool:any_guard = false;
    bool:any_fall = false;
    for (int32:a0 in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm0 = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a0));
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(raw arm_guard(arm0)))) { any_guard = true; }
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw arm_body(arm0), 64i32)) { any_fall = true; }
    }
    bool:sel_ok = sel.ok;
    if (any_fall) { sel_ok = false; }
    // The pattern conditions, in the PARENT region (a pattern's value is a
    // constant the selector is compared with on every path), one per arm.
    List<Term>:conds = raw list_init::<Term>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    bool:all_ok = true;
    for (int32:a1 in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm1 = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a1));
        Term:ci = raw term_none();
        if (sel_ok) { ci = raw pattern_cond(e, raw ast_pat(e.ast, raw arm_pattern(arm1)), sel, sel_ty, conds, all_ok); }
        if (!ci.ok) { all_ok = false; }
        drop list_push(@conds, move(ci));
    }
    List<int32>:snap = raw snapshot(e);
    // THE MERGE'S INPUTS (L-8, L-9): each arm's end versions, whether it
    // completes (falls through -- for a pick expression, to its trailing
    // `give`), and the `give` term of a completing arm. A `give` anywhere
    // but as an arm's last statement leaves the arm through a nested
    // construct: the versions and the value are then a havoc and opaque.
    List<List<int32>>:snaps = raw list_init::<List<int32>>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    List<bool>:fts = raw list_init::<bool>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    List<Term>:give_terms = raw list_init::<Term>((count => int64) + 1i64);
    bool:nested_give = false;
    for (int32:a in 0i32...count) {
        StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a));
        StmtId:body = raw arm_body(arm);
        int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
        Term:region_c = raw term_none();
        if (conds[a => int64].ok && (!any_guard)) { region_c = raw term_copy(conds[a => int64]); }
        if (region_c.ok) { drop region_enter_cond(e, region_c); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop bind_pattern(e, raw ast_pat(e.ast, raw arm_pattern(arm)));
        if (conds[a => int64].ok) {
            drop hyp_push(e, conds[a => int64].text, conds[a => int64].syms);
        }
        if (!any_guard) {
            for (int32:j in 0i32...a) {
                if (conds[j => int64].ok) {
                    drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app1("not", conds[j => int64].text), conds[j => int64].syms);
                }
            }
        }
        Term:g = raw enc_expr(e, raw arm_guard(arm));
        if (g.ok && g.is_bool && (!any_fall)) { drop hyp_push(e, g.text, g.syms); }
        e.last_give = raw term_none();
        drop walk_block(e, body);
        drop region_leave(e);
        drop scope_release(e, mark);
        drop list_push(@snaps, raw snapshot(e));
        bool:trailing = raw block_ends_in_give(e, body);
        if (raw stmt_has_nested_give(e, body, 64i32)) { nested_give = true; }
        if (trailing) {
            drop list_push(@fts, raw block_reaches_last(e, body));
            drop list_push(@give_terms, raw term_copy(e.last_give));
        } else {
            drop list_push(@fts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, body, 64i32));
            drop list_push(@give_terms, raw term_none());
        }
        drop restore(e, snap);
    }
    e.last_give = raw term_none();
    // THE MERGE (L-8): every arm's condition a term (a wildcard's is the
    // negation of the ones before it), no guard, no `fall`, no nested
    // `give`; else the havoc the walk did before this step.
    bool:mergeable = all_ok && (!any_guard) && (!any_fall) && (!nested_give);
    if (nested_give) {
        List<int32>:pa = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
        for (int32:a2 in 0i32...count) {
            StmtNode:arm2 = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, start, a2));
            drop collect_assigned(e, raw arm_body(arm2), @pa);
        }
        drop invalidate(e, pa);
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    drop merge_arms(e, conds, snaps, fts, snap, mergeable);
    // THE VALUE (L-9): the chain over the completing arms' `give` terms.
    if (!(want_value && mergeable)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    Term:val = raw term_none();
    bool:have = false;
    int32:k = count;
    while (k > 0i32) decreases k {
        k = k - 1i32;
        if (!fts[k => int64]) { continue; }
        Term:gk = raw term_copy(give_terms[k => int64]);
        if (!gk.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (!have) { val = move(gk); have = true; continue; }
        if (gk.is_bool != val.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        val = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: val.is_bool,
                    text: raw smt_app3("ite", conds[k => int64].text, gk.text, val.text),
                    syms: raw syms_union(conds[k => int64].syms, raw syms_union(gk.syms, val.syms)) };
    }
    if (!have) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    pass val;
};

// Does a block's last statement `give`? The shape a pick expression's arm
// takes when its value is the arm's own (L-9).
func:block_ends_in_give = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(body)) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) { pass true; }
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { pass false; }
    int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
    if (n == 0i32) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:last = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), n - 1i32) });
    pass (last.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt);
};

// Does every statement of a block BEFORE its trailing `give` fall through?
// Then the arm completes with that give's value (L-9).
func:block_reaches_last = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { pass true; }
    int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...(n - 1i32)) {
        StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
        if (!(raw stmt_falls_through(e, ch, 64i32))) { pass false; }
    }
    pass true;
};

// A `give` anywhere in a block other than as its last statement -- nested in
// an `if`, a loop, a pick statement -- leaves the arm from inside a
// construct, which the merge does not follow (L-9).
func:stmt_has_nested_give = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(body)) { pass false; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, body);
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, body, fuel)); }
    int32:n = raw stmt_list_count(s);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...n) {
        StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
        StmtNode:c = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, ch);
        if ((i == (n - 1i32)) && (c.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt)) { continue; }
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, ch, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
    }
    pass false;
};

func:stmt_has_give = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) { pass true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw stmt_has_give(e, ch, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_then(s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_else(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw stmt_has_give(e, raw arm_body(arm), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_give(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index }, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    pass false;
};

// THE MERGE OF THE ARMS' VERSIONS (L-8). Over the bindings that existed
// before the construct: the arms that complete contribute their end
// versions; a binding they agree on keeps that version; one they differ on
// gets a new version `(ite c_1 v_1 (ite c_2 v_2 ... v_n))` -- the last
// completing arm the default -- when `mergeable` (every condition a term)
// and every contributing version is named, else a fresh opaque version. One
// completing arm: its versions are adopted and its condition is a fact of
// the parent (the others never fall through). None: nothing after is
// reachable, and nothing is said.
func:merge_arms = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<Term>:conds, List<List<int32>>:snaps, List<bool>:fts,
                      List<int32>:pre, bool:mergeable) never fails {
    int64:arms = fts.count;
    int64:completing = 0i64;
    int64:only = 0i64 - 1i64;
    for (int64:i in 0i64...arms) {
        if (fts[i]) { completing = completing + 1i64; only = i; }
    }
    if (completing == 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    // A `simd` binding's lanes are fresh past a merge (D-282): the arms'
    // lane versions are not merged, and opaque is sound.
    drop lanes_refresh_all(e);
    if (completing == 1i64) {
        drop adopt_versions(e, snaps[only]);
        if (mergeable && conds[only].ok) { drop hyp_push(e, conds[only].text, conds[only].syms); }
        pass NIL;
    }
    int64:n = pre.count;
    if (e.binds.count < n) { n = e.binds.count; }
    for (int64:i2 in 0i64...arms) { if (snaps[i2].count < n) { n = snaps[i2].count; } }
    for (int64:b in 0i64...n) {
        bool:same = true;
        int32:first = 0i32 - 1i32;
        bool:seen = false;
        bool:named = true;
        for (int64:a in 0i64...arms) {
            if (!fts[a]) { continue; }
            int32:v = snaps[a][b];
            if (v < 0i32) { named = false; }
            if (!seen) { first = v; seen = true; }
            else { if (v != first) { same = false; } }
        }
        if (same) { e.binds[b].sym = first; continue; }
        int32:name = e.binds[b].name;
        if (!(mergeable && named)) {
            List<int32>:one = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@one, name);
            drop invalidate(e, one);
            continue;
        }
        // The chain from the last completing arm backwards.
        Term:t = raw term_none();
        bool:have = false;
        int64:k = arms;
        bool:broken = false;
        while (k > 0i64) decreases k {
            k = k - 1i64;
            if (!fts[k]) { continue; }
            int32:vk = snaps[k][b];
            Term:tk = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: e.syms[vk => int64].is_bool, text: raw sym_text(e, vk),
                            syms: raw list_init::<int32>(1i64) };
            drop list_push(@tk.syms, vk);
            if (!have) { t = move(tk); have = true; continue; }
            if (!conds[k].ok) { broken = true; break; }
            t = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: t.is_bool,
                      text: raw smt_app3("ite", conds[k].text, tk.text, t.text),
                      syms: raw syms_union(conds[k].syms, raw syms_union(tk.syms, t.syms)) };
        }
        if (broken) {
            List<int32>:one2 = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop list_push(@one2, name);
            drop invalidate(e, one2);
            continue;
        }
        drop bind_assign(e, name, t);
        drop assert_rule(e, b);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// One arm's PATTERN as a condition on the selector's term (L-3), or
// `term_none`: a wildcard is the negation of the conditions before it when
// every one of them exists (`prior_ok`), and `true` -- no fact -- when it is
// the first arm.
func:pattern_cond = Term(Encoder->:e, PatNode:p, Term:sel, int32:sel_ty, List<Term>:prior, bool:prior_ok) never fails {
    if (!sel.ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatValue) {
        Term:v = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw pat_value(p), sel_ty);
        if (!(v.ok && (v.is_bool == sel.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        pass (raw term_app2("=", sel, v, true));
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatRange) {
        if (sel.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        Term:lo = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw pat_range_lo(p), sel_ty);
        Term:hi = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw pat_range_hi(p), sel_ty);
        if (!(lo.ok && hi.ok && (!lo.is_bool) && (!hi.is_bool))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        Term:ge = raw term_app2("<=", lo, sel, true);
        Term:lt = raw term_app2("<", sel, hi, true);
        if (raw pat_range_inclusive(p)) { lt = raw term_app2("<=", sel, hi, true); }
        pass (raw term_app2("and", ge, lt, true));
    }
    // `ERR:` (D-008 section 5.1): the selector is the sentinel.
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatErrPattern) {
        if (sel.is_bool) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (!(raw is_twisted(e, sel_ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app2("=", sel.text, raw tw_min(e, sel_ty)),
                   syms: raw syms_union(sel.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    }
    if (p.kind == PatKind.PatWildcard) {
        if (!prior_ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (prior.count == 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
        Term:acc = raw term_none();
        bool:first = true;
        for (int64:i in 0i64...prior.count) {
            if (!prior[i].ok) { pass (raw term_none()); }
            if (first) { acc = raw term_copy(prior[i]); first = false; }
            else { acc = raw term_app2("or", acc, prior[i], true); }
        }
        pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", acc.text),
                   syms: raw syms_union(acc.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
    }
    pass (raw term_none());
};

// A PATTERN'S VALUE (L-3): the checker compares a pattern with the selector
// and records no type on the pattern's own literal (a pattern is not an
// expression it types for its own sake), so a literal is encoded here under
// the SELECTOR's type -- the checker made it fit -- and a negated literal
// likewise; anything else, a named constant, goes through `enc_expr`.
func:enc_pattern_value = Term(Encoder->:e, ExprId:id, int32:sel_ty) never fails {
    if (raw expr_is_none(id)) { pass (raw term_none()); }
    ExprNode:n = raw ast_expr(e.ast, id);
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) {
        if (raw is_twisted(e, sel_ty)) { pass (raw twisted_int_literal(e, n.payload, sel_ty)); }
        if (!(raw is_int(e, sel_ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (raw type_is_signed(e.types, sel_ty)) { pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(n.payload), false)); }
        pass (raw term_lit(raw u64_decimal(n.payload =>! uint64), false));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprFloatLiteral) {
        if (raw is_twisted(e, sel_ty)) {
            pass (raw twisted_text_literal(e, raw intern_get(e.interns, n.payload =>! int32), sel_ty));
        }
        pass (raw term_none());
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprBoolLiteral) {
        if (!(raw is_bool(e, sel_ty))) { pass (raw term_none()); }
        if (n.payload != 0i64) { pass (raw term_lit("true", true)); }
        pass (raw term_lit("false", true));
    }
    if (n.kind == ExprKind.ExprUnaryExpr) {
        if ((raw expr_op(n)) == TokenKind.OpMinus) {
            ExprNode:o = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw expr_operand(n));
            if ((o.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) && (raw is_int(e, sel_ty)) && (o.payload >= 0i64)) {
                pass (raw term_lit(raw smt_int(0i64 - o.payload), false));
            }
            // A negated twisted literal (D-278): `0 - v`, in range as the
            // literal was.
            bool:tlit = ((o.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) || (o.kind == ExprKind.ExprFloatLiteral));
            if (tlit && (raw is_twisted(e, sel_ty))) {
                Term:pv = raw enc_pattern_value(e, raw expr_operand(n), sel_ty);
                if (pv.ok && (!pv.is_bool)) {
                    pass Term{ ok: true, is_bool: false, text: raw smt_app2("-", "0", pv.text),
                               syms: raw syms_union(pv.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
                }
                pass (raw term_none());
            }
        }
    }
    pass (raw enc_expr(e, id));
};

// Is there a `fall` anywhere under this statement? Conservative in the
// direction that matters: a `fall` found means no arm of the pick gets a
// condition (L-3).
func:stmt_has_fall = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass false; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFallStmt) { pass true; }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, ch, fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_then(s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_else(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) { pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt)   { pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)); }
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_counted_body(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw stmt_has_fall(e, raw arm_body(arm), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        pass (raw stmt_has_fall(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index }, fuel - 1i32));
    }
    pass false;
};

// DOES A STATEMENT FALL THROUGH TO WHAT FOLLOWS IT (L-2)? False only for a
// syntactic terminator -- `pass`, `fail`, `return`, `exit`, `trap`, `break`,
// `continue`, `give` -- and for a block holding one, an `if` whose two arms
// hold one each, a `pick` whose every arm does. Everything else falls through
// as far as this walk claims: a loop, a `when`, a `defer`, a call, a `fall`,
// `#unreachable()`. Exact in the direction that matters, because the claim
// "never falls through" becomes a hypothesis after the construct.
func:stmt_falls_through = bool(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid, int32:fuel) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass true; }
    if (fuel <= 0i32) { pass true; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTrapStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBreakStmt)
        || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt)) {
        pass false;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) {
        for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
            StmtId:ch = StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) };
            if (!(raw stmt_falls_through(e, ch, fuel - 1i32))) { pass false; }
        }
        pass true;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        if (raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_then(s), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        pass (raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_else(s), fuel - 1i32));
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        for (int32:a in 0i32...(raw pick_arm_count(s))) {
            StmtNode:arm = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, raw pick_arm_at(e.ast, raw pick_arm_start(s), a));
            if (raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw arm_body(arm), fuel - 1i32)) { pass true; }
        }
        pass false;
    }
    pass true;
};

// ADOPT an arm's end versions as the current ones (L-2): the other arm never
// falls through, so what follows sees exactly this arm's state. A limited
// name whose version changed gets its rule re-asserted in this region, as a
// merge's havoc would (1.5.2 L-7).
func:adopt_versions = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<int32>:vers) never fails {
    int64:n = vers.count;
    if (e.binds.count < n) { n = e.binds.count; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...n) {
        bool:changed = (e.binds[i].sym != vers[i]);
        e.binds[i].sym = vers[i];
        if (changed) { drop assert_rule(e, i); }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

func:walk_block = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);
    if (s.kind != StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { drop walk_stmt(e, sid); pass NIL; }
    int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
    for (int32:i in 0i32...(raw stmt_list_count(s))) {
        drop walk_stmt(e, StmtId{ index: raw ast_id_at(e.ast, raw stmt_list_start(s), i) });
    }
    drop scope_release(e, mark);
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:walk_stmt = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:sid) never fails {
    if (raw stmt_is_none(sid)) { pass NIL; }
    StmtNode:s = raw ast_stmt(e.ast, sid);

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtBlockStmt) { drop walk_block(e, sid); pass NIL; }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtVarDeclStmt) {
        int32:name = raw stmt_name(s);
        int32:dty = raw subst_emitted_param(e.ctx, raw resolve_type(e.tr, raw stmt_decl_type(s), e.scope));
        ExprId:init = raw stmt_decl_init(e.ast, s);
        Term:t = raw term_none();
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(init))) { t = raw enc_expr(e, init); }
        int32:vrule = raw limit_rule_of(e, raw stmt_decl_limit(e.ast, s));
        drop bind_define(e, name, dty, t, vrule, false);
        if (raw is_simd(e, dty)) { drop bind_lanes_from(e, raw bind_find(e, name), init); }
        // THE FIRST WRITE POINT (1.5.2 step 3, D-251, L-7): after the new
        // version and its definition, the site's obligation -- the rule over
        // the version -- and THEN the rule as a hypothesis, so the goal is
        // never in its own cone. A declaration without an initialiser is not
        // a write point and gets no hypothesis: its vacant value is never
        // read (definite assignment); its first assignment is the write.
        if ((vrule != 0i32) && (!(raw expr_is_none(init)))) {
            drop after_write(e, name, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssignStmt) {
        TokenKind:op = raw stmt_op(s);
        ExprId:target = raw stmt_target(s);
        ExprNode:tn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, target);
        Term:rhs = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_assigned(s));
        if (tn.kind != ExprKind.ExprIdentifierExpr) {
            // A field, element or pointee write: its own subexpressions are
            // sites; no local symbol changes (an address-taken local is never
            // defined, so a write through a pointer invalidates nothing here).
            // THE TARGET'S OWN INDEX IS MEMOISED AND THE TARGET IS A GUARD
            // SITE WHEN MARKED (D-286, 1.5.5 step 2): the children are walked
            // once, the top node's index kept for the `disjoint` row.
            // A LIMITED FIELD'S WRITE POINT (D-308 SS2, 1.5.8b step 6): the
            // rule over the value STORED, at the member access -- the emitter's
            // own key. A plain `=` stores the right-hand side; a compound
            // stores the arithmetic's result, which the `fov` branch below
            // builds as `ft` for the `overflow` row, so the row is recorded
            // there. A limited ROOT's row is `emit_assign_limit`'s, at the
            // statement's key: two checks, two keys, both counted.
            if (tn.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
                if (op == TokenKind.OpAssign) {
                    drop record_field_limit(e, raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(tn)),
                                            tn.payload =>! int32, rhs, target.index, s.span);
                }
            }
            if (tn.kind == ExprKind.ExprIndexExpr) {
                Term:tbase = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(tn));
                Term:tidx = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(tn));
                drop memo_put(e, (raw expr_rhs(tn)).index, tidx);
                // THE WRITE'S OWN `bounds` ROW (1.5.8b step 5): an element
                // WRITE is guarded exactly as a read is -- `addr_of_place` is
                // one function for both -- and until this line only the read
                // had a row, so `t.haspt[id] = 1i32` left a trap the belts
                // could not account for (71 of them in the compiler's own
                // emission). The site is the INDEX node, the key the emitter
                // elides under, and the length is the target base's.
                int32:tbty = raw ty_of(e, raw expr_lhs(tn));
                if ((raw type_kind(e.types, tbty)) != (raw TY_POINTER())) {
                    Term:tlen = raw term_none();
                    if ((raw has_len_term(e, tbty)) || (raw type_is_list(e.tr, tbty))) {
                        tlen = raw place_len_term(e, raw expr_lhs(tn), tbty);
                    }
                    drop record_bounds(e, tidx, tlen, (raw expr_rhs(tn)).index, s.span);
                }
            } else {
                drop walk_children(e, tn);
            }
            drop enc_alias_site(e, target);
            if ((op == TokenKind.OpSlashAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpPercentAssign)) {
                int32:pt = raw ty_of(e, target);
                if (raw is_int(e, pt)) {
                    Term:cur = raw term_opaque(e, pt);
                    drop record_division(e, pt, cur, rhs, target.index, s.span);
                }
                // A `simd` PLACE's compound division (D-284, 1.5.4e step 0;
                // DEF-39): the any-lane rows over opaque current lanes and the
                // right-hand side's.
                if (raw is_simd(e, pt)) {
                    List<Term>:pla = raw lanes_of(e, target, pt);
                    List<Term>:plb = raw lanes_of(e, raw stmt_assigned(s), pt);
                    drop record_division_lanes(e, raw type_elem(e.types, pt), pla, plb, target.index, s.span);
                }
            }
            // A COMPOUND `+= -= *=` THROUGH A FIELD OR ELEMENT (1.5.8b step 3):
            // the guard's `overflow` row at the target's site, over an opaque
            // current value (the place has no symbol here) -- the any-lane row
            // for a `simd` place.
            bool:fov = ((op == TokenKind.OpPlusAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpMinusAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpStarAssign));
            if (fov) {
                int32:pt3 = raw ty_of(e, target);
                TokenKind:fbop = raw arith_base(op);
                if (raw is_int(e, pt3)) {
                    Term:fcur = raw term_opaque(e, pt3);
                    Term:ft = raw term_none();
                    if (rhs.ok && (!rhs.is_bool)) {
                        if (fbop == TokenKind.OpPlus)  { ft = raw term_app2("+", fcur, rhs, false); }
                        if (fbop == TokenKind.OpMinus) { ft = raw term_app2("-", fcur, rhs, false); }
                        if (fbop == TokenKind.OpStar)  { e.nonlinear = true; ft = raw term_app2("*", fcur, rhs, false); }
                    }
                    drop record_overflow(e, pt3, ft, target.index, s.span);
                    // ... and the limited FIELD's row over the same result.
                    if (tn.kind == ExprKind.ExprMemberAccessExpr) {
                        drop record_field_limit(e, raw ty_of(e, raw expr_operand(tn)),
                                                tn.payload =>! int32, ft, target.index, s.span);
                    }
                }
                if (raw is_simd(e, pt3)) {
                    int32:felem = raw type_elem(e.types, pt3);
                    if (raw is_int(e, felem)) {
                        List<Term>:fla = raw lanes_of(e, target, pt3);
                        List<Term>:flb = raw lanes_of(e, raw stmt_assigned(s), pt3);
                        drop record_overflow_lanes(e, felem, raw overflow_out_lanes(e, fbop, felem, fla, flb, s.span),
                                                   target.index, s.span);
                    }
                }
            }
            // A COMPOUND SHIFT THROUGH A FIELD OR ELEMENT (DEF-41, 1.5.4e step
            // 0): the emitter has guarded `s.f <<= n` since D-277 and this
            // branch recorded no row for it, so a verified build carried a
            // trap the belts could not account for. The scalar row as the
            // identifier path's, the any-lane row for a `simd` place.
            if ((op == TokenKind.OpShlAssign) || (op == TokenKind.OpShrAssign)) {
                int32:pt2 = raw ty_of(e, target);
                if (raw is_int(e, pt2)) {
                    drop record_shift(e, pt2, rhs, raw stmt_assigned(s), target.index, s.span);
                }
                if (raw is_simd(e, pt2)) {
                    List<Term>:plb2 = raw lanes_of(e, raw stmt_assigned(s), pt2);
                    drop record_shift_lanes(e, raw type_elem(e.types, pt2), plb2, target.index, s.span);
                }
            }
            // THE SECOND WRITE POINT through a field or element (D-251): the
            // ROOT's rule over the root's whole value -- `unencoded` while the
            // root's type is outside the fragment (L-6), and no hypothesis
            // (the root has no symbol to assert over).
            drop after_write(e, raw limited_root_name(e, target), raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
            pass NIL;
        }
        int32:name = tn.payload =>! int32;
        drop assign_ident(e, s, op, target, name, rhs);
        // THE SECOND WRITE POINT (D-251, L-7), AFTER the new version: the
        // site's obligation, then the rule as a hypothesis.
        drop after_write(e, name, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtIfStmt) {
        // THE CONDITION IS A FACT IN THE ARM IT GUARDS (L-1): `c` in the
        // then-region, `(not c)` in the else-region; nothing when it is
        // outside the fragment. Encoded LOUD in the parent: it runs on every
        // path.
        Term:c = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_cond(s));
        bool:has_c = c.ok && c.is_bool;
        Term:nc = raw term_none();
        if (has_c) {
            nc = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", c.text),
                       syms: raw syms_union(c.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        StmtId:then_s = raw stmt_then(s);
        StmtId:else_s = raw stmt_else(s);
        List<int32>:snap = raw snapshot(e);
        if (has_c) { drop region_enter_cond(e, c); drop hyp_push(e, c.text, c.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop walk_block(e, then_s);
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_then = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap);
        if (has_c) { drop region_enter_cond(e, nc); drop hyp_push(e, nc.text, nc.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop walk_block(e, else_s);
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_else = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap);
        // AFTER THE `if` (L-2, L-8): the two arms merge -- an arm that never
        // falls through contributes nothing; a binding the arms left at
        // different versions is `(ite c then else)` when both are named and
        // the condition has a term, a havoc otherwise.
        List<Term>:conds = raw list_init::<Term>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@conds, raw term_copy(c));
        drop list_push(@conds, raw term_copy(nc));
        List<List<int32>>:snaps = raw list_init::<List<int32>>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@snaps, move(snap_then));
        drop list_push(@snaps, move(snap_else));
        List<bool>:fts = raw list_init::<bool>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@fts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, then_s, 64i32));
        drop list_push(@fts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, else_s, 64i32));
        drop merge_arms(e, conds, snaps, fts, snap, has_c);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhileStmt) {
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_while_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_body(e.ast, s),
                       raw stmt_cond(s), raw stmt_label(s), raw counter_none(), raw stmt_while_measure(e.ast, s));
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtForStmt) {
        // A RANGE `for` (L-12): the bounds are the range node's two operands
        // (sites, encoded once here), captured at entry (D-234), the limit
        // exclusive (`..` adds one); the binding's entry version is the low
        // bound, its body version a havoc inside the bounds. Any other
        // iterable: the binding opaque, havoced per body.
        ExprId:iter = raw stmt_for_iter(e.ast, s);
        Counter:ctr = raw counter_none();
        DeclNode:bd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, raw stmt_for_binding(s));
        int32:bt = raw subst_emitted_param(e.ctx, raw resolve_type(e.tr, raw param_type(bd), e.scope));
        ctr.kind = 1i32;
        ctr.name = raw decl_name(bd);
        Term:entry = raw term_none();
        bool:is_range = false;
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(iter))) {
            ExprNode:itn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, iter);
            if (itn.kind == ExprKind.ExprRangeExpr) { is_range = true; }
        }
        if (is_range) {
            ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, iter);
            Term:lo = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_lhs(rn));
            Term:hi = raw enc_expr(e, raw expr_rhs(rn));
            if (rn.payload == 1i64) {
                if (hi.ok && (!hi.is_bool)) { hi = raw term_app2("+", hi, raw term_lit("1", false), false); }
                else { hi = raw term_none(); }
            }
            ctr.ranged = true;
            ctr.start = raw term_capture(e, bt, lo);
            ctr.limit = raw term_capture(e, bt, hi);
            ctr.step = raw term_lit("1", false);
            ctr.asc = raw term_lit("true", true);
            entry = raw term_copy(ctr.start);
        } else {
            Term:it = raw enc_expr(e, iter);
        }
        int64:mark = raw scope_mark(e);
        drop bind_define(e, raw decl_name(bd), bt, entry, 0i32, false);
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_for_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_for_body(e.ast, s),
                       ExprId{ index: 0i32 }, raw stmt_label(s), ctr, raw verify_none());
        drop scope_release(e, mark);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if ((s.kind == StmtKind.StmtLoopStmt) || (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt)) {
        // THE HEAD (L-11, L-13): `loop(start, limit, step)` or `till(limit,
        // step)` -- each argument a site, encoded once; the start (`0` for
        // `till`), the limit and the step captured; the direction `asc =
        // start < limit` as the emitter computes it once. A COMPUTED step's
        // positivity is the `loop-step` row (S-46), its compare the guard,
        // and `step > 0` is then a fact of every continuing execution (the
        // guard trapped otherwise); a literal step is the checker's (TYPE-068)
        // -- no row, no guard -- and positive by construction.
        int32:argc = raw stmt_counted_argc(e.ast, s);
        int32:i64t = raw tt_int(e.types, 64i32, true);
        Counter:ctr = raw counter_none();
        ctr.kind = 2i32;
        List<Term>:args = raw list_init::<Term>(4i64);
        for (int32:ai in 0i32...argc) {
            drop list_push(@args, raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_counted_arg(e.ast, s, ai)));
        }
        Term:st = raw term_lit("0", false);
        Term:li = raw term_none();
        Term:sp = raw term_none();
        if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtTillStmt) {
            if (argc == 2i32) { li = raw term_copy(args[0i64]); sp = raw term_copy(args[1i64]); }
        } else {
            if (argc == 3i32) {
                st = raw term_copy(args[0i64]);
                li = raw term_copy(args[1i64]);
                sp = raw term_copy(args[2i64]);
            }
        }
        ctr.start = raw term_capture(e, i64t, st);
        ctr.limit = raw term_capture(e, i64t, li);
        ctr.step = raw term_capture(e, i64t, sp);
        if (ctr.start.ok && ctr.limit.ok) { ctr.asc = raw term_app2("<", ctr.start, ctr.limit, true); }
        StepLit:sl = raw counted_step_literal(e.ast, s);
        if (sl.is_lit) {
            if (argc >= 1i32) {
                ExprNode:sx = raw ast_expr(e.ast, raw stmt_counted_arg(e.ast, s, argc - 1i32));
                if (sx.kind == ExprKind.ExprIntLiteral) { ctr.lit_step = sx.payload; }
            }
        } else {
            if (ctr.step.ok) {
                Term:pos = raw term_app2(">", ctr.step, raw term_lit("0", false), true);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_LOOP_STEP(), pos.text, pos.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
                drop hyp_push(e, pos.text, pos.syms);
            } else {
                List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_LOOP_STEP(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
            }
        }
        if (sl.is_lit && ctr.step.ok) {
            Term:pos2 = raw term_app2(">", ctr.step, raw term_lit("0", false), true);
            drop hyp_push(e, pos2.text, pos2.syms);
        }
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_counted_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_counted_body(s),
                       ExprId{ index: 0i32 }, raw stmt_label(s), ctr, raw verify_none());
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtWhenStmt) {
        // The loop half through `walk_loop`; then `then` and `end` as the two
        // arms of "did the body run" (L-5, D-027): the body ran at least once
        // exactly when the condition held at the FIRST head visit, over the
        // pre-loop versions. `then` knows that; `end` knows its negation and
        // that the loop changed nothing -- every name the body havoced equals
        // its pre-loop version. The condition over the pre-loop versions is
        // encoded QUIET (its sites are the body region's, once).
        List<int32>:ka = raw list_init::<int32>(4i64);
        drop collect_assigned(e, sid, @ka);
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:cpre = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_cond(s));
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        bool:has_pre = cpre.ok && cpre.is_bool;
        List<int32>:snap_pre = raw snapshot(e);
        drop walk_loop(e, sid, raw stmt_when_invariant(e.ast, s), raw stmt_when_body(e.ast, s),
                       raw stmt_cond(s), raw stmt_label(s), raw counter_none(), raw stmt_when_measure(e.ast, s));
        List<int32>:snap_post = raw snapshot(e);
        Term:npre = raw term_none();
        if (has_pre) {
            npre = Term{ ok: true, is_bool: true, text: raw smt_app1("not", cpre.text),
                         syms: raw syms_union(cpre.syms, raw list_init::<int32>(1i64)) };
        }
        if (has_pre) { drop region_enter_cond(e, cpre); drop hyp_push(e, cpre.text, cpre.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        drop walk_block(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s));
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_then = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap_post);
        if (has_pre) { drop region_enter_cond(e, npre); drop hyp_push(e, npre.text, npre.syms); } else { drop region_enter(e); }
        int64:np = snap_post.count;
        if (snap_pre.count < np) { np = snap_pre.count; }
        for (int64:bi in 0i64...np) {
            int32:post = snap_post[bi];
            int32:pre = snap_pre[bi];
            if ((post != pre) && (post >= 0i32) && (pre >= 0i32)) {
                List<int32>:two = raw list_init::<int32>(2i64);
                drop list_push(@two, post);
                drop list_push(@two, pre);
                drop hyp_push(e, raw smt_app2("=", raw sym_text(e, post), raw sym_text(e, pre)), two);
            }
        }
        drop walk_block(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s));
        drop region_leave(e);
        List<int32>:snap_end = raw snapshot(e);
        drop restore(e, snap_post);
        // THE MERGE (L-8): `then` and `end` are the two arms of "did the body
        // run", the body's own names already havoced by the loop.
        List<Term>:wconds = raw list_init::<Term>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@wconds, raw term_copy(cpre));
        drop list_push(@wconds, raw term_copy(npre));
        List<List<int32>>:wsnaps = raw list_init::<List<int32>>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@wsnaps, move(snap_then));
        drop list_push(@wsnaps, move(snap_end));
        List<bool>:wfts = raw list_init::<bool>(2i64);
        drop list_push(@wfts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_when_then(e.ast, s), 64i32));
        drop list_push(@wfts, raw stmt_falls_through(e, raw stmt_when_end(e.ast, s), 64i32));
        drop merge_arms(e, wconds, wsnaps, wfts, snap_post, has_pre);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPickStmt) {
        drop record_checker(e, raw OK_EXHAUSTIVE(), raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
        Term:sel = raw enc_expr(e, raw pick_selector(s));
        Term:pv = raw walk_pick_arms(e, raw pick_arm_start(s), raw pick_arm_count(s), sel, raw ty_of(e, raw pick_selector(s)), false);
        pass NIL;
    }

    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtDeferStmt) {
        // Runs at an exit the straight line does not see: every name opaque
        // while it is walked, the outer state restored after.
        // AND ONCE PER EXIT (DEF-82, 1.5.8b step 5): the walk sees this body
        // once, the emitter writes it at every exit that runs it, so a guard
        // in here is one row and several traps. The rows recorded under this
        // body carry its statement id, and the table multiplies their traps
        // by the copies the emitter reports. Nested defers need no special
        // case: the inner body's id is counted once per copy of the outer.
        int32:pdefer = e.cur_defer;
        e.cur_defer = (raw stmt_target(s)).index;
        List<int32>:snap = raw snapshot(e);
        drop region_enter(e);
        drop invalidate_all(e);
        drop walk_block(e, StmtId{ index: (raw stmt_target(s)).index });
        drop region_leave(e);
        drop restore(e, snap);
        e.cur_defer = pdefer;
        pass NIL;
    }

    // `prove(e)` (1.5.4 step 4, L-15; S-48): a guard-less row over the
    // proposition, walked QUIET -- nothing executes, so a division inside is
    // not a site; its conditions are the proposition's (DEF-33: a claim over
    // an expression that would trap is not proven); `unencoded` when the
    // proposition is outside the fragment. THEN
    // the proposition is a hypothesis (L-7's order: never in its own cone):
    // a proven claim is knowledge for every site after it -- sound because
    // the verified build refuses an undischarged `prove` and the plain build
    // elides nothing.
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtProveStmt) {
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        int64:pm = raw prop_begin(e);
        Term:pv = raw prop_end(e, pm, raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_expr(s)));
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        if (pv.ok && pv.is_bool) {
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_PROVE(), pv.text, pv.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 0i32);
            drop hyp_push(e, pv.text, pv.syms);
        } else {
            List<int32>:pnone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
            drop record_at(e, raw OK_PROVE(), "", pnone, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                           raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 0i32);
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // `assert_static(e)` (L-17, L-20): the frontend folded it; the row is the
    // inventory's, `checker`; the proposition walked QUIET (nothing executes).
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtAssertStaticStmt) {
        e.quiet = e.quiet + 1i32;
        Term:av = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_expr(s));
        e.quiet = e.quiet - 1i32;
        drop record_checker(e, raw OK_ASSERT_STATIC(), raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtGiveStmt) {
        // THE ARM'S VALUE (L-9): remembered for the pick expression's chain.
        e.last_give = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_expr(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (raw stmt_carries_expr(s.kind)) {
        Term:x = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_expr(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtPassStmt) {
        ExprId:pv = raw stmt_operand(s);
        Term:v = raw enc_expr(e, pv);
        drop record_seam(e, sid, s.span, v, raw ty_of(e, pv), !(raw expr_is_none(pv)));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtReturnStmt) {
        // THE LONG FORM (L-12): `return Result{ value: v }` is a success when
        // its error field is absent or the literal 0; the value is `result`.
        ExprId:ro = raw stmt_operand(s);
        if (!(raw expr_is_none(ro))) {
            ExprNode:rn = raw ast_expr(e.ast, ro);
            if (rn.kind == ExprKind.ExprResultLiteralExpr) {
                Term:rv = raw term_none();
                bool:has_v = (rn.a != 0i32);
                int32:vty = 0i32;
                if (has_v) { rv = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: rn.a }); vty = raw ty_of(e, ExprId{ index: rn.a }); }
                bool:success = true;
                if (rn.b != 0i32) {
                    Term:re = raw enc_expr(e, ExprId{ index: rn.b });
                    success = false;
                    if (re.ok) { if (string_equals(re.text, "0")) { success = true; } }
                }
                if (success) { drop record_seam(e, sid, s.span, rv, vty, has_v); }
                pass NIL;
            }
        }
        Term:rt = raw enc_expr(e, ro);
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtExitStmt) {
        ExprId:xo = raw stmt_operand(s);
        Term:xv = raw enc_expr(e, xo);
        // `failsafe`'s POSTCONDITION (L-14, D-267): the code is positive.
        if (e.is_failsafe) {
            if (!xv.ok) { xv = raw term_opaque(e, raw ty_of(e, xo)); }
            if (xv.ok && (!xv.is_bool)) {
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_FAILSAFE_POST(), raw smt_app2(">", xv.text, "0"), xv.syms,
                               raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true, raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
            } else {
                List<int32>:none = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                drop record_at(e, raw OK_FAILSAFE_POST(), "", none, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                               raw ROLE_GUARD(), sid.index, 1i32);
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtFailStmt) {
        Term:fv = raw enc_expr(e, raw stmt_operand(s));
        pass NIL;
    }
    if (s.kind == StmtKind.StmtContinueStmt) {
        // A HEAD VISIT (L-8): the invariant of the loop this re-enters holds
        // here -- a preservation row keyed at the `continue`.
        int64:fr = raw loop_frame(e, raw stmt_label(s));
        if (fr >= 0i64) {
            // THE MEASURE AT A `continue` (D-304): the head's check runs again
            // with the values here -- a row against the body-start value.
            VerifyId:cmeas = VerifyId{ index: e.loop_meas[fr] };
            if (raw enc_measure_checks(e, cmeas)) {
                int32:cmt = 1i32;
                if (e.loop_msigned[fr]) { cmt = 2i32; }
                Term:cm0 = raw term_copy(e.loop_mstart[fr]);
                Term:cmc = raw enc_expr(e, raw measure_expr(raw ast_verify(e.ast, cmeas)));
                if (cm0.ok && cmc.ok) {
                    Term:clt = raw term_app2("<", cmc, cm0, true);
                    drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), clt.text, clt.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.loop_sids[fr], cmt);
                } else {
                    List<int32>:cmnone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                    drop record_at(e, raw OK_TERMINATE(), "", cmnone, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.loop_sids[fr], cmt);
                }
            }
            VerifyId:civ = VerifyId{ index: e.loop_invs[fr] };
            int32:cnc = raw invariant_clauses(e, civ);
            if (cnc > 0i32) {
                // THE HEAD SEES THE INCREMENTED COUNTER (L-11, L-12): a
                // `continue` re-enters at the increment.
                int32:ck = e.loop_ckind[fr];
                if (ck != 0i32) {
                    drop counter_advance(e, ck, e.loop_cname[fr], raw term_copy(e.loop_cstep[fr]),
                                         raw term_copy(e.loop_casc[fr]), e.loop_cdollar[fr]);
                }
                // A VISIT OF THE HEAD, LOUD (DEF-81): its guards' rows too,
                // under the re-entered loop's clause context.
                int32:cctx = e.clause_ctx;
                e.clause_ctx = e.loop_sids[fr];
                Term:cg = raw invariant_conj(e, civ, false);
                e.clause_ctx = cctx;
                if (cg.ok) {
                    drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), cg.text, cg.syms, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, true,
                                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.loop_sids[fr], cnc);
                } else {
                    List<int32>:cnone = raw list_init::<int32>(1i64);
                    drop record_at(e, raw OK_INVARIANT(), "", cnone, raw SITE_STMT(), sid.index, s.span, false,
                                   raw ROLE_GUARD(), e.loop_sids[fr], cnc);
                }
            }
        }
        pass NIL;
    }
    // break, fall, and anything unclassified: no sites, no definitions.
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the entry: one function instance ------------------------------------------------------

// Parameters are the first bindings; the escaped set is collected before the
// body is walked, since an address taken late in the body still aliases the
// name from its first definition.
pub func:enc_param = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:ty, int32:rule,
                         int32:decl_index) never fails {
    drop enc_param_bind(e, name, ty, rule);
    drop enc_param_entry(e, name, rule, decl_index);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE TWO HALVES OF `enc_param` (1.5.8c step 4): the binding, and the entry
// write point. A function whose measure the group checks binds every
// parameter first, encodes its measure (`enc_entry_measure`), and only then
// takes each limited parameter's entry write -- so the measure's rows sit
// under the range axioms alone; every other function calls the pair back to
// back through `enc_param`, and no row of it moves.
pub func:enc_param_bind = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:ty, int32:rule) never fails {
    drop bind_define(e, name, ty, raw term_none(), rule, false);
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:enc_param_entry = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name, int32:rule, int32:decl_index) never fails {
    // THE THIRD WRITE POINT (1.5.2 step 2, D-251): a limited parameter's
    // check at the callee's entry is a row -- unencoded until step 3.
    if (rule != 0i32) {
        DeclNode:pd = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: decl_index });
        // THE ENTRY WRITE POINT (D-251, L-7): the obligation over the
        // parameter's opaque first version -- `open` unless the type implies
        // the rule -- then the rule as the hypothesis every later read has.
        drop after_write(e, name, raw SITE_DECL(), decl_index, pd.span);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// DOES THIS FUNCTION'S MEASURE CHECK ANYTHING (D-304 (5), 1.5.8c step 4): the
// emitter's `fn_measure_checks`, for the encoder -- a `decreases` on a
// function of a cyclic group.
pub func:enc_fn_measure_checks = bool(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass false; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    if (d.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { pass false; }
    if (raw verify_is_none(raw fn_measure(e.ast, d))) { pass false; }
    int32:g = raw exprtypes_group(e.et, e.fn_decl);
    if (g == 0i32) { pass false; }
    pass (raw exprtypes_group_cyclic(e.et, g));
};

// THE FUNCTION'S OWN MEASURE AT ENTRY (D-304 (5), 1.5.8c step 4): `E` encoded
// LOUD once over the parameters' entry versions -- its guards' rows are this
// function's (the predicate `<sym>.measure` lowers each guard once and reads
// these rows' answers), under the parameters' RANGE AXIOMS ALONE: the
// predicate runs at every call inside the group over the arguments BEFORE the
// callee's checked entry (D-252), so no `requires` and no limited parameter's
// rule has held where it runs, and a guard elided on their strength would be
// elided where it can trap. Hence the order in `obl_function`: after the
// parameters are bound, before any rule or `requires` is pushed. The term is
// kept as `fn_m0` for every recursive call's row; the guards' facts stand as
// hypotheses after their rows, since the body runs only past the snapshot.
pub func:enc_entry_measure = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    e.fn_m0 = raw term_none();
    if (!(raw enc_fn_measure_checks(e))) { pass NIL; }
    DeclNode:d = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    Term:m = raw enc_expr(e, raw contract_cond(raw ast_verify(e.ast, raw fn_measure(e.ast, d))));
    if (m.ok && (!m.is_bool)) { e.fn_m0 = move(m); }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE `stack-depth` ROW (D-305 (7); 1.5.8c step 4): one per cyclic group, in
// the FIRST member instance the emission reaches (the table remembers the
// groups that have one), at that member's declaration -- no guard, no query,
// derived by the runners. Its text names the members and whether every one
// states a measure. A cyclic group is kept or dropped WHOLE by D-262's trim
// (each member references another), so the row's file stands exactly when the
// group's do.
pub func:enc_stack_depth = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    if (e.fn_decl == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    int32:g = raw exprtypes_group(e.et, e.fn_decl);
    if (g == 0i32) { pass NIL; }
    if (!(raw exprtypes_group_cyclic(e.et, g))) { pass NIL; }
    if (e.ctx.obl == NULL) { pass NIL; }
    for (int64:i in 0i64...e.ctx.obl.sd_groups.count) {
        if (e.ctx.obl.sd_groups[i] == g) { pass NIL; }
    }
    drop list_push(@e.ctx.obl.sd_groups, g);
    string:members = "";
    bool:measured = true;
    int32:nd = raw ast_decl_count(e.ast);
    for (int32:di in 1i32...nd) {
        if ((raw exprtypes_group(e.et, di)) != g) { continue; }
        DeclNode:dn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: di });
        if (dn.kind != DeclKind.DeclFunctionDecl) { continue; }
        members = string_concat(members, " ");
        members = string_concat(members, raw intern_get(e.interns, raw decl_name(dn)));
        if (raw verify_is_none(raw fn_measure(e.ast, dn))) { measured = false; }
    }
    string:head = "(stack-depth unmeasured";
    if (measured) { head = "(stack-depth measured"; }
    DeclNode:fdn = raw ast_decl(e.ast, DeclId{ index: e.fn_decl });
    drop record_derived(e, raw OK_STACK_DEPTH(), raw SITE_DECL(), e.fn_decl, fdn.span,
                        string_concat(string_concat(head, members), ")"));
    pass NIL;
};

// A `Rules` body's clause, walked for its own sites (1.5.2 step 2): the
// predicate function is an instance like any other (P-3). THE CLAUSE IS A
// FACT FOR THE CLAUSES AFTER IT (1.5.4b step 2): the predicate traps on the
// first false clause (`emit_rule_fn`), so a later clause runs only where the
// earlier ones held -- `$ != 0tbb32` after `!is_err($)` compares no ERR.
pub func:enc_clause = NIL(Encoder->:e, ExprId:clause) never fails {
    Term:t = raw enc_expr(e, clause);
    if (t.ok && t.is_bool) { drop hyp_push(e, t.text, t.syms); }
    pass NIL;
};

// THE SUBJECT OF A `Rules` BODY'S OWN WALK (1.5.4b step 2): `$` reads the
// subject parameter's symbol, bound by `enc_param` before the clauses --
// until here every `$` in the predicate's walk was a fresh opaque, so the
// clauses said nothing about one value.
pub func:enc_subject = NIL(Encoder->:e, int32:name) never fails {
    int64:bi = raw bind_find(e, name);
    if (bi < 0i64) { pass NIL; }
    e.subject = raw bind_term(e, bi);
    pass NIL;
};

// THE ESCAPE SET FIRST (DEF-14): computed over the whole body BEFORE the
// parameters are bound, so an address-taken parameter is unnamed from its
// first read. 1.5.0 collected it inside `enc_body`, after `enc_param` had
// already given every parameter a stable symbol -- the same hole one line
// earlier.
pub func:enc_prepare = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    drop collect_escaped(e, body);
    pass NIL;
};

pub func:enc_body = NIL(Encoder->:e, StmtId:body) never fails {
    e.in_body = true;
    drop walk_block(e, body);
    e.in_body = false;
    pass NIL;
};

// --- the cone and the hash (P-4) -----------------------------------------------------------

func:has_sym = bool(List<int32>:l, int32:s) never fails {
    for (int64:i in 0i64...l.count) { if (l[i] == s) { pass true; } }
    pass false;
};

func:sym_sort = string(Encoder->:e, int32:idx) never fails {
    if (e.syms[idx => int64].fsort.len > 0i64) {
        pass (string_from_bytes(e.syms[idx => int64].fsort.ptr, e.syms[idx => int64].fsort.len));
    }
    if (e.syms[idx => int64].is_bool) { pass "Bool"; }
    pass "Int";
};

// `(declare-const |x.1| Int)`, or for an uninterpreted function (L-3)
// `(declare-fun |uf.f.7| (Int Int) Int)`.
func:sym_declaration = string(Encoder->:e, int32:idx) never fails {
    string:d = "(declare-const ";
    if (e.syms[idx => int64].sorts.len > 0i64) { d = "(declare-fun "; }
    d = string_concat(d, raw sym_text(e, idx));
    d = string_concat(d, " ");
    if (e.syms[idx => int64].sorts.len > 0i64) {
        d = string_concat(d, string_from_bytes(e.syms[idx => int64].sorts.ptr,
                                               e.syms[idx => int64].sorts.len));
        d = string_concat(d, " ");
    }
    d = string_concat(d, raw sym_sort(e, idx));
    pass (string_concat(d, ")"));
};

// Fill every obligation's cone, canonical text and hash.
pub func:enc_finish = NIL(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if (!e.obls[oi].encoded) {
            string:uhead = "(unencoded ";
            if (e.obls[oi].checker) { uhead = "(checker "; }
            string:u = string_concat(uhead, raw ok_name(e.obls[oi].kind));
            u = string_concat(u, " ");
            u = string_concat(u, int_to_string(e.obls[oi].ordinal => int64));
            u = string_concat(u, ")");
            // A DERIVED ROW'S TEXT IS THE GROUP (1.5.8c step 4): its members and
            // whether they are measured, never an ordinal -- so the row keeps
            // its hash while the group stands and moves when the group moves.
            if (e.obls[oi].derived) { u = string_concat(e.obls[oi].goal, ""); }
            e.obls[oi].canon = string_concat(u, "");
            string:hu = string_concat(u, "\n");
            hu = string_concat(hu, e.symbol);
            hu = string_concat(hu, "\n");
            hu = string_concat(hu, raw ok_name(e.obls[oi].kind));
            hu = string_concat(hu, "\n");
            e.obls[oi].hash = raw sha256_hex(hu);
            e.obls[oi].tier = "-";
            continue;
        }
        // The relevance closure over hypotheses [0, hyps).
        int64:limit_h = e.obls[oi].hyps;
        List<int32>:cs = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
        for (int64:g in 0i64...e.obls[oi].syms.count) {
            if (!(raw has_sym(cs, e.obls[oi].syms[g]))) { drop list_push(@cs, e.obls[oi].syms[g]); }
        }
        List<bool>:inc = raw list_init::<bool>(limit_h + 1i64);
        for (int64:h0 in 0i64...limit_h) { drop list_push(@inc, false); }
        bool:grew = true;
        // a fixed point over the hypotheses: a round that includes no new one is the last, and the hypotheses are finite (D-316)
        while (grew) unbounded {
            grew = false;
            for (int64:h in 0i64...limit_h) {
                if (inc[h]) { continue; }
                if (!(raw region_dominates(e, e.hyps[h].region, e.obls[oi].region))) { continue; }
                bool:touch = false;
                for (int64:q in 0i64...e.hyps[h].syms.count) {
                    if (raw has_sym(cs, e.hyps[h].syms[q])) { touch = true; }
                }
                if (!touch) { continue; }
                inc[h] = true;
                grew = true;
                for (int64:q2 in 0i64...e.hyps[h].syms.count) {
                    if (!(raw has_sym(cs, e.hyps[h].syms[q2]))) { drop list_push(@cs, e.hyps[h].syms[q2]); }
                }
            }
        }
        // Symbols ascending (insertion order of declaration), hypotheses in order.
        List<int32>:sorted = raw list_init::<int32>(cs.count + 1i64);
        for (int64:si in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
            if (raw has_sym(cs, si =>! int32)) { drop list_push(@sorted, si =>! int32); }
        }
        List<int32>:hl = raw list_init::<int32>(8i64);
        for (int64:h2 in 0i64...limit_h) { if (inc[h2]) { drop list_push(@hl, h2 =>! int32); } }
        SmtBuf:b = raw smtbuf_init();
        for (int64:s2 in 0i64...sorted.count) {
            drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw sym_declaration(e, sorted[s2]));
        }
        for (int64:h3 in 0i64...hl.count) {
            drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", string_concat(e.hyps[hl[h3] => int64].text, "")));
        }
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", raw smt_app1("not", string_concat(e.obls[oi].goal, ""))));
        string:canon = raw smtbuf_text(move(b));
        string:hin = string_concat(canon, e.symbol);
        hin = string_concat(hin, "\n");
        hin = string_concat(hin, raw ok_name(e.obls[oi].kind));
        hin = string_concat(hin, "\n");
        e.obls[oi].hash = raw sha256_hex(hin);
        // THE TIER (D-281): what the cone's theory is -- `fp` where a float
        // sort is in it, `bv` where a bit-vector crossing is, else `int`.
        string:tier = "int";
        if (raw has_sub(canon, "int2bv")) { tier = "bv"; }
        if (raw has_sub(canon, "FloatingPoint")) { tier = "fp"; }
        if (raw has_sub(canon, "(fp.")) { tier = "fp"; }
        e.obls[oi].tier = move(tier);
        e.obls[oi].canon = move(canon);
        e.obls[oi].cone_syms = move(sorted);
        e.obls[oi].cone_hyps = move(hl);
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// The `--elide` reader marks rows whose hash the manifest lists as discharged.
pub func:enc_mark_discharged = NIL(Encoder->:e, List<string>:hashes) never fails {
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        for (int64:h in 0i64...hashes.count) {
            if (string_equals(e.obls[oi].hash, hashes[h])) { e.obls[oi].discharged = true; }
        }
    }
    pass NIL;
};

// Is the site (an ExprId index) of kind `kind` discharged? The emitter's question.
pub func:enc_site_discharged = bool(Encoder->:e, int32:space, int32:site, int32:kind) never fails {
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if ((e.obls[oi].site == site) && (e.obls[oi].kind == kind)) {
            if (e.obls[oi].space == space) { pass e.obls[oi].discharged; }
        }
    }
    pass false;
};

// --- the solver file for one function ------------------------------------------------------

// The header comment, the logic, the definitions, every declaration at the
// base level, then one push/assert/check-sat/pop per obligation over its cone
// (P-6, P-7, P-16, P-17). Unencoded rows take no query.
pub func:enc_file_text = string(Encoder->:e) never fails {
    SmtBuf:b = raw smtbuf_init();
    drop smtbuf_line(@b, string_concat("; ", e.symbol));
    int64:checks = 0i64;
    for (int64:oi in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        string:c = string_concat("; o", int_to_string(oi + 1i64));
        c = string_concat(c, " ");
        c = string_concat(c, raw ok_name(e.obls[oi].kind));
        c = string_concat(c, " ");
        c = string_concat(c, e.obls[oi].hash);
        c = string_concat(c, " ");
        c = string_concat(c, int_to_string(e.obls[oi].line => int64));
        c = string_concat(c, ":");
        c = string_concat(c, int_to_string(e.obls[oi].col => int64));
        if (!e.obls[oi].encoded) {
            if (e.obls[oi].checker) { c = string_concat(c, " checker"); }
            else { c = string_concat(c, " unencoded"); }
        }
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, c);
        if (e.obls[oi].encoded) { checks = checks + 1i64; }
    }
    drop smtbuf_line(@b, string_concat("; checks ", int_to_string(checks)));
    // THE LOGIC: linear or nonlinear integer arithmetic, with uninterpreted
    // functions (L-3) the moment one is declared -- QF_LIA refuses a
    // `declare-fun` of arity above zero.
    bool:has_uf = false;
    for (int64:ui in 0i64...e.syms.count) { if (e.syms[ui].sorts.len > 0i64) { has_uf = true; } }
    // A FLOAT SORT IN THE FILE (D-281): `ALL`, since every file carries Int
    // symbols beside the float ones (a parameter's range axiom at least).
    if (e.uses_fp) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic ALL)"); }
    else { if (e.nonlinear) {
        if (e.uses_bv) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic ALL)"); }
        else { if (has_uf) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_UFNIA)"); }
        else { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_NIA)"); } }
    } else {
        if (e.uses_bv) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic ALL)"); }
        else { if (has_uf) { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_UFLIA)"); }
        else { drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(set-logic QF_LIA)"); } }
    } }
    if (e.uses_sdiv) {
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(define-fun npk_sdiv ((a Int) (b Int)) Int (ite (>= a 0) (ite (>= b 0) (div a b) (- (div a (- b)))) (ite (>= b 0) (- (div (- a) b)) (div (- a) (- b)))))");
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(define-fun npk_srem ((a Int) (b Int)) Int (- a (* b (npk_sdiv a b))))");
    }
    for (int64:si in 0i64...e.syms.count) {
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw sym_declaration(e, si =>! int32));
    }
    for (int64:oi2 in 0i64...e.obls.count) {
        if (!e.obls[oi2].encoded) { continue; }
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(push)");
        for (int64:h in 0i64...e.obls[oi2].cone_hyps.count) {
            int32:hi = e.obls[oi2].cone_hyps[h];
            string:named = string_concat("(! ", e.hyps[hi => int64].text);
            named = string_concat(named, " :named h");
            named = string_concat(named, int_to_string(hi => int64));
            named = string_concat(named, ")");
            drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", named));
        }
        string:goal = string_concat("(! ", raw smt_app1("not", string_concat(e.obls[oi2].goal, "")));
        goal = string_concat(goal, " :named o");
        goal = string_concat(goal, int_to_string(oi2 + 1i64));
        goal = string_concat(goal, ")");
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, raw smt_app1("assert", goal));
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(check-sat)");
        drop smtbuf_line(@b, "(pop)");
    }
    pass (raw smtbuf_text(move(b)));
};
